PVD("japan_ndp_2025-2025",{"docs":["","JPN Honebuto 2025 English"],"s":{"1":[[1,"92","7","Wage Increase Support Measures","mobilize all measures to support wage increases",""],[1,"6","1","Minimum Wage Increase Policy","minimum wage increase, based on the idea that wage increases are the cornerstone of the Growth Strategy.",""],[1,"92","5","Minimum Wage Increase Policy","including raising minimum wages",""],[1,"3","7","Wage Increase Support Policy Measures","Implementing all possible policy measures to support wage increases",""],[1,"3","8","Five-year Plan for Promoting Wage Increases at Small Businesses","Implementing the Five-year Plan for Promoting Wage Increases at Small-",""],[1,"3","9","Trinity Labor Market Reform and Wage Increase Support","Trinity labor market reforms and supporting wage increases",""],[1,"7","5","Future Wage Increase Measures","we intend to further increase spendable income through future wage hikes",""],[1,"8","1","Wage Increase Promotion Policy","by spreading and keeping wage increases above price hikes.",""],[1,"12","2","Five-Year Wage Increase Promotion Plan","Implementing all possible policy measures to support wage increases",""],[1,"7","2","SME Wage Increase Support Measures","the government will mobilize all measures to support wage increases, such as passing on prices, enhancing productivity, and backing business succession and M&As to strengthen management foundations.",""],[1,"7","2","Minimum Wage Increase Programme","We will steadily raise the minimum wage and continue to work tirelessly toward our lofty goal of achieving the national average of 1,500 yen in the 2020s.",""],[1,"13","5","Small and Medium Enterprise Wage Increase Initiatives","In addition, the government will promote initiatives based on the Five-year Plan for Increasing Wages at Small and Medium Enterprises and Small Business,5",""],[1,"14","2","SME Wage Increase and Productivity Support Initiative","the public and private sectors will intensively implement maximum measures over the next five years by supporting wage increases of affected SMEs and Small Business through proper price pass-through and backing for productivity improvement",""],[1,"14","3","Minimum Wage Review and Increase Policy","With regard to raising the minimum wage, the Central Minimum Wage Council is requested to discuss the minimum wage based on the data of the three statutory elements",""],[1,"14","4","Five-Year SME Wage Increase Plan","The Five-Year Plan for Increasing Wages at Small and Medium Enterprises and Small Business stipulates improvements in their productivity and the price pass-through in public sector demand, etc.",""],[1,"14","4","Focused Subsidy Support for SME Wage Increases","the government will provide focused support through government subsidies and fully support various efforts of such prefectures using subsidies as special measures to expand sales and improve productivity in a sustainable manner",""],[1,"14","5","Local Minimum Wage Deliberation Mechanism","Local Minimum Wage Councils are requested to discuss the minimum wage based on the data of the three statutory elements to make deliberative decisions in light of the actual situation, taking into account these government-wide efforts and",""],[1,"15","2","Regional Minimum Wage Equalization Policy","The government will narrow regional disparities, such as increasing the ratio of the lowest regional minimum wage to the highest regional minimum wage.",""],[1,"9","5","Wage Increase Establishment Policy","firmly establish wage increases",""],[1,"92","5","SME Price Pass-Through Facilitation Measure","facilitating appropriate price pass-through",""],[1,"92","5","Regional SME Productivity Improvement Support","productivity improvements",""],[1,"92","5","SME Business Succession and M&A Support","supporting business succession and M&As to strengthen their management foundations",""],[1,"93","1","Widespread Wage Growth Promotion","promoting widespread and sustained wage growth that exceeds inflation",""]],"2":[[1,"6","4","Labor Mobility Facilitation Policy","facilitating labor mobility",""],[1,"13","2","Vice President Once a Week Campaign","the government will promote the \"Vice President Once a Week\" campaign",""],[1,"13","2","Local Human Resources Matching Support","strengthen matching support",""],[1,"13","2","By-Jobs and Side-Jobs Promotion","promote by-jobs and side-jobs",""],[1,"13","4","Advanced Essential Workforce Development Programme","the government will urge universities, junior colleges, colleges of technology (KOSEN), and professional schools to work on developing advanced essential workers,17 including incumbent ones.",""],[1,"13","4","Worker Insurance and Conditions Improvement Measures","we will make efforts to reduce the burden of insurance premiums and to improve workers’ conditions, such as by raising official prices, with the aim of securing human resources in healthcare, long-term care, childcare, welfare, and similar sectors.",""],[1,"13","6","Urban Manager Side-Job Support for Local SMEs","In this campaign, managerial personnel in urban areas are involved in the management of local SMEs, etc. about once a week in the form of a by-job or a side-job.",""],[1,"14","3","Local Community Human Resources and Treatment Improvement","development of human resources who play an active role in local communities and improvement of their treatment",""],[1,"10","1","Public-Private Human Resources Development","the public and private sectors will collaborate to develop human resources",""],[1,"10","1","Regular Employment Expansion","increasing the number of regular employees",""],[1,"10","1","Reskilling and Upskilling Support","supporting those engaged in reskilling and upskilling",""],[1,"10","1","Diverse Working Styles Promotion","promoting diverse working styles.",""],[1,"15","4","Digital Skills Training Benefit Expansion","Specifically, the government will expand the digital skills -related courses eligible for, including AI, for educational training benefits",""],[1,"15","4","Online Vocational Training Access Programme","make it possible for nationwide non-regular employees, etc. to take online vocational training courses",""],[1,"15","4","Career Planning and Second-Career Support","We will support career planning, including reskilling and upskilling of middle-aged and elderly people for second careers.",""],[1,"15","4","Industry-Academia Reskilling Programme Expansion","The reskilling and upskilling program through industry-academia collaboration will be expanded in terms of its venues and its coverage/content",""],[1,"15","4","Frontline Personnel Skills and Treatment Improvement","the government will develop an environment for improving the skills and treatment of frontline personnel",""],[1,"15","4","National Frontline Skills Improvement Campaign","will carry out a national campaign aimed at improving their skills",""],[1,"15","4","Job-Based Personnel Management Guidelines Dissemination","We will disseminate the Job-Based Personnel Management Guidelines",""],[1,"15","4","Human Capital Visualization Guidelines Review","review the Human Capital Visualization Guidelines",""],[1,"15","4","Human Capital Disclosure Enhancement","enhance information disclosure regarding human capital in annual securities reports",""],[1,"15","4","Public Job Posting Data Collection and Analysis","the government will enhance the collection and analysis of public job postings from the public and private sectors",""],[1,"15","4","Certification System Skill Evaluation Strengthening","strengthen ... the skill evaluation in the certification system",""],[1,"16","1","Hello Work Public Employment Service System Strengthening","We will strengthen the system of Hello Work (Japan’s public employment service) system)",""],[1,"16","1","AI-Enabled Career Support Promotion","promote the use of AI to enhance career support, including such support for incumbent employees.",""],[1,"16","2","Growth-Sector Labor Mobility Facilitation","raising the labor participation rate through the facilitation of labor mobility to growth sectors and enterprises with high productivity",""],[1,"16","2","Diverse and Flexible Work Styles Promotion","the promotion of diverse and flexible working styles",""],[1,"16","3","Short-Time Regular Employment System","including short-time regular employees",""],[1,"16","3","Working-Hour Interval System","the introduction of a working-hour interval system",""],[1,"16","3","Selective Four-Day Work Week","the spread of a selective four-day work week",""],[1,"16","3","Work-Family Caregiving Support","support for balancing work with childcare and caregiving",""],[1,"16","3","Employment Support for People Facing Difficulties","work support that reaches all people with employment difficulties",""],[1,"16","4","Employer Support for Higher Wages and Working Hours","implement measures to support employers who raise workers' income by extending working hours or raising wages",""],[1,"16","5","Work Style and Labor Standards Legislation Review","The government comprehensively reviews the Act Related to Work Style Reform23 after five years of enforcement, and will consider how to review the labor standards legislation based on the actual conditions and needs of work styles.",""],[1,"16","6","National Public Employee Workforce Flexibility and Conditions Reform","For national public employees, the government will promote the flexibility of working hours and places, the strengthening of management, the flexibility of the recruitment process, and the improvement of working conditions",""],[1,"16","6","Wage-Raising Efforts in Individual Industries","Efforts to raise wages in Individual industries",""],[1,"16","7","Construction Labor Cost Standards","setting standards for labor costs and ensuring their effectiveness",""],[1,"16","7","Construction Career Up System Expansion","expanding the use of the Construction Career Up System",""],[1,"16","7","Wage-Responsive Fare Setting","setting fares in response to wage increases",""],[1,"16","7","Strengthened Corrective Guidance for Shippers","strengthening corrective guidance to shippers",""],[1,"16","7","Labor Cost Price Pass-Through Promotion","the government will promote the price pass-through of labor costs",""],[1,"16","8","Public-Private Salary Comparison Review","In this regard, the National Personnel Authority (NPA) is considering a review of the size of enterprises that will be subject to salary comparison between the public and private sectors.",""],[1,"17","1","Public Sector Procurement Pricing and Separate Ordering Mechanism","setting proper unit prices and thoroughly implementing separate orders, including additional premiums based on the degree of risk and importance in the public sector demand.",""],[1,"17","2","Healthcare and Care Sector Remuneration Improvement Review","we will ascertain and examine the effects of past efforts to revise remuneration, etc., and discuss how to improve them, aiming to draw a conclusion by the end of 2025.",""]],"4":[[1,"12","3","SME Price Pass-Through and Fair Transactions Policy","the government will work on passing on prices and ensuring proper transactions",""],[1,"12","3","SME Productivity Improvement Initiative","the government will work on ... improving productivity",""],[1,"12","3","SME Business Succession and M&A Support","the government will work on ... strengthening the management base through business succession and M&As",""],[1,"12","3","SME Human Resources Development Programme","the government will work on ... developing human resources",""],[1,"12","3","Local Workers’ Conditions Improvement Initiative","the government will work on ... improving workers’ conditions in local communities",""],[1,"13","1","Supply Chain Transaction Fairness Initiative","promote initiatives to ensure proper transactions throughout the supply chains, including expanding and improving the effects of the Declaration of Partnership Building.",""],[1,"13","1","SME Intellectual Property Infringement Surveys","conducting fact-finding surveys on infringement of intellectual property affecting SMEs",""],[1,"13","1","Antimonopoly Act Intellectual Property Guidelines","formulating guidelines under the Antimonopoly Act",""],[1,"13","1","IP Business Management Literacy Support","the government will work on improving literacy through the IP Business Management Support Network.",""],[1,"13","2","Productivity Improvement Investment and Support Initiative","the public and private sectors will invest approximately 60 trillion yen in productivity improvement over the five years until fiscal 2029 as intensive efforts by that fiscal year, through support using digital support tools, nationwide accompanied support, and multi-year productivity improvement support",""],[1,"13","3","Business Succession Needs Identification Support","support institutions will strengthen their engagement to uncover the needs of sellers",""],[1,"13","3","Business Succession and Transfer Support Center Strengthening","strengthen the structure of business succession and transfer support centers",""],[1,"13","3","Business Succession Tax Policy Review","the government will consider how business succession-related policies should be",""],[1,"13","3","Successor Management Capability Development","work on developing successors’ management capabilities",""],[1,"13","6","Intellectual Property Support Framework for SMEs","A framework in which the Japan Patent Office, National Center for Industrial Property Information and Training, Japan Patent Attorneys Association, and the Small and Medium Enterprise Agency cooperate with the Japan Chamber of Commerce and Industry to support SMEs and small-sized business operators from the perspective of intellectual property.","Small and Medium Enterprise Agency"],[1,"13","6","Business Succession Policy Discussion","We will continue to discuss how business succession should be, In light of concerns about the stagnation of generational change and the impact of business succession on the growth of regional economies.",""],[1,"14","3","SME Price Pass-Through and Proper Transactions Measures","thorough implementation of price pass-through and proper transactions, including measures for public sector demand that is important for local SMEs and Small Business",""],[1,"14","3","SME Labor-Saving Investment and Productivity Support","improvement of productivity of SMEs and Small Business through the enhancement of the Labor-saving Investment Promotion Plan by sector and the relevant detailed support measures as well as the development of support systems",""],[1,"14","3","SME Business Succession and M&A Support Environment","improvement of an environment in which business owners and executives of SMEs and Small Business can make management decisions for the future in a systematic manner by removing their concerns and barriers related to business succession and M&As",""]],"5":[[1,"34","3","Digital Agency Control Tower Strengthening","the government will strengthen the control tower function of the Digital Agency","Digital Agency"],[1,"34","3","Society-Wide Digital Technology Implementation","promote the social implementation of digital technologies, including AI and web 3,78 and create new value through the use of data",""],[1,"34","3","Data Integration Systems and Infrastructure Development","The government will advance the development of systems based on the Strategic Plan for Data Utilization Frameworks79 and a common infrastructure for data integration.",""],[1,"34","3","Cross-Border Data Flows and Security Promotion","the government will work on the promotion of cross-border data flows and data security",""],[1,"34","3","Business Operators Digital Portal","We will advance the development of the Portal for Business Operators (tentative name).81",""],[1,"34","3","Online Information Harm Technology Development","the government will work to develop technologies",""],[1,"34","3","Public-Private Digital Information Awareness Initiative","raise awareness through public-private partnerships",""],[1,"34","3","Digital Advertisement Distribution Regulation","properly distribute digital advertisements",""],[1,"34","3","Digital Infrastructure Improvement","we will improve the digital infrastructure",""],[1,"34","3","Structural Technology and Systems Development","develop structural technologies and systems",""],[1,"34","4","Digital Lifeline Development Plan","The government will promote the ”Digital Lifeline Development Plan”83",""],[1,"34","4","Ouranos Cross-Industry Data-Sharing Platform","building a platform for data sharing and system linkage across the borders between enterprises and industries (Ouranos Ecosystem)",""],[1,"34","5","Geospatial Information Enhancement and Utilization","the government will promote the enhancement and utilization of geospatial information (G-spatial information), which is common infrastructure supporting new technologies in various fields",""],[1,"34","5","National Geospatial Infrastructure Development and Renewal","strongly promote the development and renewal of National Geospatial Infrastructure, such as GNSS Continuously Operating Reference Stations and three-dimensional Digital Japan Basic Map, which serve as the foundation for accurate G-spatial information",""],[1,"34","5","Cross-Sectoral Geospatial Technology Social Implementation","the government will strongly promote the social implementation of new technologies utilizing the G-spatial information and National Geospatial Infrastructure in a wide, cross-sectional",""],[1,"36","3","Digital Administrative and Fiscal Reform Measures","implement measures based on the Report of Digital Administrative and Fiscal Reform 2025 to maintain and enhance public services, advance regional economic revitalization, and realize social transformation by making the best use of digital.",""],[1,"36","3","Digital Regulation and Systems Review","the government will review regulations and systems from the user perspective and promote digital utilization",""],[1,"36","3","Shared National and Local Infrastructure Development","promote the development of shared national and local infrastructure.",""],[1,"36","3","Data and Artificial Intelligence Utilization Framework","the government will accelerate efforts and establish a virtuous cycle of data and AI.",""],[1,"36","3","Cross-Sectional Data Utilization Legal Reform","We will also conduct necessary studies regarding a cross-sectional legal system, including a fundamental revision of the Basic Act on the Advancement of Public and Private Sector Data Utilization and a new law, aiming to submit a bill to the next ordinary Diet session.",""],[1,"36","3","Personal Information Protection Act Amendment","We also aim to reach an early conclusion on a bill to amend the Act on the Protection of Personal Information",""],[1,"36","4","Digital Administration Promotion Initiative","The entire government, centered around the Digital Agency, will promote the digitalization of administration, including the utilization of AI, the promotion of web","Digital Agency"],[1,"37","1","Integrated Digital Government and Human Resources Development","the development of digital human resources, based on the Priority Policy Program,80 etc., in a consistent manner among administrative frameworks, operations, and systems, from the viewpoint of users, and in a trinity.",""],[1,"37","1","Digitalization Cost-Benefit Performance Visualization","We will promote the visualization of the cost-benefit performance to ensure that both the demand side and the supply side can fully appreciate the benefits of digitalization by quantitatively assessing benefits, etc.",""],[1,"37","1","Legislative Digitalization Review","we will strengthen the review of digitalization in legislation to ensure that no new analogue-based regulations are introduced.",""],[1,"37","1","Japan Dashboard for Data-Based Policymaking","the government will put into place the Japan Dashboard to visualize the Japanese economy, finance, and living.",""],[1,"37","2","My Number Card Digital Access Environment","the government will work to develop an environment where citizens can obtain My Number Cards smoothly, enable card functions to be integrated into smartphones, and continuously improve the My Number portal site.",""],[1,"37","2","Online City Hall Service","we will enhance convenience through the Online City Hall Service, which delivers public services tailored to residents in a push-type manner",""],[1,"37","2","My Number Card Digital ID Initiative","the Initiative of Making the My Number Card a Digital ID for Citizens, which enables users to receive various high-quality services with a single card.",""],[1,"37","2","Online Digitalization of National Qualifications","the online digitalization of national qualifications",""],[1,"37","2","My Number Health Insurance and Medical Subsidy Card Integration","the integration of the My Number health insurance card with a recipient card of medical expenses subsidies",""],[1,"37","2","My Number Card Ambulance Service Promotion","the nationwide promotion of ambulance services with the use of My Number Card",""],[1,"37","2","My Number Card and Residence Card Integration","the integration of the My Number Card with the Residence Card",""],[1,"37","2","My Number Driver’s License System","smooth operation of the My Number driver’s license system",""],[1,"37","2","Private-Sector My Number Card Authentication Expansion","The government will accelerate the use of My Number Cards in the private sector by using authentication apps, such as providing services free from impersonation, aiming to further establish them as digital public infrastructure.",""],[1,"37","3","Local Government Standards-Based Systems Reform","We will work on the shift to standards-based systems by local governments and advance initiatives based on comprehensive measures relating to system operation costs after the shift.",""],[1,"37","3","National and Local Digital Infrastructure Coordination","Based on the Basic Policy on the Development and Operation of Common Digital Infrastructure for National and Local Governments, 92 the national and local governments will cooperate, according to the commonality promotion policy, to promote initiatives in the operations and systems to be selected by the National and Local Digital Infrastructure Promotion Liaison Council.",""],[1,"37","4","Public Sector Systems Modernization Reform","promoting the commonality and modernization of public sector systems",""],[1,"37","4","Quasi-Public Sector Data Integration Infrastructure","the establishment of data integration infrastructure in quasi-public sectors",""],[1,"37","4","Gov-Cloud Adoption Initiative","promoting the shift to Gov-Cloud",""]],"6":[[1,"38","2","Nationwide Healthcare and Long-Term Care DX System","the government will strongly promote the establishment of a system or systems to provide high-quality and efficient healthcare and long-term care services nationwide through the rapid implementation of technological innovations of DX for healthcare and long-term care",""],[1,"38","2","My Number Health Insurance Card System","the government will promote the use of My Number health insurance cards as the basis of healthcare DX",""],[1,"38","2","Nationwide Healthcare Information Platform","The government will build the Nationwide Healthcare Information Platform",""],[1,"38","2","Clinical Information Sharing Service Dissemination","promote the dissemination of the Clinical Information Sharing Service",""],[1,"38","2","Electronic Prescription Expansion","expand the use of electronic prescriptions",""],[1,"38","2","Personal Health Record Information Utilization","promote the utilization of PHR information",""],[1,"38","2","Standard Electronic Medical Records Dissemination","promote their dissemination",""],[1,"38","2","Long-Term Care Information System Development","the government will promote the development of the Long-Term Care Information System",""],[1,"38","2","Medical Fee Revision Digital Transformation","the DX of medical fee revisions",""],[1,"38","2","Pharmacy Information Standardization and DX","the standardization and DX of information held by pharmacies",""],[1,"38","2","AI Drug Discovery and AI Hospitals","The government will support the practical application of AI drug discovery and AI hospitals",""],[1,"38","2","Cloud-Based Hospital Information Systems","The government will formulate standard specifications and advance discussions toward the development and introduction of hospital information systems utilizing cloud technology",""],[1,"38","2","Standard Drug and Test Code Master Data Management","the government will promote the central management of the master data based on the examination of an appropriate modus of standard codes for drugs and tests",""],[1,"38","2","Digital Vaccination Procedures","the digitalization of vaccination procedures",""],[1,"38","2","Electronic Vaccine Adverse Reaction Reporting","electronic reporting of suspected vaccine adverse reactions",""],[1,"38","2","Vaccination Database Development","the development of a vaccination database",""],[1,"38","2","Pseudonymized Healthcare Data Utilization Systems","the government will promote the development of systems that enable the use of pseudonymized information from public healthcare and long-term care databases",""],[1,"38","2","Health Insurance Claims Review Service Reorganization","We will also smoothly implement the reorganization of Health Insurance Claims Review & Reimbursement Services",""],[1,"38","2","Online Qualification Confirmation in Public Expense Healthcare","online qualification confirmation in the public expense healthcare system",""],[1,"38","2","Pharmaceutical and Medical Device Product Database","we will build a product database that contributes to the logistics DX for pharmaceuticals and medical devices etc.",""],[1,"38","2","Healthcare Institute Cybersecurity Measures","promote cyber security measures at healthcare institutes",""],[1,"38","2","Healthcare DX Roadmap Review","the government will consider a review of the Healthcare DX Roadmap as necessary",""],[1,"38","3","Healthcare DX Promotion Roadmap","Roadmap for the Promotion of Healthcare DX",""],[1,"39","1","Child-Related Measures Digital Transformation Initiative","In consideration of ease of use for child-rearing generations, the government will promote the DX of Child-Related Measures, including measures for childcare or maternal and child health, etc.",""]],"7":[[1,"39","2","GIGA School Education DX Programme","the government will accelerate education DX, including the use of generative AI, to integrate children's personalized and self-regulated learning and collaborative learning as well as to reduce the workload of teachers.",""],[1,"39","2","Joint Procurement of School Devices","this includes device replacements under a joint procurement scheme",""],[1,"39","2","Next-Generation School Work DX Environment","accelerating support for the development of the next-generation school work DX environment",""],[1,"39","2","School Network Environment Improvement","improving the network environment at schools",""],[1,"39","2","DX High School Project","promoting exploratory, interdisciplinary, and practical learning through the continuous implementation of the DX High School Project",""],[1,"39","2","ICT Use and Information Ethics Support","creating good examples for the use of ICT and for the development of children's information ethics and strengthening follow-up support",""],[1,"39","2","Digital Textbook Expansion","promoting the use of digital textbooks",""],[1,"39","2","Educational Data Standardization and Utilization Mechanism","the government will promote the collection, analysis, and utilization of educational data through collaboration among systems while thoroughly ensuring the protection of personal information",""],[1,"39","2","Authentication Infrastructure Technology Research","We will also advance the research, studies and demonstration of technologies concerning the authentication infrastructure to ensure the authenticity of subjects and data.",""],[1,"39","5","Systematic Digital Education Programme","This includes the promotion of systematic digital education from the compulsory education stage.","Digital Agency | Ministry of Internal Affairs and Communications | Ministry of Education, Culture, Sports, Science and Technology | Ministry of Economy, Trade and Industry"]],"8":[[1,"39","4","Regional Transportation MaaS and Data Utilization Initiative","The government will promote initiatives, such as the advancement of transportation services through mobility as a service (MaaS) and the utilization of data, to enhance the sustainability, productivity, and convenience of regional transportation.",""],[1,"39","4","Regional Transportation Digital Transformation Initiative","We will also promote DX for regional transportation, such as the promotion of cashless transactions and ride-hailing apps.",""],[1,"39","4","eVTOL Social Implementation Initiative","The government will promote the social implementation of eVTOLs (electric Vertical Take-Off and Landing).",""],[1,"39","4","Autonomous Driving Institutional Arrangements","To accelerate the social implementation of autonomous driving mobile services, the government will make institutional arrangements",""],[1,"39","4","Nationwide Autonomous Driving Mobility Projects","promote nationwide projects based on the Mobility Roadmap 2025.",""],[1,"39","4","Autonomous Driving Technology Development and Demonstration","We will also promote the development and demonstration of autonomous driving technologies",""],[1,"40","1","Autonomous Driving and Ride-Sharing Initiatives","the government will advance necessary initiatives for autonomous driving and ride-sharing based on the Basic Policy 2024, etc.",""],[1,"40","1","Rural Mobility System Design","we will discuss an appropriate modus of systems to solve the shortage of mobility in small and medium-sized cities in rural areas and other regions where the public transportation mode is less convenient.",""],[1,"40","1","Unmanned Aircraft Systems Lines Expansion and Development","To promote the wide use of UAS (Unmanned Aircraft Systems), the government will expand the areas where UAS Lines are implemented and work on the institutional arrangements and technological development.",""]],"9":[[1,"40","3","Disaster Management Digital Platform","the government aims to realize a disaster management digital platform as early as possible",""],[1,"40","3","Integrated Disaster Management Information System Enhancement","We will also further strengthen the functions of the new Integrated Disaster Management Information System (SOBO-WEB), which will play a central role in the platform",""],[1,"40","3","Disaster Data Integration Infrastructure","build, coordinate, and utilize the data integration infrastructure, L-Alert, 102 and D24H 103",""],[1,"40","3","Integrated Disaster Information Mapping System Improvement","improve the Integrated Disaster Information Mapping System",""],[1,"40","3","Regional Disaster Information Distribution","promote the information distribution among regional disaster management organizations",""],[1,"40","3","Wide-Area Disaster Victim Support Collaboration Mechanism","build a mechanism for wide-area collaboration of disaster victim support systems",""],[1,"40","3","National Geospatial Infrastructure Development and Upgrading","The government will develop and upgrade National Geospatial Infrastructure as the basis for various economic and social activities and disaster response",""],[1,"40","3","AI-Enhanced Weather Observation and Forecasting","The use of AI technology will sophisticate weather observations and forecasting, etc.",""],[1,"40","4","National Disaster Information Distribution System","A system that simultaneously distributes disaster information collected from local governments across the country to media organizations, etc., and delivers it quickly and efficiently to residents.",""],[1,"40","4","Disaster Health, Medical, and Welfare Support System","A support system for health, medical, and welfare activities during a disaster.",""]],"10":[[1,"31","2","Factory and Household Energy Conservation and Non-Fossil Fuel Support","the government will support energy conservation and the shift to non-fossil fuel at factories and households",""],[1,"31","2","Energy Conservation Diagnosis Programme","promote energy conservation diagnosis",""],[1,"31","2","Energy Conservation Support System Strengthening","strengthen support systems, including financial institutions",""],[1,"31","2","Specialist Energy Conservation Human Resources Development","secure specialist human resources",""],[1,"31","3","Domestic Renewable Energy Supply Chain Programme","In order to expand domestic renewable energy, the government will build a resilient supply chain in Japan in cooperation with universities, National Research and Development Agencies, startups, etc.",""],[1,"31","3","Perovskite Solar Cell Deployment Support","The government will support the introduction of perovskite solar cells, including tandem solar cells",""],[1,"31","3","Floating Offshore Wind Development Programme","encourage the technological development for floating offshore wind power, the relevant infrastructure improvement, the related-project arrangements as well as the formulation of a human resources development strategy",""],[1,"31","3","Next-Generation Geothermal Systems Implementation","support the social implementation of next-generation geothermal systems",""],[1,"31","3","Small and Medium Hydropower Development Support","We will also support the creation of small and medium hydropower projects",""],[1,"31","3","Existing Hydropower Facility Replacement Programme","support the replacement of existing hydropower generation facilities",""],[1,"31","3","Inter-Regional Power Interconnection Development","In addition to the development of inter-regional interconnection lines, including submarine high-voltage, direct current power transmission between Hokkaido and Honshu",""],[1,"31","3","Systematic Local Grid Development Framework","the government will study a framework for the systematic development of local grids",""],[1,"31","3","Energy Storage and Demand Response Deployment","the government will advance the introduction of safe and sustainable storage batteries and the use of DR",""],[1,"31","3","Domestic Battery Production Capacity Expansion","We will work on expanding the domestic production capacity for storage batteries, parts, materials, and manufacturing equipment",""],[1,"31","3","Next-Generation Battery Technology Development","as well as developing next-generation battery technology",""],[1,"32","2","Decarbonized Power Investment Market Arrangements","the government will consider institutional arrangements in the market and business environment to enhance the predictability of investment recovery.",""],[1,"32","2","Public Credit Enhancement and Government-Backed Loans","We will also consider the use of public credit enhancement as well as loans backed by the creditworthiness of the Government.",""],[1,"33","4","Manufacturing Energy Efficiency and Electrification Policy","On the demand side, the government will promote thorough energy efficiency improvement as well as fuel switching and electrification within the manufacturing sector.",""],[1,"33","4","Renewable and Nuclear Power Utilization Initiative","On the supply side, we will maximize the use most of renewable and nuclear power, both of which contribute to improving energy self-sufficiency and have significant decarbonization effects.",""],[1,"33","4","Oil and Critical Minerals Stockpiling Mechanism","To ensure stable supplies of oil and critical minerals, such as minor metals, we will secure sufficient stockpiles.",""],[1,"33","4","Overseas Upstream Development for Energy Supply Chains","In addition, we will promote the strengthening of supply chains through upstream development abroad, including Japan’s own independent initiatives, which will also encompass natural gas.",""],[1,"33","4","Strategic Buffer LNG Security Mechanism","The government will strategically secure buffer LNG.",""]],"11":[[1,"32","1","Nuclear Fuel Cycle Promotion","the promotion of the nuclear fuel cycle",""],[1,"31","4","Nuclear Reactor Reactivation Programme","The government will advance the reactivation of nuclear reactors based on the reviews and inspections conducted by the Nuclear Regulation Authority.",""],[1,"31","4","Next-Generation Innovative Reactor Development and Installation","The government will work on the development and installation of next-generation innovative reactors",""],[1,"31","4","Nuclear Power Plant Replacement Programme","will progressively realize the replacement of the nuclear power plants scheduled for the",""],[1,"32","1","Nuclear Power Plant Replacement Programme","decommission with new ones on the same sites owned by the electric power providers who have decided on decommission",""],[1,"32","1","Nuclear Energy Research and Development","The government will work on R&D",""],[1,"32","1","Nuclear Energy Human Resources Development","The government will work on ... human resources development",""],[1,"32","1","Nuclear Energy Supply Chain Strengthening","the maintenance and strengthening of supply chains",""],[1,"32","1","Nuclear Power Plant Decommissioning Programme","the advancement of the decommissioning of nuclear power plants in a steady and efficient manner",""],[1,"32","1","Final Disposal Local Government Engagement","The national government will take the lead in actively engaging with local governments to achieve final disposal",""],[1,"32","1","Nuclear Emergency Preparedness System","We will enhance the nuclear emergency preparedness system, including securing evacuation routes through road development, and responses during a complex disaster",""],[1,"32","1","Nuclear Emergency Evacuation Route Development","securing evacuation routes through road development",""]],"12":[[1,"32","3","Forest Carbon Sink Measures","implement measures for forest carbon sinks.",""],[1,"32","3","Low-Carbon Hydrogen Supply Chain Development","the government will support research and development, capital investment, as well as the development of hubs and related infrastructure, aiming to construct domestic and international supply chains.",""],[1,"32","3","Sustainable Aviation Fuel Development","With regard to SAF (Sustainable Aviation Fuel), the government will promote R&D and capital investment toward the realization of internationally competitive prices.",""],[1,"32","3","Biofuel Demand Creation System","We will study systems to create demand for biofuels and others",""],[1,"32","3","Electrified Vehicle Introduction","while also promoting the introduction of electrified vehicles.",""],[1,"32","3","Alternative Fuel and Carbon Capture Deployment","the government will encourage the fuel conversion to natural gas and the utilization of hydrogen and its derivatives and CCUS, including artificial photosynthesis.",""],[1,"32","3","Carbon Capture and Storage Support Systems","We will consider support systems for CCS",""],[1,"33","2","Decarbonization Leading Areas Deployment Initiative","the government will take measures the nationwide deployment of advanced initiatives in decarbonization leading areas",""],[1,"33","2","New Technology Decarbonization Pilot Project","consider establishing a pilot project for introducing new technologies",""],[1,"33","2","Infrastructure Buildings and Mobility Decarbonization","We will work on the decarbonization of infrastructure, 71 buildings, and mobility 72-related fields",""],[1,"33","2","Building Life-Cycle Assessment System","the establishment of the LCA system 73 for buildings",""],[1,"33","2","Decarbonized Products and Services Labeling Rules","the widespread use of decarbonized products and services by formulating labeling rules",""],[1,"33","2","Decokatsu and Reuse Promotion Initiative","the promotion of “Decokatsu”74 and reuse",""],[1,"33","5","Carbon Neutral Port Infrastructure","This includes Carbon Neutral Ports for stably receiving and supplying hydrogen and other clean energy sources.",""],[1,"33","5","Zero-Emission Transport Technology Deployment","This includes fuel-cell railway vehicles, zero-emission ships, and next-generation aircraft.",""],[1,"33","5","Whole-Life-Cycle CO2 Emissions Assessment","Assessment of CO2 emissions throughout the entire life cycle from construction to demolition (Life Cycle Assessment).",""],[1,"33","5","National Net-Zero Lifestyle Transformation Campaign","A new national campaign to facilitate behavior change and lifestyle transformation among citizens, aiming to achieve net-zero by 2050.",""]],"13":[[1,"32","6","Blue Infrastructure Conservation and Restoration Initiative","This includes the utilization of the J-Credit and blue carbon (carbon derived from carbon dioxide sequestrated by marine ecosystems) through the conservation, restoration, and creation of blue infrastructure (seagrass beds, tidal flats, etc., and bio-symbiotic port structures).",""],[1,"32","4","Arterial-Venous Industry Collaboration System","the government will consider proper systems for the collaboration between arterial and venous industries",""],[1,"32","4","Solar Panel Disposal and Recycling System","systems for the disposal and recycling of solar panels",""],[1,"32","4","Plastics and Metals Recycling Innovation Investment","will support the R&D for and capital investment in recycling plastics and metals, such as aluminum",""],[1,"32","4","International Circular Economy Cooperation","We will also promote international cooperation",""],[1,"32","4","International Circular Economy Rules","the establishment of rules",""],[1,"32","6","Resource Circulation Network and Domestic Bases","This includes the establishment of a resource circulation network and its domestic bases that collect and dispose wastes, etc. even from overseas and stably supply high-quality recycled materials to manufacturers.",""],[1,"33","2","Service Station Network Maintenance Support","the government will support the maintenance of the service station (SS) network",""],[1,"33","2","LP Gas Disaster Response Strengthening","the strengthening of LP gas disaster responses",""]],"15":[[1,"41","4","Strategic Space Policy Coordination Mechanism","the Strategic Headquarters for National Space policy serving as the control tower",""],[1,"41","4","Satellite Constellation Development","the government will build satellite constellations",""],[1,"41","4","Next-Generation Space Technology Development and Demonstration","develop and demonstrate next-generation technologies",""],[1,"41","4","Proactive Space Technology Procurement","proactively procure",""],[1,"42","1","Rocket Development and Launch Expansion Support","We will support rocket development by the public and private sectors and raise the frequency of their launches.",""],[1,"42","1","Pressurized Lunar Rover Development","Under the Artemis program,107 we will advance the development of a pressurized rover for the achievement of a moon landing by Japanese astronauts.",""],[1,"42","1","Low Earth Orbit Activity Enhancement","We will enhance Low Earth Orbit activities",""],[1,"42","1","Beyond-Moon and Mars Exploration Research","advance research and development for exploration beyond the moon and Mars",""],[1,"42","1","Quasi-Zenith Satellite Constellation Expansion","advance the construction of the seven-satellite constellation of the Quasi-Zenith Satellite System and the development towards an eleven-satellite constellation.",""],[1,"42","1","Space Strategy Fund Financing Support","The government will aim to promptly provide approximately one trillion yen in support to the Space Strategy Fund",""],[1,"42","1","Long-Term Government Procurement for Space Startups","will promote medium- to long-term government procurement to facilitate the business expansion of startups, etc.",""],[1,"42","1","Private Space Transportation Regulatory Reform","We aim to submit to the next ordinary Diet session a bill to amend the Act on Launching Spacecraft and Launch Vehicle and Control of Spacecraft108 to enable private companies to carry out new space transportation projects.",""],[1,"42","1","Space-Use Screening and Satellite Operations Arrangements","The government will promote the institutional arrangements that will enable smooth screening in response to the expansion of space use and the sustainable operation of quasi-zenith satellites.",""],[1,"42","1","JAXA Technical and Human Resource Strengthening","We will also promote the strengthening of JAXA's technical foundation and human resources.",""]],"16":[[1,"42","2","Minamitorishima Rare Earth Production Research","research and development for rare earth production in the waters around Minamitorishima Island",""],[1,"42","2","Autonomous Underwater Vehicle Demonstration Programme","the government will support the use and demonstration of Autonomous Underwater Vehicles and their peripheral technologies",""],[1,"42","2","Maritime Domain Awareness Technology Research","research for the advancement and oversea expansion of maritime domain awareness systems using satellite data combined with AI analysis technologies",""],[1,"42","2","Overseas Maritime Domain Awareness Capacity Development","preparation for oversea countries' MDA capacity development with this systems",""],[1,"42","2","Mirai II Arctic Research Vessel Construction","the construction and actual service of Mirai II, the Arctic Research Vessel (ARV)",""],[1,"42","2","Deep-Sea Mother Ship Planning","The government will discuss an appropriate method of a mother ship that has the exploration and sampling platform functions for deep seas and trench areas.",""],[1,"42","2","Populated Remote Territorial Islands Conservation Measures","The government will examine the efforts for the conservation of populated remote territorial islands and the maintenance of local communities based on the Act on Populated Remote Territorial Islands,110 which will expire at the end of fiscal 2026, and will promote related measures.",""]],"18":[[1,"44","2","Startup Development Plan Implementation Initiatives","The government will promote initiatives based on the Startup Development Five-year Plan.113",""],[1,"44","3","Entrepreneurship Education Programme","We will enhance entrepreneurship education",""],[1,"44","3","International Entrepreneurship Dispatch and Training Programme","work on overseas dispatch, invitation, and entrepreneur training",""],[1,"44","3","International Startup Information Transmission Initiative","strengthen information transmission to the international community",""],[1,"44","3","Startup City Ecosystem Development Programme","The government will foster the startup ecosystem in startup cities by increasing the number of selected cities in the second-term.",""],[1,"44","3","Startup Creation and Growth Support Programme","We will encourage the creation and growth of startups",""],[1,"44","3","KOSEN Entrepreneurship Education Programme","entrepreneurship education at colleges of technology (KOSEN)",""],[1,"44","3","Public Procurement from Startups","Both the national and local governments will expand public procurement from startups",""],[1,"44","3","Global Startup Campus International Research Programme","the government will implement international research",""],[1,"44","3","Global Startup Campus Commercialization Support Programme","commercialization support",""],[1,"44","3","Global Startup Campus Fellowship Programme","fellowship programs",""],[1,"44","4","Deep Tech Startup Commercialization Support Programme","The government will enhance support ranging from start-up to operationalization and commercialization in the deep tech field.",""],[1,"44","4","Growth-Stage Startup Funding Mechanism","We will develop an environment in which funds can be smoothly supplied to startups in accordance with their growth stages, including the later stage and post-listing, by activating the distribution of unlisted shares and expanding debt guarantees.",""],[1,"44","4","Venture Capital Governance and Contract Reform","the government will promote initiatives, such as improving the governance of venture capitals (VCs) and investment contract practices,",""],[1,"44","4","Fair Value Assessment Introduction Framework","as well as introducing fair value assessment, etc.",""],[1,"44","4","JIC Investment Function Strengthening","In addition to strengthening the investment function of JAPAN INVESTMENT CORPORATION (JIC),",""],[1,"44","4","Asset Allocation Verification and Institutional Arrangements","the government will proceed with measures such as verifying asset allocation and making institutional arrangements, etc.",""],[1,"45","2","Mergers and Acquisitions Revitalization Initiative","The government will revitalize M&As to diversify exit strategies.",""],[1,"45","2","Startup Open Innovation Programme","We will carry out new open innovation involving startups, in addition to universities and large corporations.",""],[1,"45","2","Goodwill Accounting Procedures Discussion Mechanism","We will support discussion among relevant parties over the state of accounting procedures concerning goodwill.",""]],"19":[[1,"48","1","Banking and Securities Firewall Regulation Review","The government will review the regulations on the firewall between banking and securities operations.",""],[1,"48","5","Financial Group Information-Sharing and Conflict-of-Interest Regulations","These regulations prohibit banks and securities firms within a financial group from sharing customers' non-public information without the customers' consent, and from engaging in actions that create conflicts of interest.",""],[1,"44","5","Second-Term Base City Selection","the second-term base cities are to be newly selected after the public invitation in January 2025.",""],[1,"44","5","Joint Public Procurement by Local Governments","joint public procurement by multiple local governments over a wide area.",""],[1,"44","5","Overseas Investment Attraction System","building a system to attract overseas investment.",""],[1,"44","5","Tax Measures for Overseas Investment Partners","the consideration of measures based on policy needs and issues concerning the special provisions for taxation on foreign partners of overseas investors (special treatment of the permanent establishment (PE)).",""],[1,"44","5","Monitoring Investment Commitments to Japan-Based Funds","the status of investment commitments to Japan-based PE funds and VCs as a result.",""],[1,"44","5","Collaborative Upgrading of Investment Methods","the upgrading of investment methods through collaboration with other investors",""],[1,"44","5","Annual Assessment of Alternative Investment Asset Caps","an annual proper assessment of efforts to cap alternative investment assets.",""],[1,"45","1","Government Pension Investment Fund Investment","investment120 by the Government Pension Investment Fund (GPIF) up to the limit.",""],[1,"45","3","Impact Measurement Data and Indicators Development","the development of data and indicators necessary for measuring and managing impacts",""],[1,"45","3","Donation Utilization Promotion","the promotion of the use of donations",""],[1,"47","5","NISA Programme Enhancement","the government will consider further enhancing the NISA program",""],[1,"47","5","Financial Asset and Cash Flow Identification Environment","develop an environment in which financial assets and cash flows can be easily identified",""],[1,"48","1","Defined Contribution Pension Contribution Limit Increase","The government aims to promptly raise the contribution limit based on the Outline of the Tax Reform for Fiscal 2025.",""],[1,"48","1","Corporate Pension Investment Management Visualization","Investment management will be visualized for participants in corporate pension plans.",""],[1,"48","1","Household Financial and Economic Education","The government will enhance financial and economic education as a foundation for steady asset building for households.",""],[1,"48","1","TSE Growth Market Function Improvement","The government will improve the functions of the TSE Growth Market.",""],[1,"48","1","Impact Investment Market Expansion","The government will expand the impact investment market.",""],[1,"48","1","Data Center REIT Incorporation","The government will promote the incorporation of data centers into REITs (Real Estate Investment Trusts).",""],[1,"48","1","Pre-Meeting Securities Report Disclosure Measures","The government will consider cross-regulatory measures to encourage the disclosure of annual securities reports before shareholder meetings.",""],[1,"48","1","Corporate Governance Reform","The government will reform corporate governance.",""],[1,"48","1","Financial and Asset Management Special Zone Promotion","The government will focus on the promotional activities of the Special Zones for Financial and Asset Management Businesses for overseas asset management companies in collaboration with the four regions designated as the special zones.",""],[1,"48","1","Asset Owner Principles Adoption Promotion","The government will promote the acceptance of Asset Owner Principles.",""],[1,"48","2","Initiatives Dissemination through Japan Weeks and Asset Management Forum","These and other initiatives will be disseminated at Japan Weeks and the Asset Management Forum in October 2025.",""],[1,"48","2","Financial Services Agency Structural Strengthening","the government will strengthen the structure of the Financial Services Agency that is necessary to promote these measures.","Financial Services Agency"],[1,"48","3","Board Nomination Function Governance Reform","With regard to the organizational design of a Company with a Nominating Committee, etc., in light of the increasing importance of strengthening the nominating function of the Board of Directors, the government will promptly advance considerations of the formulation and enactment of an amendment proposal to resolve the issues.",""]],"20":[[1,"45","4","Economic Partnership Agreement Expansion","expand EPAs",""],[1,"45","4","Rules-Based International Economic Order Initiative","Japan strongly urges the United States to reconsider its measures, and will work to maintain and strengthen the free and fair rules-based international economic order.",""],[1,"45","4","CPTPP Expansion and Development Initiative","We will lead discussions on the expansion and development of the CPTPP",""],[1,"45","4","RCEP Agreement Implementation","ensure the implementation of the RCEP Agreement",""],[1,"45","4","Domestic Economic Partnership Agreement Utilization Measures","promote domestic measures to utilize these economic partnership agreements",""],[1,"45","4","World Trade Organization System Strengthening","Japan will strengthen the WTO systems",""],[1,"45","4","International Supply Chain Resilience Cooperation","cooperate with like-minded countries well as to make supply chains more resilient",""],[1,"45","5","Trade Digitalization Promotion Initiative","The government will promote trade DX, including the use of the trade platform (Trade PF), data standardization, and the electronification of bills of lading through the amendment of the Commercial Code.",""],[1,"45","5","ERIA Activity Strengthening","will strengthen ERIA activities.",""],[1,"45","6","Digital Services Overseas Expansion Initiative","Amid the expansion of AI and other digital-related markets, Japan will promote overseas expansion of Japan’s digital-related overall services, including not only so-called digital deficit fields but also financial services, such as fund settlement and intellectual property royalties, thereby aiming to improve digital-related balance of payments.",""],[1,"45","7","Impact Investment Dialogue and Communication Forum","Established in November 2023 as a forum for dialogue and communication related to impact investment.",""],[1,"45","7","Trade Procedures Digitization Action Plan Roadmap","Action Plan Roadmap for the Digitization of Trade Procedures",""]],"21":[[1,"79","2","Universal Health Coverage Knowledge Hub","we will establish the UHC Knowledge Hub in Japan as a global center for universal health coverage (UHC)",""],[1,"79","2","Impact Investment Initiative for Global Health","Through ‘Impact Investment Initiative for Global Health (Triple I for GH)’ we will continue encouraging Japanese companies to expand overseas and to contribute to global health.",""],[1,"79","2","Foreign Healthcare Personnel Development","developing foreign healthcare personnel in collaboration with ERIA",""],[1,"79","2","International Health and Medical Care Initiatives","expanding international initiatives in health, medical care, and long-term care, including inbound medical travel",""],[1,"79","2","International Infectious Disease Control","combating infectious diseases",""],[1,"79","2","Health Systems Strengthening in Low-Income Countries","strengthening health systems, particularly in low-income countries",""]],"22":[[1,"59","4","Cross-Government Foreign Nationals Inclusion Leadership","we will strengthen cross-government leadership, including the Ministerial Conference on Acceptance and Coexistence of Foreign Nationals, to realize well-ordered inclusion and integration foreign nationals.",""],[1,"59","4","Foreign Nationals Situation Monitoring","We will also enhance our understanding of the actual situation",""],[1,"59","4","Government Information Infrastructure Improvement","improve the information infrastructure of both national and local governments",""],[1,"59","4","Globalized Society Administrative Systems Review","we will carry out a comprehensive and cross-cutting review of systems and administrative practices that were not originally designed with a globalized society in mind.",""],[1,"59","5","Japan Electronic System for Travel Authorization","The government aims to introduce the Japan Electronic System for Travel Authorization (JESTA) in FY 2028.",""],[1,"59","5","Visa and Immigration Fee Review","We will set and review fees of visas and immigration procedure, taking into account factors including the standards of other major countries.",""],[1,"59","5","Immigration Screening and Residency Management Enhancement","By utilizing digital technologies and strengthening both personnel and physical resources, we will enhance and sophisticate immigration screening and residency management;",""],[1,"59","5","Support Programme for Foreign Residents","improve support for foreign residents to realize a society of harmonious coexistence;",""],[1,"59","5","New Specified Residence Card","introduce a new type of residence card (Specified",""],[1,"60","1","Refugee Protection and Assistance Measures","ensure the swift and reliable protection and assistance for refugees and others in need",""],[1,"60","1","Illegal Employment Control and Provisional Release Monitoring","tighten measures against illegal employment and improve monitoring the movements of provisional releasees",""],[1,"60","1","Zero Illegal Foreign Residents Enforcement Policy","pursue the principle of “Zero Illegal Foreign Residents” through detection and deportation",""],[1,"60","2","Foreign Worker Admission Field and Quota Framework","the government will establish industrial fields and expected numbers of foreign nationals to be accepted",""],[1,"60","2","Supervising and Support Organization Requirements Reform","tighten the requirements for supervising and support organizations",""],[1,"60","2","Employment-for-Skill-Development Administrative Infrastructure","establish the necessary administrative infrastructure, including the Employment-for-Skill-Development Organization",""],[1,"60","2","Nationally Accredited Japanese Language Education System","We will also develop the system of nationally accredited Japanese language educational institutions and promote their active use.",""],[1,"60","2","Foreign Driver License Conversion and Social Security Compliance Improvement","Improving procedures for foreign driver’s license conversion and social security compliance",""],[1,"60","3","Foreign Driver’s License Conversion Verification Reform","To improve the process of converting foreign driver's licenses into Japanese driver's licenses, the government will tighten address verification procedures and strengthen the confirmation of applicants' knowledge and driving skills.",""],[1,"60","3","Residence Screening Information Integration","We will consider better integration of information on outstanding payments and unpaid medical expenses into the residence screening process.",""],[1,"60","3","Foreign Nationals Insurance Coverage Framework Review","Review the framework for insurance coverage for foreign nationals.",""],[1,"60","3","Foreign Nationals Benefits Use Management Measures","We will take necessary measures to ensure that foreign nationals use child allowances and financial aid for educational expense appropriately and in line with their actual circumstances.",""]],"23":[[1,"3","12","Regional Revitalization 2.0 Policy","Promoting Regional Revitalization 2.0—the Reiwa Era remodeling of the",""],[1,"10","1","Regional Revitalization 2.0 Initiative","the government will construct strong economic foundations and affluent living foundations in regional areas through initiatives under \"Regional Revitalization 2.0.\"",""],[1,"10","1","Regional Connections and Value Creation Platform","Strengthening connections among individuals and organizations creates new value which will attract new people, further diversify regions, and create a richer and stronger virtuous cycle, making a new platform for creating values.",""],[1,"10","1","Ten-Year Regional Revitalization Framework","the government will strongly promote the framework for the next 10 years based on the Basic Concepts for Regional Revitalization 2.0",""],[1,"9","5","Regional High-Quality Industry and Employment Development","create high-quality industries and employment opportunities in regional areas",""],[1,"19","1","Population Decline Adaptation Measures","then to take adaptation measures to enable economic growth and the functioning of society even if the population size shrinks.",""],[1,"19","1","Local Development for Young People and Women","Therefore, we need to develop local areas chosen by young people and women.",""],[1,"19","2","AI and Digital Technology Deployment for Local Living","The thorough use of AI and digital technologies will create a safe and comfortable living environment for local residents.",""],[1,"19","2","Local Technology-Enabled Product and Service Development","will also combine new technologies with local unique natural resources, culture, and traditional technologies, etc., enabling us to create high-value-added products and services.",""],[1,"19","3","Urban-Regional Exchange and Collaboration Mechanism","By creating a flow of exchange and combination of people, goods, and technologies centered on the population with strong relationship to the areas, and cross-sectoral cooperation and collaboration between urban and regional areas, as well as within and outside regions, urban and regional areas can transcend the binary oppositional structure and have symbiotic relationships, thereby enhancing Japan’s sustainability as a whole.",""],[1,"19","4","Ten-Year Basic Concept Formulation","the government is formulating a basic concept that quantitatively describes the status we aim for (our vision of an ideal society) 10 years from now",""],[1,"19","4","Regional Revitalization 2.0","vigorously promoting the Regional Revitalization 2.0 as the Reiwa Era remodeling of the Japanese archipelago",""],[1,"19","5","Regional Advanced Initiative Adaptation Mechanism","Achievements of advanced initiatives will be independently and proactively understood by each region, involving diverse stakeholders such as industry, government, academia, finance, labor, media, and professionals,and will be incorporated flexibly, according to the characteristics, resources, and issues of each region",""],[1,"19","5","Regional Workstyle and Workplace Reform","The government will promote social change starting with the reform of working styles and workplaces in regional areas",""],[1,"19","5","Regional Human Resources Development Initiative","The government will promote social change starting with ... the development of human resources who are attached to regional areas and play an active role in",""],[1,"20","1","Sustainable Regional Service Bases Development","we will work on the development of sustainable regional service bases with an eye to the future",""],[1,"20","1","Regional Healthcare Provision System","the maintenance and ensuring of the regional healthcare provision system",""],[1,"20","1","Public-Private Regional Community Development","community development by the public and private sectors’ co-creation utilizing the power of willing and capable private citizens",""],[1,"20","1","Lifelong Active Community CCRC 2.0","the lifelong active community (Japanese version of CCRC) 2.0 for all members and all generations",""],[1,"20","1","Regional Transportation Redesign Rollout","the full-scale rollout of redesigning regional transportation",""],[1,"20","1","Flexible Side-Job Permission and Employment Rules","local governments, regional financial institutions, and Japan Agricultural Cooperatives, etc. will develop the necessary environment, including the promotion of flexible permission standards and revision of employment rules, so that employees are allowed to have by-jobs or side-jobs if they wish",""],[1,"20","1","Local Disaster Management Capacity Strengthening","strengthening disaster management capabilities to protect local areas",""],[1,"20","1","Non-Regular Employee Working Conditions Reform","improving working conditions of non-regular employees with their employment period limited to one fiscal year, and making them full-time employees after their abilities are verified",""],[1,"20","1","Regional Innovation and Creation Initiative","as the Regional Innovation Creation Initiative to create vitality in regional economies and draw out Japan’s potential growth by creating various new combinations",""],[1,"21","1","Integrated Export and Overseas Expansion Support","We will also provide integrated support for exports and overseas expansion",""],[1,"21","1","Luxury Destination Development","increase the creation of luxury destinations",""],[1,"21","1","Smart Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries Development","make agriculture, forestry and fisheries industries smarter",""],[1,"21","1","Japanese Alcoholic Beverage Export Expansion","expand exports of Japanese alcoholic beverages",""],[1,"21","1","Regional Financial Capacity Strengthening","strengthen regional financial power",""],[1,"21","1","Regional Startup Ecosystem and Hub Development","build an ecosystem and hubs to create startups",""],[1,"21","1","Government Agency Relocation to Regional Areas","the relocation of government agencies to regional areas",""],[1,"21","1","Enterprise and University Decentralization","the decentralization of enterprises and universities",""],[1,"21","1","Hometown Resident Registration System","the government will establish the Hometown Resident Registration System to visualize the population with strong relationship to the areas",""],[1,"21","1","Regional Exchange and Dual Residency Promotion","such as promotion of dual residency, promotion of regional exchanges among young people and women, and utilization of hometown tax payment",""],[1,"21","1","Watt-Bit Collaboration Infrastructure Development","the government will promote Watt-Bit Collaboration as infrastructure development to promote industrial location (GX industrial location) that advances GX and DX as well as economic growth",""],[1,"21","1","Nationwide Digital Lifelines Development","The government will promote the development of digital lifelines across the nation in order to accelerate the social implementation of new technologies",""],[1,"22","1","AI-Enabled Regional Issue-Solving and Local Economic Value Creation","make efforts to solve regional issues, such as maintaining and improving their living environment, as well as increasing the added value of their local economy by utilizing AI and digital technologies.",""],[1,"22","1","Wide-Area Regional Cooperation Mechanism","The government will promote Wide-Area Regional Cooperation in order to create conditions for measures that lead to regional economic growth to be seamlessly carried out across a wide area.",""],[1,"22","2","Regional Revitalization Support System for Local Governments","The national government will support small and medium-sized local governments through programs, such as the regional revitalization accompanied support system",""],[1,"22","2","Institutional Reform for Local Structural Issues","will also strengthen institutional approaches to address structural issues facing local communities",""],[1,"22","2","Nationwide Support for Children Childrearing and Education","We will consider how to provide nationwide support, including the issue of financial resources, in light of the role of the national government in children, childrearing and education, as well as the relevant national standards.",""],[1,"22","2","Special Zone Regulatory Reform and Expansion","the government will drastically strengthen the operation of special zone systems through measures such as quickly universalizing the results and providing thorough support for regional challenges",""],[1,"22","2","Regional Revitalization Comprehensive Strategy and PDCA System","the government will formulate a comprehensive strategy that includes appropriate KPIs on the premise of thorough implementation of the PDCA cycle by the end of 2025",""],[1,"22","2","Regional Revitalization Implementation Roadmaps","We will also prepare the roadmap for each period, such as one, three, and five years, to show how policy effects will steadily be built up.",""]],"24":[[1,"25","2","Inbound Tourism Content and Profitability Initiative","the creation of diverse tourism content, such as adventure tourism and the improvement of profitability",""],[1,"25","2","Tourism Human Resources Development Programme","the development of human resources for tourism, including local guides",""],[1,"25","2","Luxury Inbound Tourism Destination Development","the creation of luxury inbound tourist destinations",""],[1,"25","2","National Parks and Public Facilities Tourism Enhancement","the improvement of the appeal of national parks, quasi-national parks, national gardens, and public facilities",""],[1,"25","2","Foreign Visitor Acceptance Infrastructure Improvement","the improvement of environments for accepting foreign nationals such as airports, CIQs, and secondary transportation",""],[1,"25","2","Regional Domestic Aviation Network Expansion","expanding the use of domestic aviation networks, including regional routes, through inbound tourism",""],[1,"25","2","Sustainable Cruise Growth and Base Formation","the sustainable growth and the base formation for cruises",""],[1,"25","2","Strategic Tourism Promotion Initiative","strategic promotion",""],[1,"25","2","MICE Attraction and Hosting Programme","the attraction and holding of MICE",""],[1,"25","2","Integrated Resort Development and Casino Regulation","the development of integrated resorts (IR), including enforcement of strict casino regulations",""],[1,"25","2","Digital Nomad Attraction Initiative","attracting digital nomads",""],[1,"25","2","Outbound Tourism and Interactive Exchange Promotion","the expansion of interactive exchanges by outbound promotion",""],[1,"25","3","Tourism Facility Renovation Programme","renovating facilities",""],[1,"25","3","Seamless Tourist Reception Environment Development","developing the seamless reception environment of tourist spots, including the removal of abandoned buildings",""],[1,"25","3","Destination Management Organization Management Strengthening","strengthening the management system of Destination Management / Marketing Organization (DMO)",""],[1,"25","3","Domestic Tourism Exchange Market Expansion","we will promote initiatives related to the expansion of the domestic exchange market",""],[1,"25","3","Tourism Operational Efficiency and Labor-Saving Measures","including the improvement of operational efficiency and labor saving",""],[1,"25","3","Tourism Human Resource Shortage Measures","measures against human resource shortages",""],[1,"25","3","Overtourism Prevention and Control Measures","the prevention and curb of overtourism",""],[1,"25","3","Universal Tourism Promotion Initiative","the promotion of universal tourism",""],[1,"25","4","Basic Plan for the Promotion of a Tourism Nation","the government will formulate a new Basic Plan for the Promotion of a Tourism Nation by the end of fiscal 2025",""],[1,"25","4","National Tourism Financial Resource Measures","will specifically consider measures to secure necessary national financial resources",""],[1,"25","6","Mountain Hut and Trail Conservation Programme","This includes the maintenance and conservation of mountain huts and trails as well as utilization of long trails.",""],[1,"25","6","Airport Operations Workforce Development Programme","This includes promoting efforts to secure and nurture human resources in airport operations, including local airports, such as ground handling and security screening, and to improve their working conditions.",""]],"25":[[1,"28","2","Forest Reforestation Programme","reforestation",""],[1,"28","2","Forest Consolidation Policy","promote forest consolidation",""],[1,"28","2","Digital Forest Demarcation Initiative","demarcation using digital technology",""],[1,"28","2","Forestry Human Resources and Management Body Development","development of diverse human resources and management bodies responsible for the circular use of forest resources",""],[1,"28","2","Forest Road Infrastructure Development","forest road infrastructure development",""],[1,"28","2","Smart Forestry Development","smart forestry",""],[1,"28","2","Domestic Wood Conversion and Utilization Expansion","conversion of domestic wood and expansion of wood use through CLT and JAS structural materials",""],[1,"28","3","Marine Resource Surveys and Assessments Improvement","the fundamental improvements in resource surveys and assessments",""],[1,"28","3","New Fisheries Operating Models","the shift to new forms of operation",""],[1,"28","3","Fisheries Management and Human Resources Development","the securing of management bodies and human resources",""],[1,"28","3","Fishing Port and Grounds Improvement","the strengthening of fisheries by improving fishing ports and grounds",""],[1,"28","4","Cost Indicator Publication Mechanism","The government will advance initiatives to formulate and publish cost indicators, which take into account raw material costs, labor and other costs, so as to contribute to price formation.",""],[1,"29","1","Aquaculture Growth Sector Development","to turn aquaculture into a growth sector",""],[1,"29","1","Nationwide UMIGYO Development","the nationwide development of the UMIGYO",""]],"27":[[1,"65","4","Gender-Responsive Policy and Project Planning","planning and implementing policies and projects that consider sex-disaggregated differences in the impact and needs",""],[1,"65","4","Sex-Disaggregated Data Collection and Analysis","strengthening sex-disaggregated data collection and analysis",""],[1,"65","5","Women’s Entrepreneurship Support Programme","supporting women’s entrepreneurship",""],[1,"65","5","Gender Pay Gap Information Disclosure Policy","disclosing information concerning pay differences",""],[1,"66","1","Work-Life Balance Support for Women","helping women balance work with childcare, long-term care, and health issues",""],[1,"66","1","Female Digital Talent Development Programme","developing female talent in digital fields",""],[1,"66","1","Gender Pay Gap Action Plans","formulating action plans in five industries with large pay differences between men and women",""],[1,"66","1","Women in Science and Engineering Initiative","We will also implement initiatives to increase the proportion of women in science and engineering, including in AI and IT, among university and technical college students, faculty, and others.",""],[1,"66","1","Early STEM Opportunities and Role Models Programme","we will foster interest among female junior and senior high school students and enhance their motivation and potential by providing early and continuous opportunities to learn cutting-edge science and technology and to engage with female role models in STEM.",""],[1,"66","1","Cross-Sector STEM Gender Coordination Mechanism","These efforts will be supported through coordinated initiatives involving industry, academia, government, and local communities",""],[1,"66","1","Women’s Senior University Leadership Appointments","promoting the appointment of women to senior positions at universities",""],[1,"66","1","Regional Women’s Reskilling and Upskilling Support","We will further strengthen reskilling and upskilling support for women living in regional areas",""],[1,"66","1","Skills-Based Employment Support for Regional Women","promote initiatives that help them find jobs where they can make use of their skills",""],[1,"66","2","Gender Equality Promotion Organization Establishment","we will establish a new organization to replace and strengthen the functions of the National Women's Education Center and promote gender equality in local communities",""],[1,"66","2","Women's Health Research and Support Network","we will advance research and studies conducted at the Integrated Center for Women's Health, universities, and research institutions, and the development of a nationwide support network",""],[1,"66","2","SME KENKO Investment for Health Support","we will support KENKO investment for Health efforts in small and medium-sized enterprises",""],[1,"66","2","Femtech Promotion for Women's Health","promote the use of femtech as part of broader women's health initiatives",""],[1,"66","2","Women's Restroom Access and Conditions Improvement","We will improve access to and conditions for women’s restrooms by monitoring domestic and international trends and advancing necessary measures",""],[1,"66","2","Gender-Responsive Disaster Management and Reconstruction","disaster management and reconstruction from the perspective of gender equality",""],[1,"66","2","Women, Peace and Security Implementation","Women, Peace and Security (WPS)",""],[1,"66","2","Sexual and Domestic Violence Response Measures","countermeasures against sexual crimes, sexual violence, domestic violence, and stalking, including expanding consultation and support for diverse victims196",""],[1,"66","2","Support for Women Facing Complex Challenges","assistance for women facing complex challenges",""],[1,"67","1","Public-Private Collaborative Support System for Young Women","young women, through the development of collaborative support systems between the public and private sectors.",""],[1,"67","3","Non-Consensual Sexual Image Protection Law","the Act Prescribing Punishments for the Non-Consensual Recording and Distribution of Sexual Images, and Establishing Measures for Deleting the Electronic and Magnetic Records of Non-Consensual Images That Have Been Recorded on Seized Articles (Act No. 67 of 2023)",""],[1,"67","3","Sexual Harm Reality and Reporting Difficulty Surveys","implementation of surveys on the reality of sexual harm, including difficulty in reporting.",""]],"28":[[1,"61","2","Measures Against Crimes and Nuisance Behavior","we will strengthen measures against crimes and nuisance behavior.",""],[1,"61","3","CBRNE Threat Countermeasures","countermeasures against CBRNE 162 threats",""],[1,"61","3","Counter-Terrorism and Threat Response Measures","counter-terrorism measures, including responses to illegal drone flights and lone-offender163 threats",""],[1,"61","3","Civil Protection Measures","enhancing civil protection measures",""],[1,"61","3","Anti-Money Laundering and Terrorist Financing Measures","strengthening efforts against money laundering, terrorist financing, and proliferation financing in anticipation of the FATF's164 5th round Mutual Evaluation of Japan",""],[1,"61","3","Law Enforcement Drone Use Promotion","promoting the use of drones by law enforcement agencies",""],[1,"61","4","Advanced Investigation Methods for Anonymous Criminal Groups","These efforts will include more sophisticated investigation methods, aiming to eliminate anonymous and fluid criminal groups.",""],[1,"61","4","Local Crime Prevention and Security Camera Support","In parallel, we will reinforce local crime prevention capabilities, including support for the installation of security cameras.",""],[1,"61","5","Inmate Treatment Enhancement Programme","enhance treatment of inmates in penal institutions",""],[1,"61","5","Volunteer Probation Officer Support Measures","promote measures such as enhancing support for volunteer probation officers",""],[1,"61","5","Crime Victim Support Measures","we will strengthen relevant measures",""],[1,"61","7","Crime Victim Support Measures","Includes the Further Promotion of Measures for Crime Victims",""],[1,"61","5","Domestic and Overseas Preventive Justice Support","enhance preventive justice support functions both in Japan and overseas",""],[1,"61","5","Comprehensive Legal Support Enhancement","comprehensive legal support",""],[1,"61","5","Online Human Rights Protection Measures","reinforce measures against human rights violations on the internet",""],[1,"61","5","Legal Professional and Justice Infrastructure Development","develop the necessary human and material infrastructure by securing legal professionals and taking other measures",""],[1,"61","6","Legal Technical Assistance and Justice Affairs Diplomacy","We will promote international cooperation and advance “Justice Affairs Diplomacy”, including through legal technical assistance 170",""],[1,"61","7","Offender Rehabilitation Facility Support","enhanced support for offender rehabilitation facilities",""],[1,"61","7","Local Government Crime Prevention Collaboration","strengthening collaboration with local governments",""],[1,"61","7","Law-Related Education Promotion","promotion of law-related education",""],[1,"61","7","Support for Public-Interest Legal Professionals","consideration of necessary support to broaden the activities of young and mid-career legal professionals engaged in public-interest work",""],[1,"61","7","International Counterterrorism Cooperation","strengthened cooperation with countries in Central Asia and other regions",""],[1,"62","1","United Nations Reoffending Reduction Standards Promotion","actively promote the use of United Nations Standards and Norms on Reducing Reoffending",""],[1,"62","1","International Arbitration Promotion","promote international arbitration",""],[1,"62","1","International Legal Human Resources Development","develop international legal human resources",""],[1,"62","1","Foreign-Language Translation of Japanese Laws","accelerate translation of Japanese laws and regulations into foreign languages",""]],"32":[[1,"54","3","Diplomatic Capability Strengthening","we will strengthen our diplomatic capabilities to lead the international community toward global stability and prosperity.",""],[1,"54","4","Sanctions Against Russia","sanctions against Russia",""],[1,"55","1","Official Security Assistance Strengthening","We will also strategically strengthen Official Security Assistance (OSA).",""],[1,"55","2","United Nations and Security Council Reform","We will also work to strengthen the functions of the United Nations, including reform of the Security Council;",""],[1,"55","2","International Law-Based Dispute Resolution","resolve disputes based on international law;",""],[1,"54","3","Rules-Based International Diplomacy Policy","The government will pursue diplomacy that upholds and reinforces a free and open international order based on the rule of law, in order to protect our national interests143.",""],[1,"54","3","Japan-U.S. Alliance Cooperation Enhancement","we will elevate Japan-U.S. cooperation to new heights, recognizing the Japan-U.S. Alliance as the cornerstone of regional peace and prosperity.",""],[1,"54","3","Coordination with Like-Minded Countries and Organizations","we will deepen coordination with like-minded countries and organizations, including the G7, ASEAN, Australia, India, the Republic of Korea, the EU, and NATO.",""],[1,"54","3","Global South Engagement for Enhanced Global Governance","We will also work to enhance global governance through stronger engagement with the Global South144.",""],[1,"54","4","Support for Ukraine","Japan will continue support for Ukraine",""],[1,"54","4","Official Development Assistance Expansion","the government will expand Official Development Assistance (ODA) through a variety of approaches",""],[1,"54","4","CO-creation for Common Agenda Initiative","implementation of new frameworks such as the CO-creation for common agenda initiative",""],[1,"54","4","JICA Act Amendment for Private Capital Mobilization","the amendment of the JICA Act to further promote private capital",""],[1,"54","5","Regional and International Partnership Cooperation","This commitment includes strengthening cooperation with ASEAN and India, as well as Japan's leadership in frameworks such as the Tokyo International Conference on African Development (TICAD), the Pacific Islands Leaders Meeting (PALM), and the \"Central Asia plus Japan\" Dialogue.",""],[1,"55","1","JICA Overseas Cooperation Volunteer Mobilization","leveraging the JICA Overseas Cooperation Volunteer",""],[1,"55","1","International Partnership Collaboration Mechanism","strengthening collaboration with international organizations and other partners",""],[1,"55","1","Humanitarian Crisis Assistance","responding to humanitarian crises, including assistance for Palestine",""],[1,"55","1","Global Food, Health, Climate and Pollution Response","addressing global challenges in areas such as food security, health, climate change, and plastic pollution",""],[1,"55","2","Nuclear Disarmament Leadership under NPT Regime","Japan will lead efforts under the NPT regime to realize a world without nuclear weapons.",""],[1,"55","2","International Norm Development through Organizations","contribute to the development of international norms through international organizations",""],[1,"55","2","Expansion of Japanese International Organization Personnel","increase the number of Japanese personnel serving in these bodies;",""],[1,"55","2","Women, Peace and Security Agenda Advancement","advance the Women, Peace and Security (WPS) agenda;",""],[1,"55","2","Human Security Promotion Policy","promote human security;",""],[1,"55","2","Japan Affinity and Knowledge Cultivation Programme","cultivate people with great affinity toward or knowledge of Japan, including individuals of Japanese descent;",""],[1,"55","2","Accurate Sovereignty and History Information Provision","actively provide accurate information concerning such subjects as territory and sovereignty, recognition of history both in Japan and abroad;",""],[1,"55","2","Cultural Diplomacy Enhancement Policy","enhance cultural diplomacy.",""],[1,"55","2","North Korea Relations Normalization Initiative","The government will achieve the normalization of relations with North Korea, in accordance with the Japan-DPRK Pyongyang Declaration, through comprehensively resolving outstanding issues of concern such as the abductions146, nuclear, and missile issues, as well as settlement of the unfortunate past.",""],[1,"55","3","Diplomatic Operations Efficiency Reform","improving efficiency and streamlining operations",""],[1,"55","3","Diplomatic Human Resource Capacity Strengthening","we will strengthen our human resource capacity",""],[1,"55","3","Diplomatic Financial Base and Flexible Work Support","build a more robust financial base, including support for diverse working styles",""],[1,"55","3","Overseas Mission Resilience Improvement","improve the resilience of overseas missions",""],[1,"55","3","Expanded Consular Services","expand consular services",""],[1,"55","3","Diplomatic Information Security Infrastructure Enhancement","enhance our information security infrastructure",""],[1,"55","5","Act for Partial Revision of the Japan International Cooperation Agency Act","Act for Partial Revision of the Act on the Japan International Cooperation Agency, Independent Administrative Agency (Act No. 21 of 2025).",""]],"34":[[1,"59","3","Technology Leakage Prevention Measures","implement measures to prevent technology leakage, including the management of trade secrets",""],[1,"59","3","Economic Coercion Response Measures","address economic coercion",""],[1,"58","2","Multi-Stakeholder Government and Civil Society Collaboration","promote collaboration and mutual understanding among national and local governments, industry, academia, and civil society",""],[1,"58","3","Economic Intelligence and Think Tank Capacity Strengthening","work to strengthen our response capabilities—including economic intelligence functions and integrated think tank capabilities 157",""],[1,"58","3","Critical Infrastructure Resilience Enhancement","while also enhancing the resilience of critical infrastructure.",""],[1,"58","4","Economic Security Promotion Act Review","we will promptly begin reviewing the Act with a view to securing Japan's strategic autonomy and indispensability.",""],[1,"58","4","Critical Goods and Essential Services Supply Stabilization","We will consider measures to ensure a stable supply of goods essential for providing services, including international communications, submarine cables, and shipping, and also ensure service delivery essential for supply of these goods.",""],[1,"58","4","Critical Goods Supply Effort Effectiveness Measures","we will consider ways to enhance the effectiveness of efforts to ensure a stable supply of critical goods.",""],[1,"58","4","Digitalization and Robotics Labor Shortage Response","We will also study measures to advance digitalization, robotics, and data integration to address labor shortages.",""],[1,"58","4","Critical Technology Areas Definition and Collaboration","A list of critical technology areas must be defined to accelerate the development of advanced key technologies and promote international collaboration for that purpose.",""],[1,"58","4","Essential Infrastructure System Expansion","adding the Health Insurance Claims Review & Reimbursement Services and medical institutions to the Essential Infrastructure System",""],[1,"58","4","Major Data Holder Regulatory Framework","ensuring appropriate regulations for major data holders, as well as entities responsible for data storage and processing",""],[1,"58","4","AI and Digital Infrastructure Strengthening","strengthening AI and digital infrastructure",""],[1,"58","4","Overseas Connectivity Project Expansion Support","supporting the overseas expansion of projects that help maintain and enhance economic connectivity with allied and like-minded countries and the Global South, such as those on ports and repair docks project.",""],[1,"58","4","Manufacturing Technology and Supply Strengthening","We will promote the development of manufacturing technologies and strengthen supply",""],[1,"58","5","Integrated Economic Security Think Tank Function","An integrated think tank function that provides the government with comprehensive policy recommendations in the field of economic security from the perspectives of diplomacy, intelligence, defense, economy, and technology.",""],[1,"59","1","Unmanned Aerial Vehicle Production Infrastructure","establishing production infrastructure for unmanned aerial vehicles, including drones.",""],[1,"59","2","Strategic Technology Standards Rulemaking Support","supporting rulemaking for strategic domains such as quantum, digital, and AI technologies",""],[1,"59","2","Public-Private Innovation Networks","building public-private networks",""],[1,"59","2","Domestic Testing and Certification Infrastructure","enhancing domestic testing and certification infrastructure",""],[1,"59","2","International Standards in Government Procurement","promoting the application of international standards in government procurement",""],[1,"59","3","Foreign Investment Screening Effectiveness Measures","The government will work to ensure the effectiveness of investment screening under the Foreign Exchange and Foreign Trade Act 160",""],[1,"59","3","Advanced Technology Export Controls","control the export of advanced technologies",""],[1,"59","3","Research Security and Integrity Safeguards","safeguard research security and integrity",""],[1,"59","3","Foreign Student and Researcher Screening","strengthen the screening of foreign students and researchers",""],[1,"59","3","Sanctions and Trade Remedy Response Measures","respond to various sanctions and trade remedy measures",""]],"35":[[1,"48","4","National Crisis Management System Reinforcement","the government will reinforce the country's crisis management system to protect lives and ensure the continuity of essential state and social functions, including enhancing its capacity to respond to complex and multiple disasters.",""],[1,"49","1","Disaster Response Capability Strengthening","we will work to improve our disaster response capabilities.",""],[1,"49","2","Disaster Management Agency Establishment","the government will establish an agency for disaster management by FY 2026.",""],[1,"49","2","Evacuation Living Environment Improvement Programme","improving the evacuation living environment",""],[1,"49","2","Disaster Welfare Support Enhancement","enhancing welfare support",""],[1,"49","2","Local Disaster Management Strengthening","strengthening local disaster management",""],[1,"49","2","Public-Private Disaster Management Collaboration","promoting public-private collaboration",""],[1,"49","2","Disaster Management Education and Awareness Programme","advancing education for disaster management and awareness",""],[1,"49","2","Disaster Management Training and Capacity Building","training and capacity building",""],[1,"49","2","Digital Transformation in Disaster Management","promoting digital transformation in disaster management",""],[1,"49","2","Advanced Disaster Response Technology Development","developing and globally promoting advanced technologies for disaster response, such as rescue robots that can operate on-site using AI and robotics",""],[1,"49","2","Regional Disaster Management Hub Development","We will also explore the establishment of regional disaster management hubs.",""],[1,"49","3","National Resilience and Disaster Mitigation Initiative","To this end, we will steadily promote initiatives to strengthen national resilience, including disaster management, mitigation, and countermeasures against aging infrastructure, without interruption.",""],[1,"50","1","Integrated National Resilience Measures","promote efforts that integrate hard and soft measures, in accordance with the Fundamental Plan for National Resilience.",""],[1,"50","2","National Resilience Implementation and Adaptive Development","The government will steadily promote the engagement based on the First Mid-term Plan for the Implementation of National Resilience133 and will proceed with national development that will not succumb to disasters.",""],[1,"51","2","Project Progress Monitoring Mechanism","we will begin examining concrete approaches to monitor project progress",""],[1,"51","2","Financial Resource Mobilization Mechanism","we will begin examining concrete approaches to monitor project progress and secure financial resources",""]],"37":[[1,"52","1","Fukushima Daiichi Nuclear Power Station Decommissioning","steadily proceed with the decommissioning of Fukushima Daiichi Nuclear Power Station.",""],[1,"52","1","ALPS Treated Water Safety and Livelihood Support Measures","we will carry out all possible measures to ensure safety, prevent adverse impacts on reputation, and support continuation of livelihoods.",""],[1,"52","1","Advocacy for Lifting Food Import Restrictions","We will strongly call for the immediate lifting of import restrictions on Japanese food products.",""],[1,"52","1","Managed Recycling and Final Disposal of Removed Soil","We will promote the managed recycling of removed soil arising from decontamination activities in reconstruction and revitalization projects, and take a whole-of-government approach to ensuring its final disposal outside Fukushima Prefecture.",""],[1,"52","1","Fukushima Decontamination and Return-Area Infrastructure Development","we will proceed with decontamination and infrastructure development in the specified living areas for returnees.",""],[1,"52","1","Expanded Activity Options in Restricted Areas","we will begin exploring ways to allow freer activity in restricted areas, based on the premise of ensuring safety.",""],[1,"52","1","Living Environment Improvement in Evacuation-Order-Lifted Areas","The living environment must be improved in evacuation-order-lifted areas.",""],[1,"52","1","Forest Restoration Initiatives","Restoration initiatives must be launched in forests where no restoration program has yet been implemented.",""],[1,"52","1","Fukushima Innovation and New Energy Promotion","the government will promote the efforts of the Fukushima Institute for Research, Education and Innovation and the Fukushima Plan for a New Energy Society.",""],[1,"52","1","Fukushima Livelihood Reconstruction Programme","We will also advance the reconstruction of livelihoods, including in agriculture, forestry, and fisheries.",""],[1,"52","1","New Industry Development in Energy, Robotics and Space","support the development of new industries such as energy, robotics, and space",""],[1,"52","1","Hope Tourism and Fukushima Hamadori Cycle Route Promotion","Our initiatives will also include promoting \"Hope Tourism,\" where the Fukushima Hamadori Cycle Route can serve as a key attraction",""],[1,"52","1","Cultural and Arts-Based Visitor Attraction Development","capitalizing on cultural and art assets of the prefecture to expand non-residential visiting and/or relational population.",""]],"38":[[1,"68","3","Medium- to Long-Term Economic and Fiscal Outlook Development","developing a medium- to long-term view of our economic and fiscal outlook",""],[1,"68","4","Business and Individual New Action Support","the government to actively support those undertaking new actions through a range of policy tools",""],[1,"68","4","Fiscal Consolidation Policy","we will also pursue fiscal consolidation",""],[1,"68","4","Multi-Year Policy Implementation Planning","it is important to implement key policies over multiple fiscal years in a planned and consistent manner",""],[1,"68","4","Evidence-Based Wise Spending Mechanism","we will fully enforce wise spending based on the evidence-based policy making (EBPM) approach",""],[1,"68","5","Domestic Government Bond Ownership Promotion","we must continue our efforts to further encourage domestic ownership of government bonds",""],[1,"68","5","Stable Government Bond Issuance Mechanism","maintaining conditions that allow for the stable issuance of government bonds in the market",""],[1,"68","5","Fiscal Consolidation for Emergency Fiscal Space","we must pursue fiscal consolidation to secure fiscal space",""],[1,"68","6","Expenditure Reform Policy","continue expenditure reform efforts",""],[1,"69","2","Flexible Macroeconomic Policy and Fiscal Consolidation","macroeconomic policy options in line with the circumstances, including the response to the U.S. tariff measures, and appropriate response to price hikes",""],[1,"69","3","Fiscal Consolidation and Public Debt Reduction Policy","we will resolutely pursue fiscal consolidation",""],[1,"69","3","Economic and Fiscal Impact Response Mechanism","we should examine their economic and fiscal impacts and respond to them appropriately",""],[1,"69","3","Public Expenditure Reform Programme","the government will continue expenditure reform efforts set forth in the Basic Policy 2024",""],[1,"69","3","Social Security Insurance Burden Restraint Measures","we will continue our efforts to restrain insurance premium burdens through past reforms",""],[1,"69","3","Professional Services Stability and Wage Increase Measures","we will implement measures that surely lead to stable business management and wage increases for a wide range of professionals working in the field",""],[1,"70","1","Economic and Price Trend Adjustment in Public Finance","we will also reflect economic and price trends appropriately, taking into account Section 4, Chapter 3, \"Review and Revision of public systems in line with rising prices.\"",""],[1,"70","2","Primary Balance Surplus Return Rule","At the same time, we will also begin examining the establishment of a rule whereby, if a primary balance turns into a surplus and exceeds a certain level, it will be returned to the economy and society by expanding policies that contribute to economic growth and other objectives.",""],[1,"70","3","Comprehensive Tax System Review for Structural Changes","we will conduct comprehensive studies to manifest the best tax system for coping with a declining birthrate, an aging population, globalization, and other socioeconomic structural changes.",""],[1,"70","4","Personal Income Tax System Reform","From the perspectives of addressing rising prices, correcting disparities, and ensuring effective income redistribution, the government will undertake a fundamental reform of the personal income tax system203.",""],[1,"70","4","Evidence-Based Policymaking Promotion","The government will steadily promote efforts for EBPM.",""],[1,"70","4","Digital Tax Administration and Compliance Reform","At the same time, from the perspectives of building a tax system and improving the tax compliance environment suited to a digital society as well as ensuring proper and fair taxation, we will step up efforts both in terms of the system and its enforcement and seek to respond to new international taxation rules.",""],[1,"70","5","Technological Innovation Promotion","we will promote technological innovation",""]],"39":[[1,"72","1","Fair Social Security Burden-Sharing Reform","ensuring fair burden-sharing based on the ability to pay, by revising the current structure that places a disproportionate load on working-age generations",""],[1,"72","4","Financial-Income-Based Insurance Premium Reform","To reflect financial income in the premium burden under the medical and long-term care insurance systems, we will develop specific policy designs.",""],[1,"73","1","Evidence-Based Social Security Spending and Analysis","spending based on EBPM, including various data analyses and research, while controlling the rise in insurance premium burdens.",""],[1,"73","1","Public Information on the Social Security System","we will provide clear and accessible information to the public, including young people, about the future vision of the social security system for all generations.",""],[1,"74","5","Medical Insurance Benefits and Burdens Review","With regard to the medical insurance system, we will proceed with a comprehensive review of benefits and burdens, while trying to balance between the two and restrain the rising burden on the working generation.",""],[1,"74","5","High-Cost Medical Expense Policy Review","we will carefully listen to the views of stakeholders, including long-term care patients themselves, and decide on a policy",""],[1,"75","4","Working-Style-Neutral Public Pension Framework","we will work to create a framework that is neutral to working styles",""],[1,"75","4","Employees’ Insurance Coverage Expansion","we will further expand employees' insurance coverage",""],[1,"75","4","Old-Age Pension System Review","review the old-age pension system for current workers",""],[1,"75","4","Annual Income Barrier and Support Enhancement Package","we will promote the use of the Annual Income Barrier and Support Enhancement Package216",""],[1,"75","6","Fiscal Support Framework Review","reviewing the framework of fiscal support, including Adjustment Subsidies and the Insurer Effort Support System",""],[1,"75","6","Medical Care System Structure Review for Older Persons","examining the structure of the Medical Care System for the Latter-Stage Elderly",""],[1,"75","6","Future Direction of Medical Assistance under Public Assistance","considering the future direction of medical assistance under public assistance recipients",""],[1,"75","6","National Pension System Reform","Act Partially Amending the National Pension Act, Etc., to Strengthen the Functions of the Pension System Based on Socio-economic Changes (enacted on June 13, 2025).",""]],"40":[[1,"71","2","Service Fee Revision for Healthcare and Welfare Sectors","we will take appropriate and necessary actions, such as the next revision of service fees, to ensure that the robust wage increases achieved in the 2025 spring labor-management negotiations204 and the effects of recent price hikes firmly lead to stable management and wage increases for a wide range of professionals working in the field.",""],[1,"71","3","Medical Fee Revision Impact Assessment and Future Measures","we will assess and verify the actual impacts of the revision of medical fees for FY2024, including improvements in working conditions and management circumstances, and consider appropriate future measures",""],[1,"71","3","Long-Term Care and Disability Welfare Workforce Improvement","we will strive to achieve improvements in treatment that are on a par with other occupations, as well as to reduce their workload",""],[1,"71","3","Assessment of Long-Term Care and Disability Welfare Improvements","we will assess and verify the actual outcomes of the improvements that have been implemented to date, and consider future measures",""],[1,"71","3","Tailored Support Responses for Service Providers","We will also explore effective responses for service providers, tailored to their management structure and the nature of services they offer",""],[1,"71","4","Review of Insurance Benefits for OTC Equivalents","reviewing of insurance benefits for over-the-counter (OTC) equivalents205",""],[1,"71","4","Nationwide Expansion of Regional Formularies","expanding the adoption of regional formularies nationwide206",""],[1,"71","4","Hospital Bed Reduction for Community Health Care Planning","reducing hospital beds in preparation for the next phase of Community Health Care Visions207",""],[1,"71","4","Medical Digitalization for More Efficient Care","promoting more efficient and higher-quality care through medical digital",""],[1,"71","5","OTC Medicines and Test Kits Self-Medication Promotion Review","The review will include studying appropriate use policies for specific items and exploring effective approaches to promote the adoption of OTC medicines and test kits for self-medication.",""],[1,"71","5","Healthcare Access and Out-of-Pocket Expense Protection","In the course of the review, we will ensure that necessary access to medical care at healthcare facilities is maintained and that consideration is given to children, individuals with chronic conditions, and low-income patients in terms of out-of-pocket expenses.",""],[1,"71","5","Regional Formulary Development Support","We will consider measures to promote the use of regional formularies and support efforts so that such formularies are developed in each region.",""],[1,"71","5","Community Healthcare Bed Capacity Surveys","For general, long-term, and psychiatric care beds that are likely to become unnecessary owing to population decline and other factors, we will conduct surveys based on local conditions.",""],[1,"71","5","Regional Healthcare Bed Capacity Reduction","Toward the new round of Community Health Care Visions to be formulated in two years, we will take irreversible steps and aim to reduce beds based on the survey results before the next plan is finalized.",""],[1,"72","2","Healthcare and Care Digital Transformation Initiative","the government will work to achieve productivity improvements and labor savings in the medical, long-term care, and disability welfare sectors and to reduce the workload of personnel while enhancing their skills by promoting healthcare and long-term care DX, ICT, long-term care technologies, the implementation of robotics and digital tools, and the secondary use of data",""],[1,"72","2","Expanded Use of Trained Nurses and Task-Sharing Reform","making better use of nurses who have completed training in specified medical procedures; and encouraging task shifting and task sharing",""],[1,"72","2","Regional Medical and Social Welfare Coordination Networks","the government will utilize Regional Medical Coordination Promotion Corporations and Social Welfare Coordination Promotion Corporations, and build networks among small-scale providers",""],[1,"72","2","Healthcare and Welfare Provider Management Transparency Initiative","We will also work to further enhance the visibility of management information of medical institutions, nursing care facilities, and disability welfare service providers",""],[1,"72","2","Regulation of Inappropriate Healthcare Staffing Agency Practices","we will implement effective measures to address the issue of inappropriate staffing agency practices in the medical, nursing care, and disability welfare sectors",""],[1,"74","1","Primary Care and Integrated Medical Services Coordination System","system that ensures the effective functioning of primary care physicians; promoting the functional differentiation and coordination of medical services, as well as collaboration between health care and long-term care",""],[1,"74","1","Emergency Medical Services Provision","securing emergency medical services",""],[1,"74","1","Doctor Helicopter Operations and Equipment Renewal","ensuring the safe and sustainable operation of doctor helicopters, including the renewal of necessary equipment",""],[1,"74","1","Physician Dispatch System Strengthening","we will strengthen physician dispatch systems by supporting university hospitals and core medical institutions",""],[1,"74","1","Clinical Training Environment for Medical Students","establish an environment that enables medical students to focus on clinical training",""],[1,"74","1","Appropriate Online Medical Consultation Use","promote appropriate use of online medical consultations",""],[1,"74","1","Surgeon Workforce Support","support the surgeon, which is in decline",""],[1,"74","1","Prefectural Government Governance Reinforcement","we will work to reinforce the governance of prefectural governments",""],[1,"74","2","Community Health Care Coordination Guidelines","To facilitate smooth coordination within each region regarding the Community Health Care Visions, we will formulate guidelines by the end of FY 2025.",""],[1,"74","2","Community Health Care Vision Development Support","Based on these guidelines, we will support prefectural governments in developing new Community Health Care Visions starting in FY 2026.",""],[1,"74","3","Regional Physician Distribution Correction Package","To correct the uneven distribution of physicians across regions and specialties, we will sequentially implement a comprehensive package of measures.",""],[1,"74","3","Physician Distribution Measures Effectiveness Evaluation","We will also evaluate the effectiveness of these initiatives.",""],[1,"74","4","Physician Placement Support Review","The government will review approaches to supporting the appropriate placement of physicians by the end of 2025.",""],[1,"74","4","Nationwide Physician Matching Function","establishing a nationwide matching function",""],[1,"74","4","Physician Recurrent Education Enhancement","enhancing recurrent education",""],[1,"74","4","Comprehensive Medical Care Physician Development","fostering physicians with comprehensive medical care capabilities, including through medical education",""],[1,"74","4","Overall Physician Training Process Improvement","improving the overall physician training process",""],[1,"74","4","Physician Distribution Imbalance Correction","we will work to correct imbalances in distribution",""],[1,"74","4","Medical School Admissions Optimization","we will proceed with optimizing the number of medical school admissions from FY 2027 onward",""],[1,"74","4","Nursing Personnel Recruitment and Training","we will secure and train nursing personnel for the purpose of addressing regional disparities and other issues",""],[1,"74","4","Digital Transformation in Nursing","promote digital transformation in nursing, including the use of ICT in home-visit care",""],[1,"74","4","Home-Based Medical and Long-Term Care Expansion","advance home-based medical and long-term care, such as by diversifying home care services",""]],"41":[[1,"75","2","Standard Childbirth Cost Elimination Policy","we will work toward eliminating out-of-pocket costs for standard childbirth expenses by around FY 2026.",""],[1,"75","2","Public Funding for Prenatal Checkups","We will promote public funding for prenatal checkups.",""],[1,"75","2","Shussan Navi Information Service Expansion","We will expand the functions of “Shussan Navi (Website for Providing Information on Childbirth Facilities)”.",""],[1,"75","2","Pediatric and Perinatal Medical System Strengthening","we will secure a pediatric and perinatal medical system that includes advanced medical care.",""],[1,"75","2","Obstetric and Pediatric Facility Cooperation and Consolidation Support","we will provide necessary support, including promoting cooperation, consolidation, and prioritization of medical facilities.",""],[1,"75","2","Safe and High-Quality Painless Childbirth Access","We will create an environment where safe and high-quality painless childbirth options are available.",""]],"42":[[1,"75","5","Disease-Specific Health Measures Programme","We will promote measures tailored to specific diseases, including cancer217",""],[1,"76","1","Noncommunicable and Chronic Disease Prevention Efforts","We will also promote efforts addressing intractable diseases, transplant medicine 220, allergies 221, addiction, deafness, nutrition, unwanted second-hand smoking, as well as infectious diseases such as pneumonia",""],[1,"76","1","Scientifically Grounded Vaccination Promotion","including the promotion of scientifically grounded vaccinations222",""],[1,"76","1","Comprehensive Women's Health Support","we will advance comprehensive support for women's health, including responses to menopause and osteoporosis223",""],[1,"76","1","Sleep Apnea Measures in the Transport Industry","we will further promote efforts to address sleep apnea in the transport industry",""],[1,"76","1","Medical Access for Sleep Disorders","improve access to medical care for sleep disorders",""],[1,"76","1","Sleep-Related Health Research","promote sleep-related research",""],[1,"76","1","Sleep Guidelines for Health Promotion Dissemination","raise awareness through the dissemination of Sleep Guidelines for Health Promotion 2023",""],[1,"76","1","KENKO Investment for Health Practices","advance KENKO investment for Health practices",""],[1,"76","1","Sleep-Related Sector Market and Business Support","we will further promote market development and business support in the sleep-related sector",""],[1,"76","2","Lifelong Dental Checkup Promotion Initiative","promote specific initiatives for lifelong dental checkups",""],[1,"76","2","Professional Oral Health Management Programme","We will enhance oral health management by dental professionals to address oral frailty and prevent the progression of dental diseases",""],[1,"76","2","Multi-Professional Dental and Medical Collaboration","promote multi-professional collaboration including between dental institutions and medical-dental-pharmaceutical cooperation",""],[1,"76","2","Dental Workforce Recruitment and Retention Measures","implement measures to secure dental hygienists and dental technicians, including addressing staff turnover",""],[1,"76","2","Dental Laboratory Quality Assurance","ensure the quality of dental laboratories",""],[1,"76","2","Dental Health ICT Adoption Initiative","promote the use of ICT in the dental field",""],[1,"76","2","Dental Healthcare Service Delivery Strengthening","work to develop and strengthen dental health care service delivery systems, including examining the appropriate allocation of dentists based on analysis of shortages in certain regions",""],[1,"76","2","Insurance Coverage for Effective Dental Innovations","promote the coverage under insurance of digital technologies and other new techniques and materials that have been verified to be effective and safe",""],[1,"76","2","Rehabilitation and Social Reintegration Support","We will also promote rehabilitation to support patients' self-reliance, return to home, and reintegration into society",""],[1,"76","4","Cardiovascular Disease Control Initiatives","Initiatives based on the Basic Plan to Promote Cardiovascular Disease Control (Decided by Cabinet on March 28, 2023), including infrastructure development, promotion of research, and support for patients with aftereffects.",""],[1,"76","4","Palliative Care for Renal Failure Patients","Includes palliative care for patients with renal failure.",""],[1,"76","4","Domestic Organ Donation and Transplantation System Restructuring","Includes comprehensive restructuring of systems for domestic organ donation, coordination, and transplantation based on the Istanbul Declaration.",""],[1,"76","4","Uniform Medical Care for Allergic Diseases","Includes the promotion of uniformity of medical care for allergic diseases such as atopic dermatitis.",""],[1,"76","4","Cancer Screening Promotion","Includes efforts to increase cancer screening rates, such as promoting breast cancer screening with consideration for women's specific needs based on scientific evidence.",""]],"43":[[1,"4","8","Declining Birthrate and Child Support Measures","Promoting measures to cope with the declining birthrate and for children",""],[1,"9","2","Declining Birthrate Countermeasure Programme","measures against the declining birthrate",""],[1,"9","2","Children and Young People Policy Promotion","the promotion of policies for children and young people",""],[1,"80","1","Children-Centered Society Policy Package","Through these efforts, we will reverse the trend of declining births and enhance the well-being of children and young people.",""],[1,"80","1","Evidence-Based Policy and Expenditure Management Mechanism","we will make full use of indicators—including the environment surrounding children, the status of local child-rearing support, and numerical targets such as the percentage of women who continued working and the percentage of male workers who take childcare leave—and ensure the effective application of EBPM to achieve wise spending.",""],[1,"80","1","Public Communications for Child-Centered Policies","we will carry out careful public communications to gain broad public support, especially from children and young people, as well as child-rearing households.",""],[1,"80","2","Economic Support for Child-Rearing Households","including economic support, assistance for all children and child-rearing households, and initiatives to promote dual-income and co-parenting families",""],[1,"80","2","Improved Early Childhood Care Staffing","we will improve the treatment of nursery staffs and kindergarten teachers, etc. and improvement of the staff-to-child ratios",""],[1,"80","2","National Early Childhood Education and Care Rollout","national rollout of the Connecting All Children to Early Childhood Education and Care System",""],[1,"80","2","Expanded After-School Children’s Clubs","we will strengthen support for after-school children’s clubs,etc.",""],[1,"80","2","Housing Assistance for Households with Children","provide housing assistance for households with children",""],[1,"80","2","Impact Assessment of Child-Rearing Measures","we will thoroughly assess the overall impact of these measures using indicators related to fertility rates and children's well-being",""],[1,"80","2","Evidence-Based Reprioritization of Child Policies","we will consider reprioritizing and revising the policies to improve their effectiveness",""],[1,"80","2","Expenditure Reform for Child Support Financing","we will secure financial resources by rigorously pursuing expenditure reforms in line with the Reform Process",""],[1,"80","2","Public Awareness for Child-Rearing Support Contributions","we will prepare to raise public awareness about the significance and intended use of the System of Child and Child-rearing Support Contribution to ensure its smooth introduction starting in FY 2026 and to gain public understanding",""],[1,"80","2","Public-Private Collaboration on Child-Rearing","we will foster a shared awareness throughout society through public-private collaboration that children and child-rearing households must",""],[1,"80","3","Promotion of Diverse Experiential Activities","Implementation should include the promotion of diverse experiential activities.",""],[1,"81","1","General Principles for Child-Related Measures","Promoting the General Principles for Child-Related Measures, including support for youth and children facing difficulties",""],[1,"81","2","Child and Youth Protection Support Initiative","We will strengthen support for children and young people facing difficult circumstances, such as abuse, through initiatives, including shelters for children and young people.",""],[1,"81","2","Youth-Led Organization Sustainability Support","We will also implement measures to help sustain the activities of organizations mainly led by young people, which often struggle with funding shortages and maintaining membership.",""],[1,"81","2","Children and Youth Participation in Policymaking","In addition, we will promote participation of children and young people in society and reflection of their views in policymaking, including appointing them as members of various councils and committees.",""],[1,"81","2","Young People’s Life Planning and Marriage Support","Furthermore, we will provide support for life planning and marriage among young people through public-private collaboration.",""],[1,"81","3","Early Childhood Development Quality Enhancement","We will enhance the quality of early childhood development based on the First 100 Months of Growth Vision238",""],[1,"81","3","Child-Friendly Ibasho Support","provide support aligned with the Guidelines for the Creation of Ibasho (place where one feels comfortable, safe and accepted) for Children239",""],[1,"81","3","Childcare Workforce Workload Reduction","work to reduce the workload in childcare settings",""],[1,"81","3","Childcare Personnel Security Initiative","secure childcare personnel as outlined in the amended Child Welfare Act240",""]],"44":[[1,"81","3","Maternal and Child Health Services","maternal and child health services such as postpartum care, newborn screening, newborn hearing screening, and health checkups for infants and children",""],[1,"81","3","Infertility and Recurrent Pregnancy Loss Consultation Support","consultation support for infertility and recurrent pregnancy loss",""],[1,"81","3","Miscarriage and Stillbirth Support","support for those who have experienced miscarriage or stillbirth",""],[1,"81","3","Preconception Care Promotion Plan","We will advance initiatives outlined in the Five-Year Plan for Promoting Preconception Care241",""],[1,"81","3","Egg Freezing Information and Evidence Environment","work to establish an environment that facilitates access to information and evidence collection related to egg freezing",""],[1,"81","3","Children Mannaka Community Development","promote the development of Children Mannaka communities",""],[1,"82","1","Child Food, Learning, and Experiential Support","strengthen watching over by supporting children's cafeterias, meal deliveries for children, learning assistance, and opportunities for experiential activities.",""],[1,"82","1","Single-Parent Household Support","We will strengthen multi-faceted, hands-on support for single-parent households, including securing child support payments while considering each child's specific circumstances.",""],[1,"82","1","Employment and Financial Support Review","we will review the approaches to employment and financial support, taking into account broader socioeconomic trends.",""],[1,"82","2","Disability Support and Inclusion Programme","We will provide support for children with disabilities, including those with developmental disabilities or under medical care, and their families; promote inclusion",""],[1,"82","2","Nationwide Children's Hospice Expansion","work to expand children's hospices nationwide",""],[1,"82","2","Young Carer Assistance Programme","offer assistance to young carers.",""],[1,"82","2","Safe Community Places for Children","We will promote the creation of diverse Ibasho (place where one feels comfortable,safe and accepted) for Children outside of school and home",""],[1,"83","1","Early Childhood Education and Care Support","support for early childhood education and care for children including those aged 0 to 2",""],[1,"84","1","Early Childhood Education and Childcare Improvement","the qualitative improvement of education and childcare in early childhood and during the transition to elementary school",""]],"45":[[1,"81","3","Child Sexual Violence Prevention Enforcement Preparation","we will advance preparations for the enforcement of the Prevention of Sexual Violence against Children Act242",""],[1,"81","3","Life Safety Education Programme","promote Life Safety Education",""],[1,"81","3","Youth Internet-Related Issues Response","responses to internet-related issues among youth",""],[1,"82","1","Child and Family Center Capacity Strengthening","To prevent child abuse, we will take measures such as strengthening the capacity of Child and Family Centers(including improving staffing)",""],[1,"82","1","Child Abuse Prevention Home Visits","conducting home visits to provide support",""],[1,"82","1","Professional Certification for Child Abuse Prevention","promoting the acquisitions of professional certifications.",""],[1,"82","2","Child Sexual Violence Support System","We will establish a support system sensitive to the needs of children who have experienced sexual violence.",""],[1,"82","2","Family-Based Foster Care Support","We will provide support through foster parents and family homes based on the concept of permanency guarantee243 and the principle of giving priority to family rearing244",""],[1,"82","2","Support for Vulnerable Young Women and Care-Leavers","We will ... assist young pregnant women and those with experience in social child care.",""],[1,"82","2","Amended Civil Code Awareness Initiative","We will work to raise awareness for the smooth implementation of the amended Civil Code245",""],[1,"82","2","Foster Home and Child Guidance Capacity Strengthening","while also improving the caregiving functions of foster homes and enhancing the capacity of Child Guidance Centers.",""],[1,"82","4","Family-Based Living Environment for Children","Ensuring a stable and long-term family-based living environment for children.",""],[1,"82","4","Civil Code Partial Revision Reform","Act for Partial Revision of the Civil Code, etc. (Act No. 33 of 2024).",""]],"47":[[1,"82","2","High-Quality Public Education Revitalization","We will strongly promote the revitalization of high-quality public education.",""],[1,"9","2","Public Education Revitalization Programme","the revitalization of public education",""],[1,"10","1","Public Education Revitalization and Reform","to revitalize and reform public education.",""],[1,"82","3","Authentic and High-Quality Learning Initiative","we will pursue more authentic and high-quality learning.",""],[1,"82","3","National Curriculum Standards Reform","we will revise the National Curriculum Standard to enable the development of flexible curricula that support the growth of each child's potential.",""],[1,"83","1","Public Education Revitalization and Upper Secondary Reform Support","fundamentally enhancing support by the national government for reforming upper secondary education and related areas",""],[1,"83","1","Tuition-Free Upper Secondary Education","so-called tuition-free upper secondary education",""],[1,"83","1","Free School Lunch Programme","free school lunches",""],[1,"84","1","Special Needs Education Enhancement","the government will promote the enhancement of the systems and environments for special needs education",""],[1,"84","1","Special Schools and Evening Classes Expansion","the nationwide establishment and functional enhancement of special schools for chronical absentees and evening classes at junior high schools",""],[1,"84","1","Local Japanese Language Education Systems","the development of local systems for Japanese language education",""],[1,"84","1","Foreign Student Support Systems","the strengthening of support systems for foreign students",""],[1,"84","1","School Supplies as School Property","the dissemination of the principle that school supplies should be provided as school property",""],[1,"84","1","Educational Support Center Strengthening","strengthening functions of educational support centers inside and outside schools",""],[1,"84","1","Experiential and Reading Activities","experiential activities and reading activities to nurture rich sensitivity and creativity",""],[1,"84","1","AI-Enabled English Education","English education will be promoted through the use of AI and initiatives aimed at highlighting the appeal of regional areas",""],[1,"84","1","Practical Vocational High School Models","we will promote the development of practical vocational high school models with hands-on support, including the dispatch of personnel from industry and other sectors",""],[1,"84","3","Individual Support Plan Information Sharing Mechanism","This includes sharing of information from individual support plans for coordination with the welfare sector.",""]],"48":[[1,"83","2","Teacher Workstyle Reform Programme","To attract and retain high-quality teachers, we will implement a comprehensive approach that includes further accelerating workstyle reforms, improving treatment, enhancing the instruction systems, and strengthening professional development.",""],[1,"83","2","School Operations Digital Transformation","improve operational efficiency through digital transformation (DX)",""],[1,"83","2","Education Reform Progress Monitoring Mechanism","make visible the progress of initiatives by individual boards of education, strengthen the PDCA cycle",""],[1,"83","2","Teacher Compensation and Salary Reform","We will improve the treatment of teachers through measures such as raising the additional adjustments for the teaching profession to 10 percent by FY 2030 and introducing a well-defined salary system based on responsibilities and workload.",""],[1,"83","2","Lower Secondary Class Size and Staffing Reform","Based on the revised act, we will increase the number of teaching staff to achieve 35-student classes in lower secondary schools starting in FY 2026",""],[1,"83","2","External Personnel Allocation for School Workstyle Reform","expand the allocation of external personnel to support workstyle reform",""],[1,"83","2","Teacher Training University Function Strengthening","We will also take action to strengthen the functions of teacher training universities, including through the use of regional admission quotas",""],[1,"83","2","Teacher Candidate Recruitment and Development Reform","reform systems to nurture and secure teacher candidates from the training stage onward",""],[1,"83","2","Teacher Professional Development Programme","enhance teacher development programs",""],[1,"83","2","Teacher Scholarship Repayment Support","further examine support for scholarship repayment, including at the undergraduate level",""]],"49":[[1,"85","1","Research Quality Enhancement Mechanism","Construction of a mechanism to enhance the quality of research",""],[1,"85","2","University Hospital Physician Work-Style Reform","promoting work-style reform for physicians at university hospitals",""],[1,"9","2","Research Activities Revitalization Programme","the revitalization of research activities",""],[1,"43","2","Science, Technology, and Innovation R&D Investment Programme","we will consistently promote R&D and social implementation through cross-sectional technology integration in areas such as AI, quantum, fusion energy, materials, biotechnology, semiconductors, next-generation information and communications infrastructure (Beyond 5G), and health and medical care, etc.",""],[1,"43","2","Strategic International Research Cooperation Programme","The government will promote strategic international cooperation, such as cutting-edge joint research and exchanges of researchers and students like-minded countries, including the G7, and the Global South, including ASEAN and India.",""],[1,"43","2","Overseas Cutting-Edge Research Opportunities","providing researchers based in Japan with opportunities to experience cutting-edge research overseas",""],[1,"43","2","International Researcher Attraction Programme","the government will actively attract outstanding researchers from foreign research institutes",""],[1,"43","2","International Talent Mobility and Circulation Mechanism","establish international talent mobility and circulation by taking initiatives, including emergency measures in light of recent changes in the international situation",""],[1,"43","3","World-Class Research Universities Programme","the government will advance efforts to create world-class research universities through the Universities for International Research Excellence program",""],[1,"43","3","Diverse Research Universities Development","to form a diverse and robust group of research universities",""],[1,"43","3","Research University Effectiveness Assessment","examining the effectiveness of such efforts",""],[1,"43","3","Advanced Research Facilities Development Mechanism","we will build a mechanism to promote the strategic development, share, and upgrade of advanced research facilities and equipment",""],[1,"43","3","AI for Science Research Innovation","The government will innovate scientific research through AI for Science",""],[1,"43","3","Research Data Information Infrastructure Strengthening","the strengthening of the information infrastructure that supports the utilization of research data",""],[1,"43","3","Industry-Academia-Government Cooperation Expansion","We will promote the larger scale and globalization of industry-academia-government cooperation",""],[1,"43","4","University and KOSEN Faculty Reorganization in Growth Fields","we will support reorganization of university and colleges of technology (KOSEN) faculties in growth fields",""],[1,"43","4","New Colleges of Technology Establishment","we will support ... establishment of new colleges of technology (KOSEN)",""],[1,"43","4","Advanced and Internationalized Science and Technology Human Resources Development","advancement and internationalization of human resources development111 in response to cutting-edge technologies",""],[1,"43","5","Quantum Technology Use Case and Business Model Development","For quantum technology, the government will work on creating use cases and building business models.",""],[1,"43","5","Quantum Technology Initial Demand Stimulation Study","We will also study ways to stimulate initial demand",""],[1,"43","6","Statistical Experts Development Initiative","This includes the development of statistical experts.",""],[1,"44","1","International Standardization and Base Collaboration Initiative","promote international standardization activities and collaboration among bases.",""],[1,"44","1","Fusion Energy and Materials Strategy Initiatives","With regard to fusion energy and materials, we will promote initiatives based on the new national strategies.",""],[1,"85","2","Integrated Education Research and Governance Reform","the government will promote integrated reforms of education, research, and governance",""],[1,"85","2","Evidence-Based Policymaking for Science and Technology","strengthening EBPM (evidence-based policymaking) across all science and technology policies",""],[1,"85","2","Basic Research Funding for Universities","we will secure basic funding, including operating grants and subsidies for private universities",""],[1,"85","2","Competitive Research Funding Support","we will consider appropriate forms of support",""],[1,"85","2","Advanced Large Research Facility Development","promoting the strategic development, public utilization, and upgrade of advanced large research facilities",""],[1,"85","2","Highly Skilled Research Professional Development","fostering and securing highly skilled professionals",""],[1,"85","2","Stable Research Positions for Early-Career Researchers","improving the treatment of doctoral students and young researchers by securing stable positions",""],[1,"85","2","Industry Academia Government Co-Creation Platforms","creating platforms for co-creation among industry, academia, and government",""],[1,"85","2","Next Science Technology and Innovation Basic Plan","the government will formulate the next Science, Technology, and Innovation Basic Plan within FY 2025",""],[1,"85","2","Science Technology and Innovation Plan Monitoring","monitor and evaluate its progress using indicators, and use the results to further promote science, technology, and innovation policies",""],[1,"85","3","Science Council of Japan Institutional Strengthening","We will support the Science Council of Japan in strengthening its functions under the new law257, with the aim of advancing academic excellence and contributing to the resolution of social issues.",""]],"50":[[1,"86","2","Compact Urban Development through Location Optimization Plans","We will enhance efforts based on Location Optimization Plans and promote the compact development of urban areas across broader regions, also taking into account the goal of building disaster-resilient national and regional land.",""],[1,"86","2","Strategic Management of National and Public Properties","We will promote the strategic management of national and public properties in a manner rooted in local communities, aiming to enhance area value.",""],[1,"87","1","Small Concessions for Vacant House Reuse","promote the spread of Small Concessions that utilize existing stock such as vacant houses",""],[1,"87","2","Land Use Conversion Facilitation Policy","we will work to ensure the smooth conversion of land use, including the conversion to non-residential use.",""],[1,"87","2","Vacant House Renovation and Distribution Initiative","With support for local governments, we will comprehensively and integrally promote measures to address vacant houses—aimed at enhancing disaster resilience and contributing to regional revitalization—through initiatives such as renovation and promotion of distribution.",""],[1,"87","2","Property Registration Compliance Enhancement System","including raising public awareness of and enhancing systems for complying with mandatory registration of inheritance and changes to name and address",""],[1,"87","2","Cadastral Survey and Mapping Programme","conducting cadastral surveys and preparing maps by the Legal Affairs Bureaus.",""],[1,"87","2","Public Land Appraisal Capacity Initiative","Efforts will be made to secure real estate appraisers who support public land appraisals.",""],[1,"87","2","Condominium Management and Revitalization Programme","We will work to facilitate proper management of condominiums and their revitalization.",""],[1,"87","2","Fixed-Rate Mortgage Facilitation Measures","With regard to housing loans, we will take comprehensive measures to respond to changes in the financial environment, including efforts to facilitate the use of fixed-rate mortgages.",""]],"51":[[1,"87","3","Comprehensive Watershed Water Management","we will promote Comprehensive Watershed Water Management, whereby stakeholders collaborate in efforts such as water use for power generation and the conservation and creation of watershed environments.",""],[1,"87","1","Water PPP Hands-On Support Systems","we will promote the establishment of systems to provide hands-on support in priority areas such as water PPPs",""],[1,"87","1","PPP Examination and Deliberation Streamlining","promote streamlining of examination procedures and shortening of deliberation periods",""],[1,"87","1","Private Sector PPP Profit Environment","work to build an environment in which private companies can obtain appropriate profits through their efforts and ingenuity",""],[1,"87","1","Cross-Sectoral and Wide-Area PPP Projects","promote the creation of cross-sectoral and wide-area projects",""],[1,"87","1","Local Platform Public-Private Collaboration","strengthen public-private collaboration through the use of local platforms",""],[1,"87","3","Sound Water Cycle Maintenance and Water Resource Management","We will promote the maintenance and restoration of a sound water cycle and the effective use of water resources in river basins.",""],[1,"87","3","Healthy Water Environment Creation Initiative","We will also promote the creation of a healthy water environments from a multifaceted perspective, including biodiversity and landscape, and overall human well-being263.",""],[1,"87","4","Wastewater Treatment Facility Utilization Promotion","In parallel, based on local conditions such as population decline, we will promote the utilization of wastewater treatment facilities, including Johkasou.",""]],"52":[[1,"9","2","Strategic Social Capital Development Programme","the promotion of strategic social capital development",""],[1,"85","4","Infrastructure Deterioration Prioritization and Response","address the ongoing deterioration of infrastructure by taking into account factors such as urgency and economic and social impacts, clarifying priorities",""],[1,"86","1","Wide-Area Strategic Infrastructure Management and Preventive Maintenance","Through the implementation of wide-area and strategic infrastructure management, the use of new technologies and data, and the promotion of collaboration among operators and between the public and private sectors, we will promote a full-scale shift to preventive maintenance, enhance and streamline maintenance and management",""],[1,"86","1","Regional Infrastructure Consolidation and Public Stock Optimization","advance the consolidation and reorganization of infrastructure in line with regional future visions as well as the optimization of public stock",""],[1,"86","1","Visualization of Aging Infrastructure Countermeasure Effects","We will also work to visualize the effects of aging countermeasures.",""],[1,"86","1","Financial Resource Measures for Infrastructure Maintenance","the government will consider financial resource measures",""],[1,"86","4","Stable and Sustainable Public Investment Programme","we will promote stable and sustainable public investment from a medium- to long-term perspective",""],[1,"86","4","Appropriate Public Works Price Pass-Through Mechanism","encourage appropriate price pass-through",""],[1,"86","4","Social Capital PDCA Improvement Mechanism","steadily improve social capital through effective PDCA cycles",""],[1,"86","5","Work Vessel Equipment and Materials Procurement","This includes securing work vessels and other equipment and materials.",""],[1,"88","4","Aging Regional Infrastructure Management Initiative","ensure the proper management of aging infrastructure that supports regional communities",""]],"53":[[1,"9","2","Local Administrative and Fiscal Foundation Strengthening","the strengthening of local administrative and fiscal foundations",""]],"54":[[1,"90","1","Inspection and Evaluation of Integrated Economic and Fiscal Reforms","Inspection and evaluation of integrated economic and fiscal reforms",""],[1,"90","2","Budget Formulation and Institutional Reform Framework","we aim to realize budget formulation and institutional reforms that appropriately respond to changes in the economy, society, environment, and technology.",""],[1,"90","2","Government-Wide EBPM Monitoring and Evaluation Mechanism","The Council on Economic and Fiscal Policy will monitor, review, and evaluate the progress of reforms each year based on the EBPM Action Plan, the Reform Implementation Program, and the Table of Progress Management, Checking evaluation.",""],[1,"90","3","Government-Wide Evidence-Based Policy Making","Relevant ministries and agencies will fully advance EBPM across the government in accordance with the EBPM Action Plan.",""],[1,"90","3","Annual EBPM Plan Review and Reinforcement Mechanism","At the end of each year, we will review and reinforce the plan, and reflect the results in the Basic Policy for the following fiscal year and beyond, thereby further strengthening EBPM.",""],[1,"90","4","Inter-Ministerial Data Development and Visualization Mechanism","we will strengthen inter-ministerial collaboration in the development and visualization of data, including administrative records",""],[1,"90","4","Integrated Administrative Project Review Data Mechanism","Through closer coordination with the Administrative Project Review process, we will promote the integrated and efficient collection, analysis, and evaluation of data.",""],[1,"90","4","Administrative Project Review System Enhancement and AI Data Utilization","We will also enhance the functionality of the Administrative Project Review system and promote greater utilization of data through AI technologies.",""],[1,"90","4","Big Data Analysis and Indicator Application Initiative","We will also advance the use of big data for analysis and the practical application of relevant indicators.",""],[1,"90","5","Government Funds EBPM and PDCA Management","we will promote the use of EBPM to assess their effectiveness and strengthen PDCA-based management, with a view to utilizing financial resources more effectively.",""],[1,"90","6","Cross-Sectional Fund Checking and Review Policy","Cross-Sectional Policy for Checking and Reviewing the Fund",""],[1,"91","1","Public Sector Asset Management Improvement","we will consider ways to improve their management and make better use of them",""],[1,"93","1","Prioritized Budget Resource Allocation","We will ensure a well-prioritized and focused budget formulation by allocating necessary budgetary resources to address key policy challenges",""],[1,"93","1","EBPM and PDCA Implementation","We will promote the EBPM and PDCA initiatives",""],[1,"93","1","Wise Public Spending Implementation","thoroughly implement wise spending",""]],"55":[[1,"92","6","Comprehensive Economic Measures Implementation","To this end, the government will swiftly and steadily implement the Comprehensive Economic Measures to Foster the Safety and Security of Citizens and Sustained Growth267, the supplementary budget for FY 2024, as well as the budget for FY 2025 and related measures.",""],[1,"8","1","Tax Cut Measures","implemented tax cut measures.",""],[1,"8","2","Macroeconomic Policy Coordination Mechanism","The government will continue to closely cooperate with the Bank of Japan and flexibly manage macroeconomic policies in response to economic and price conditions.",""],[1,"8","2","Structural Reforms for Competitiveness and Growth","The government will implement structural reforms to enhance competitiveness and growth potential",""],[1,"8","2","Sustainable Fiscal Structure Measures","while advancing measures to establish a sustainable fiscal structure.",""],[1,"8","2","Price Stability Monetary Policy Management","we expect the Bank of Japan to achieve the price stability target of 2% in a sustainable and stable manner, while confirming the virtuous cycle between wages and prices, by conducting appropriate monetary policy management in light of economic activity, prices and financial conditions.",""],[1,"8","3","Regular Economic and Fiscal Policy Review Mechanism","The Council on Economic and Fiscal Policy will continue to conduct regular reviews on economic and fiscal conditions, the conduct of macroeconomic policy management, including monetary policy, and efforts in reforms toward a resilient economic structure against changes in the external environment.",""],[1,"9","1","Long-Term Fiscal Sustainability Framework","expenditures as a percentage of GDP, while maintaining a certain margin of surplus in the primary balance over the long term",""],[1,"9","2","Integrated Economic and Fiscal Reform Programme","we will promote efforts for integrated economic and fiscal reforms",""],[1,"4","11","Public Systems Review and Revision","Review and Revision of public systems in line with rising prices",""],[1,"92","4","Economic and Fiscal Response to U.S. Tariff Measures","We will make all-out efforts for our economic and fiscal management, including the response to the U.S. tariff measures",""],[1,"92","7","Monetary Policy Management for Price Stability","conducting appropriate monetary policy management in light of economic activity, prices and financial conditions",""],[1,"93","1","Long-Term Economic Fiscal and Social Security Sustainability","We will move forward with efforts to ensure the sustainability of the economy, finance, and social security from a medium- to long-term perspective",""]],"56":[[1,"47","2","Strategic Field Foreign Investment Promotion","the relevant ministries and agencies will work together to promote investment in strategic fields such as DX, GX, and life sciences",""],[1,"47","2","Foreign Investment Attraction Grant Support","recommend the initiative to support the attraction of foreign direct investment in Japan through New Regional Economy and Living Environment Creation Grant",""],[1,"47","2","Special Zone System Utilization and Review","utilize and review the special zone system",""],[1,"47","2","National Local Private Investment Attraction System","build a new system for attracting foreign direct investment in Japan through cooperation among the national government, local governments, and the private sector",""],[1,"47","2","JETRO Foreign Investment Attraction System Strengthening","strengthen JETRO’ s system for attracting Foreign Direct Investment in Japan","JETRO"],[1,"47","3","Social Problem-Solving Technology Demonstration and Dissemination","At the Expo 2025 Osaka, Kansai, Japan, the government will demonstrate and disseminate technologies that will help solve social issues.",""],[1,"47","3","Nationwide Regional Attractiveness and Rural Tourism Promotion","We will also work to disseminate the attractiveness of all regions across Japan, attract visitors to rural areas",""],[1,"47","3","International Business Matching and Foreign Investment Promotion","provide opportunities for business matching that will contribute to promote international exchanges and foreign direct investment in Japan as well",""],[1,"47","4","International Horticultural Expo 2027 Preparation","As part of the preparations, we will construct the venue, invite participants, and build momentum.",""],[1,"47","6","Priority Grant Allocation for Intellectual Property Strategy","The government will clarify that this program is one of the priority allocation projects of this grant.",""]],"88":[[1,"4","8","All-Generations Social Security System Development","Building a social security system for all generations",""],[1,"8","6","Healthcare and Long-Term Care Cost Restraint Reform","address reforms to restrain the rising trend of healthcare and long-term care",""],[1,"5","5","Economic, Fiscal, and Social Security Sustainability Reform","ensuring the sustainability of economic, fiscal, and social security systems in anticipation of a full-fledged population decline",""],[1,"9","2","All-Generations Social Security System Construction","the construction of social security systems for all generations",""]],"92":[[1,"12","4","Low Bidding Price Survey and Minimum Price Systems","the government will promote efforts for expanding the introduction and utilization of a low bidding price survey system and a minimum price limit system",""],[1,"12","4","Sliding Scale and Contract Modification Adjustment","adjusting the sliding scale system in response to price increases and the relevant contract modification during the fiscal year based on the Basic Policy on Contracts of Government Agencies, etc. for Small and Medium Enterprises",""],[1,"12","4","Public-Sector Budget Provision for Proper Transactions","securing the necessary budgets for the national government, independent administrative agencies, etc. and local governments",""],[1,"12","4","Enforcement of Proper Transactions Act","While strengthening the enforcement system for the Act on Proper Transactions with Small and Medium-Sized Entrusted Business Operators",""],[1,"12","4","Publicization of Labor Cost Price Negotiation Guidelines","we will thoroughly publicize the “Guidelines on Price Negotiations for the Appropriate Passing-Through of Labor Costs.”",""]],"94":[[1,"4","1","Digital Transformation Promotion Policy","(2) Promotion of Digital Transformation (DX)",""],[1,"4","1","Advanced Science and Technology Promotion Policy","(4) Promoting advanced science and technology",""],[1,"4","1","Startup Support Programme","(5) Support for startups",""],[1,"5","5","Innovation and Productivity Improvement Initiative","Innovation and productivity improvement in order to prevent the economic pie from shrinking even in the face of a declining population",""],[1,"7","2","Stimulating Japan’s Investment Power Initiative","the government will implement initiatives for “Stimulating Japan’s Investment Power” in which the public and private sectors cooperate in investments in such fields as GX and DX, startups, and economic security.",""],[1,"11","3","Cutting-Edge Technology Preservation and Fostering Programme","preserving and fostering cutting-edge technologies",""],[1,"3","14","Green Transformation Promotion","(1) Promotion of Green Transformation (GX)",""]],"95":[[1,"4","1","Overseas Vitality Leveraging Policy","(6) Leveraging overseas vitality",""],[1,"4","1","Leading Asset Management Center Promotion Policy","(7) Promoting Japan as a Leading Asset Management Center",""],[1,"3","14","Japan Investment Power Stimulation Initiative","Increasing future wages and income through “Stimulating Japan’s Investment Power”",""],[1,"3","14","Leading Asset Management Center Promotion","Promoting Japan as a Leading Asset Management Center",""],[1,"6","4","Japan-U.S. Tariff Consultation and Cooperation Initiative","Japan will strongly urge the U.S. to reconsider its tariff measures and will persistently continue consultations to powerfully promote the cooperative relationship for the mutual growth of Japan and the U.S..",""],[1,"6","4","Domestic Industry Tariff Impact Financing Support","the government will provide necessary support, including financing measures, on the assumption of the impacts of the tariff measures on domestic industries and the economy.",""],[1,"6","4","Domestic Investment Expansion Initiative","the government will work on expanding domestic investments",""],[1,"6","4","Resilient Domestic Supply Chain Development","making supply chains more resilient",""],[1,"6","4","Foreign Direct Investment Promotion Policy","promoting foreign direct investment in Japan",""],[1,"6","4","Resilient Economic Structure and Domestic Demand Expansion","building an economic structure that is resilient to changes in the external environment, by expanding domestic demand to give an instance",""],[1,"11","3","Essential Goods Supply Chain Strengthening Initiative","strengthening the supply chains of essential goods",""],[1,"11","3","Public-Private Economic Security Collaboration Mechanism","bringing together the wisdom of the public and private sectors",""],[1,"11","3","Free and Open International Order Cooperation Policy","maintain and strengthen the free and open international order based on the rule of law in cooperation with allies and like-minded countries that share values and principles",""],[1,"11","3","Strategies for Shaping New International Order and Rules","thoroughly prepare strategies and measures to respond to and participate in the creation of new international order and rules",""],[1,"11","4","Agile Strategic Public Relations Strengthening","we will strengthen our agile and strategic public relations for both inside and outside Japan.",""]],"96":[[1,"6","5","Government Stockpiled Rice Sale","the sale of the government stockpiled rice",""],[1,"6","5","Fuel Oil Price Reduction Measure","a fixed price reduction in fuel oil prices",""],[1,"6","5","Electricity and Gas Rate Support","support for electricity and gas rates according to the situation of prices and people's lives",""]],"97":[[1,"7","4","Natural Disaster Recovery and Reconstruction","We will work on the recovery and reconstruction from natural disasters such as the Great East Japan Earthquake and the 2024 Noto Peninsula Earthquake",""],[1,"7","4","National Disaster Management","disaster management",""],[1,"7","4","Disaster Mitigation Measures","mitigation",""],[1,"7","4","National Resilience Building","building national resilience",""],[1,"7","4","Diplomatic and Security Environment Response","responding to changes in the diplomatic and security environment",""],[1,"7","4","Crime Countermeasures","strengthening crime countermeasures",""]],"98":[[1,"17","3","Business Information-Sharing Mechanism for Financial Institutions","The government will consider a mechanism to encourage business operators to provide information to regional financial institutions and Credit Guarantee Corporations(CGC) on a regular basis.",""],[1,"17","3","IT Adoption for Predictive Financial Management","Concurrently, we will promote IT adoption by regional financial institutions and CGC to strengthen predictive management.",""],[1,"17","3","Enterprise Revitalization Support Roll-Up","Through the support by government-affiliated financial institutions, the Organization for Small & Medium Enterprises and Regional Innovation or the SME Vitalization Support Centers, the government will promote the roll-up25 of enterprises in need of revitalization support.",""],[1,"17","3","Business Owner Debt Guarantee System Utilization Review","We will follow up on the utilization of the Business Operators’ Choice-Based No Provision of Debt Guarantees by Business Owners System,27 aiming to establish lending practices that do not rely on debt guarantees by business owners.",""],[1,"17","3","Revitalization and Re-Challenging Support Initiatives","The government will promote initiatives based on the Revitalization and Re-Challenging Support Facilitation Package.28",""],[1,"17","4","Regional Priority Enterprise Support System","The government will select priority support enterprises that will have a large ripple effect on local economies, and develop a proper support system for each region.",""],[1,"17","4","Leading Medium Enterprise R&D and Investment Support","We will support R&D and large-scale capital investment by leading medium enterprises (LMEs).",""],[1,"17","4","Enterprise Investment Financing Support Mechanism","In addition, their financing environment will be improved through investment from funds and other sources.",""],[1,"17","4","Overseas Expansion Human Resources Initiative","The government will encourage LMEs and SMEs to accept high-level human resources that can take on roles for overseas expansion.",""],[1,"17","4","Family Business Governance Strengthening","Family-run businesses will be encouraged to strengthen their governance.",""],[1,"17","4","Capital Investment Support for High-Growth Enterprises","The government will support capital investment by enterprises that have declared that they aim to achieve sales of more than 10 billion yen.",""],[1,"17","4","SME Business Transformation and Innovation Support","The government will support SMEs and Small Business in entering new businesses, transforming their business structures, engaging in R&D, and developing new products and services.",""],[1,"17","5","Local-Zebra Company Development Initiative","the government will promote the development of local-zebra companies that will take on roles for solving regional social issues",""],[1,"17","6","Continuous M&A Consolidation and Integration","Consolidation and integration through continuous M&As.",""],[1,"17","6","Financial Support and Debt Reduction for Struggling Businesses","Business segments in need of financial support (condition changes, debt reduction, etc.) because, for example, their financial position is deteriorating or is likely to deteriorate in the future and they have problems with future business continuity.",""],[1,"17","6","SME Credit Guarantee Without Personal Debt Guarantees","A system under which SMEs that meet certain requirements for loans with a credit guarantee can choose not to provide a debt guarantee by their respective business owners on the condition that the guarantee fee rate should be additionally raised.","Ministry of Economy, Trade and Industry | Financial Services Agency | Ministry of Finance"],[1,"18","2","SME Management Support Systems Strengthening","The government will strengthen the systems and functions to support the management of SMEs and Small Businesses, including their human resource management.",""],[1,"18","2","SEKAMACHI SME Support Matching Platform Enhancement","We will enhance the functions of the SEKAMACHI platform for matching SMEs with support institutions, which aggregates the information and support needs of enterprises.",""],[1,"18","2","Small Enterprise Management Capability Support","The government will provide support through Society of Commerce and Industry, and Chambers of Commerce and Industry to improve the management capabilities of small enterprises based on the Basic Plan for Small Enterprise Promotion.",""],[1,"18","2","Regional Industrial Property Information and Training Expansion","We will work on expanding the activities of the National Center for Industrial Property Information and Training to regional areas.",""],[1,"18","6","Mutual Assistance Businesses for Local Service Provision","new mutual assistance-type business entities, mainly consisting of cooperatives, and resident-funded companies, work on maintaining and developing the supply of such services by improving productivity through labor-saving, digitalization, coalition, etc.",""],[1,"18","6","SME Human Resources Utilization Support","Support for business owners and executives to secure, retain, and utilize human resources based on the Guidelines on Human Resources Utilization for SMEs and Small Businesses",""]],"99":[[1,"23","1","Service Function Consolidation Bases","promoting the formation of the consolidation bases of various service functions",""],[1,"23","1","National Land Connectivity Strengthening","strengthening the connection of all national land",""],[1,"23","2","Urban Revitalization and Sustainable Area Management","the public and the private sectors will collaborate to strengthen urban revitalization and international competitiveness that will also create public value, develop unique communities utilizing regional resources, and promote sustainable area management.",""],[1,"23","2","Community Development Green Transformation Initiatives","The government will promote community development GX initiatives",""],[1,"23","2","Nature-Positive Local Activities","local activities for the realization of nature positivity",""],[1,"23","2","Green Infrastructure Utilization","the utilization of green infrastructure",""],[1,"23","2","Traffic Vacuum Elimination Policy","we will work to eliminate the traffic vacuum during the intensive measures period until fiscal 2027, under comprehensive national support, which will be greater than in previous years.",""],[1,"23","2","Regional Transportation Redesign and Automation","The government will fully implement the redesigning of regional transportation by promoting labor-saving measures, securing key personnel, as well as spreading and expanding automated driving.",""],[1,"23","3","Local and Trunk Railway Network Improvement","Further efforts will be made to reconstruct local railways, deepen discussions on the ideal railway network, and make trunk railways more functional in accordance with local circumstances.",""],[1,"23","3","Municipality-Centered Local Shopping and Last-Mile Logistics System","the government will promote the establishment of a system centered on municipalities, the development of base facilities, the introduction of mobile sales vehicles, the joint sharing of deliveries, and the securing of last-mile logistics through the use of new technologies.",""],[1,"23","4","Logistics and People-Flow Network Development","the government will work on the early development and utilization of logistics and people-flow networks, such as high-standard roads, new shinkansen lines",""],[1,"23","5","People-Centered Town Street Development","This includes the promotion of the development of people-centered town streets that make people feel comfortable and want to walk on.",""],[1,"23","5","Park Utilization Initiative","In addition, we will work on the use of parks",""],[1,"23","5","Traffic Congestion Reduction Measures","measures to address traffic congestion",""],[1,"23","5","School Route Traffic Safety Measures","traffic safety measures for school routes",""],[1,"23","5","Bicycle Use Promotion","promotion of the use of bicycles",""],[1,"23","5","Post Office Service Consolidation","use of post offices as a base for consolidating various services",""],[1,"23","5","Natural Capital Data Preparation and Dissemination","This includes the preparation of data on natural capital, etc., the dissemination of such information",""],[1,"23","5","International Biodiversity Rule Formation Initiative","the initiative to form international rules",""],[1,"23","5","Transport Infrastructure Development Studies","Currently, necessary studies are being carried out",""],[1,"23","5","Early Development of Unstarted Construction Sections","we will further work on the early development of the sections where construction has not yet started",""],[1,"24","1","Transport Infrastructure and Network Strengthening Initiative","railways, ports and airports, the strengthening of modal connections, and the maintenance and activation of aviation networks,39 as well as the securing and nurturing of personnel in charge.",""],[1,"24","2","Maritime Supply Chain Strengthening Initiative","significantly strengthening maritime supply chains, including Japan-U.S. cooperation",""],[1,"24","2","Zero-Emission Ship Introduction Programme","promoting the introduction of zero-emission ships etc. by utilizing GX Economy Transition Bonds etc.",""],[1,"24","2","Japanese-Flagged Ship Ownership Cost Reduction Measure","strengthening the competitiveness of Japanese ship owners by reducing the cost of owning Japanese-flagged ships",""],[1,"24","2","Commercial Autonomous Ship Development Initiative","realizing commercial autonomous ships",""],[1,"24","2","Coastal and Passenger Shipping Transport Stabilization","stable transportation by coastal shipping and passenger ships",""],[1,"24","2","Shipbuilding Human Resources Development Programme","securing shipbuilding human resources by utilizing grants for creating New Regional Economy and Living Environment Creation Grant",""],[1,"24","3","Trunk Railway Function Enhancement Studies","we will conduct studies on the enhancement of trunk railway functions that will contribute to the realization of Regional Revitalization 2.0",""],[1,"24","3","Linear Chuo Shinkansen Financial Investment and Loan Support","based on financial investment and loan program support",""],[1,"24","3","Linear Chuo Shinkansen Environmental Monitoring and Technical Support","the government will strictly monitor the status, etc. of the environment and water resources, provide necessary guidance and technical support",""],[1,"24","3","Local Government Coordination for Linear Chuo Shinkansen Opening","work with local governments along the line to develop the environment for the opening of the entire line under the current assumed timing",""],[1,"24","4","Logistics Bases and Networks Enhancement","the government will promote functional enhancement of logistics bases and networks",""],[1,"24","4","Multimodal Freight Transport Shift","a new modal shift among land, sea, and air",""],[1,"24","4","Automated Driving Promotion","automated driving",""],[1,"24","4","Logistics Digital Transformation and Standardization","logistics DX and its standardization",""],[1,"24","4","Logistics Business Practice Reform","review of business practices such as correction of multi-transaction structures",""],[1,"24","4","Shipper and Consumer Behavior Change","change in the behavior of shippers and consumers",""],[1,"24","4","Revised Logistics Act Enforcement System","the securing of an enforcement system for the revised Logistics Act",""],[1,"24","4","Foreign Human Resources Utilization for Logistics","we will promote the further utilization of foreign human resources in order to strengthen measures to address the shortage of key personnel in the logistics and passenger",""],[1,"24","5","Infrastructure Completion and Opening Procedures","procedures and others will be devised, aiming for completion and opening as soon as possible.",""],[1,"24","5","Local Government Consultation on Opening Delays","responses to the impact of the delay in opening will be carefully addressed through hearing from local governments along the line, etc.",""],[1,"24","5","Domestic Airline Business Structural Reform","The Advisory Council on Domestic Aviation will consider measures for the structural reform of the domestic airline business.",""]],"100":[[1,"25","5","Nationwide Optical Fiber and 5G Deployment","the government will deploy optical fibers and 5G across the nation",""],[1,"25","5","Data Center Attraction Initiative","the attraction of data centers in areas that are desirable from the viewpoint",""],[1,"26","1","Electricity and Telecommunications Infrastructure Development","We will also develop the electricity and telecommunications infrastructure in a consistent and systematic manner",""],[1,"26","1","Data Center Decentralization Initiative","promote the decentralization of data centers",""],[1,"26","2","Special Zone and Business Environment Improvement Policy","the government will consider improving the business environment, including utilizing and reviewing the special zone system.",""],[1,"26","3","Local Industrial Infrastructure Development Support","supporting the development of industrial infrastructure by local governments",""],[1,"26","3","Industrial Site Regulatory Reform","the government will consider revising the related laws and regulations to promote the systematic development of industrial sites.",""]],"101":[[1,"26","5","Regional Migration Promotion Initiative","the government will strengthen efforts to encourage young people and others to migrate to regional areas",""],[1,"26","5","Regional Enterprise Relocation and Base Enhancement","promote the relocation of enterprises to regional areas and the enhancement of their bases through the improvement and maintenance of the relevant environments, including the use of the tax system",""],[1,"26","5","Community-Based Enterprise Development","promote the establishment of community-based enterprises through industry-government-academia-financial-labor-media-profession cooperation",""],[1,"26","5","Local Human Resources Mobilization Initiative","encourage the efforts by Local Vitalization Cooperators45 to secure local human resources",""],[1,"26","5","Hometown Resident Registration System","promote the establishment of a hometown resident registration system",""],[1,"26","5","Second Hometown Development Initiative","the formation of a second hometown",""],[1,"26","5","Workation and Regional Exchange Infrastructure Promotion","the advancement of workation and the improvement of the relevant exchange and basic facilities",""],[1,"26","5","Regional Matching Support Mechanism","the matching support through intermediate support organizations",""],[1,"26","6","Okinawa and Hokkaido Regional Development Programme","the government will promote the development of Okinawa and Hokkaido",""],[1,"26","6","Disadvantaged Areas Development Measures","take measures to address disadvantaged areas, such as depopulated areas, peninsulas, remote islands, Amami, Ogasawara, and areas with heavy snowfall, etc.",""],[1,"26","6","Okinawa Tourism Quality Improvement Programme","improving the quality of tourism",""],[1,"26","6","Okinawa Industry-Academia Cooperation Programme","promoting industries such as the industry-academia cooperation by the Okinawa Institute of Science and Technology Graduate University",""],[1,"26","6","Advance Acquisition of U.S. Military Base Site","acquiring the site of the U.S.military base in advance",""],[1,"26","7","Community Revitalization and Development Cooperative Mechanism","This includes the use of community revitalization entrepreneurs and specific community development project cooperatives.",""],[1,"27","1","GW2050 Northern and Remote Islands Development Projects","46 developing the northern part of the prefecture and remote islands, working on measures against child poverty and working to realize their well-being.",""],[1,"27","1","Hokkaido Production Space Development Initiative","the government will promote initiatives of maintaining and developing production spaces that support food, tourism, and Zero-Carbon Hokkaido",""],[1,"27","1","Digital Industries Integration Initiative","promoting the integration of digital industries",""],[1,"27","1","Northern Territories Neighboring Region Integrated Development","promoting the development of the Region neighboring the Northern Territories further in an integrated manner with the region",""],[1,"27","1","Public-Private Co-Creation Initiative","promoting the public and private sectors’ co-creation initiatives",""],[1,"27","1","Upopoy National Ainu Museum and Park Enhancement","enhancing Upopoy National Ainu Museum and Park",""],[1,"27","6","Naha Airport and Future Base Site Integrated Use Projects","The PROJECTS are aimed at the integrated use of Naha Airport and the site of the future return of the base by Okinawa's business community and local governments.",""]],"102":[[1,"27","3","Agricultural Farmland Parcel Consolidation and Expansion","the action toward consolidation and expansion of farmland parcels",""],[1,"27","3","Shared-Use Facility Reorganization and Consolidation","the reorganization and consolidation of facilities for shared use",""],[1,"27","3","Agricultural Smart Technology Development","the development of smart technologies",""],[1,"27","3","Agricultural Production Method Conversion Programme","the conversion and implementation of production methods",""],[1,"27","3","Agricultural Export Production Area Development","the development of export production areas",""],[1,"27","3","Dedicated Agile Agricultural Transformation Budget Framework","the government will secure necessary and sufficient budgets in a separate framework in an agile and flexible manner",""],[1,"27","3","Local Agricultural Transformation Implementation Systems","we will secure necessary systems to promote the relevant measures, including those in local areas",""],[1,"27","4","Stockpiled Rice Distribution Facilitation","the facilitation of the distribution of rice, especially its stockpiled rice",""],[1,"27","4","Rice Market Stakeholder Information Provision","providing detailed information to consumers, producers, distributors, and other stakeholders",""],[1,"28","1","Paddy Field Policy Review","the government will promote a review of paddy field policies in a concrete manner",""],[1,"28","1","Rice Market and Rice Flour Demand Expansion","expand demand for rice for developing new markets and rice for rice flour",""],[1,"28","1","Crop Productivity and Sustainable Farming Programme","improve productivity of wheat, soybeans, and domestic feed, promote organic farming and reduction of chemical pesticides and fertilizers",""],[1,"28","1","Farmland Consolidation Support System","review and strengthen the existing systems to support farmland consolidation based on regional plans",""],[1,"28","1","Agricultural Land Improvement Projects","promoting land improvement projects",""],[1,"28","1","New Farmer and Corporate Agricultural Entry Support","supporting new farmers and corporate entry, including support for agricultural, forestry and fisheries high schools",""],[1,"28","1","Agricultural Management Stabilization Measures","implementing management stabilization measures",""],[1,"28","1","Agricultural Technology and Service Enterprise Support","introducing high-yielding varieties, improving the information and communications environment, fostering start-ups and service entities",""],[1,"28","1","Animal and Plant Quarantine Strengthening","strengthening animal and plant quarantine",""],[1,"28","1","Agricultural Export and Overseas Expansion Initiative","we aim to achieve the export target of five trillion yen, as well as create a virtuous cycle of exports, overseas expansion and inbound tourism",""],[1,"28","1","Sustainable Food System Development","the government will promote rational pricing of food, such as rice and vegetables, sustainable development of the food industry, ensuring food access",""],[1,"28","1","MIDORI Strategy for Sustainable Food Systems","accelerating the MIDORI Strategy for Sustainable Food Systems",""],[1,"28","1","Food-System GX and Net-Zero Technology Deployment","leveraging the private sector’s vitality to promote GX, and promoting the deployment of Initiative for Net-zero compatible with Food security through INternational expansion of Innovative TechnologY (MIDORI ∞INFINITY) overseas",""],[1,"28","1","Food and Nutrition Education Programme","the government will promote Shokuiku(Food and Nutrition Education)for adults and expand opportunities to experience agriculture, forestry and fisheries",""],[1,"28","1","Hilly and Mountainous Area Infrastructure Support","the government will support infrastructure development and the introduction of machinery that suit the actual conditions, measures to prevent wildlife damage, and the maintenance of local communities",""],[1,"28","1","Countryside Stay and Rural Tourism Programme","We will promote the incorporation of inbound tourism demand into countryside stays and other initiatives in SATOGYO, MORIGYO, and UMIGYO",""]],"103":[[1,"29","3","Public-Private Partnership Investment Expansion","The government will expand public-private partnership investment to an internationally comparable level",""],[1,"29","3","Specialized Content Creation Human Resources Development","The government will accelerate the development of highly specialized human resources and core specialized human resources in the field of content creation as well as overseas expansion through cooperation among ministries and agencies, and promote the development of a proper environment to secure human resources.",""],[1,"29","3","National Center for Media Arts Development","The government will promote the development of bases that function as the National Center for Media Arts (tentative name) in cooperation with the industrial circle",""],[1,"29","3","National Art Museums Function Strengthening","reorganizing and strengthening the functions of the national art museums as a whole",""],[1,"29","3","National Theatre Opening","The government will take responsibility for the urgent opening of the National Theatre.",""],[1,"29","3","National Cultural Facilities Strengthening","we will strengthen the functions of national cultural facilities, including the global expansion of the New National Theatre",""],[1,"29","3","Artists’ Creative Environment Support","strengthen the foundation for artists' activities and the development of a dignified creative environment",""],[1,"29","3","Performing Arts and Japanese Film Promotion","promote the performing arts and Japanese films, including the utilization and cooperation of theaters and music halls across Japan to address the shortage of theaters in the Tokyo metropolitan area",""],[1,"29","3","Art Market Revitalization","revitalize the art market",""],[1,"29","3","Cultural Heritage Preservation and Value Enhancement","understanding, preserving, repairing, and increasing the added value of the NEXT Japan Cultural Expo (tentative name) and sustainable cultural properties",""],[1,"29","3","Cultural Tourism and Japan Heritage Promotion","promoting cultural tourism through the revitalization of Japan Heritage",""],[1,"29","3","Traditional Culture Promotion","encouraging traditional events, traditional performing arts, and lifestyle culture such as food culture",""],[1,"29","3","Regional Cultural Facilities Strengthening","strengthening the functions of regional cultural facilities such as museums and art galleries",""],[1,"29","3","Inclusive Access to Culture and Arts","We will enhance opportunities for children and persons with disabilities to view and experience culture and arts",""],[1,"29","3","Dialect Preservation and Inheritance","promote the preservation and inheritance of dialects",""],[1,"29","3","Bookstore Revitalization Plan","promote the Bookstore Revitalization Plan",""],[1,"29","3","Cultural Digital Archives Creation","create digital archives",""],[1,"29","4","Cultural Property Repair Workforce Support Programme","the promotion of securing human resources, including raising the wages of repair technicians based on the Artisans Projects for Cultural Properties",""],[1,"29","4","National Cultural Properties Repair Center Development","the development of the National Cultural Properties Repair Center",""],[1,"29","4","Takamatsuzuka Tomb Mural Preservation Facility Improvement","the promotion of improvement of the Takamatsuzuka Tomb Mural Painting Preservation and Management Publicity Utilization Facility (tentative name)",""],[1,"29","4","Museum of the Imperial Collections Full Opening","the full opening of the Museum of the Imperial Collections, Sannomaru Shozokan",""],[1,"29","4","Cultural Property Publication and Local Exhibition Programme","the publication and utilization of cultural properties, such as local exhibitions of some of the collections",""],[1,"30","1","Kitanomaru Park Science, Culture and Arts Hub Enhancement","we will improve its appeal as a hub for the transmission of cutting-edge science and technology, culture and arts.",""],[1,"30","1","Showa 100-Related Measures","promoting the Showa 100-related measures",""],[1,"30","1","National Archives Institutional Strengthening and Systems Improvement","the government will strengthen the functions of the National Archives of Japan and improve its systems in preparation for the opening of its new building.",""],[1,"30","2","Martial Arts and Sports Tourism Promotion","the promotion of martial arts”BUDO”/sports tourism",""],[1,"30","2","Sports Complexes and Hospitality Development","sports complexes and hospitality",""],[1,"30","2","Sports Digital Transformation and E-Sports Promotion","the promotion of DX including the utilization of e-sports",""],[1,"30","2","International Expansion of Sports Businesses","overseas expansion",""],[1,"30","2","Cross-Industry Sports Business Creation","business creation through cooperation with other industries",""],[1,"30","2","Regional Sports Commission Business Development","multilateral business development of regional sports commissions",""],[1,"30","2","Sports-Based Life Performance Improvement","We will work to improve life performance through sports",""],[1,"30","2","Para Sports Promotion","promote Para Sports",""],[1,"30","2","International Sports Event Hosting Support","We will support various aspects of event hosting and improve international competitiveness",""]],"104":[[1,"30","3","Domestic Investment Acceleration Initiative","the public and private sectors will work together to accelerate domestic investment toward the realization of the targets of 135 trillion yen in fiscal 2030 and 200 trillion yen in fiscal 2040",""],[1,"30","3","Household Savings Investment Mobilization Mechanism","we aim to transform household cash and deposits into investments and create a flow of funds that will increase wages and financial income and assets",""],[1,"30","4","Green Transformation Promotion Initiative","the public and private sectors will collaborate to promote GX-related",""],[1,"31","1","GX and Climate Investment Programme","investments of more than 150 trillion yen over 10 years based on sector-specific investment strategies in accordance with the GX 2040 Vision, the Strategic Energy Plan, and the Plan for Global Warming Countermeasures.",""],[1,"32","6","GX Investment Incentive Financing Mechanism","The concept of accelerating GX investment by providing incentives for upfront investments through the use of GX Economy Transition Bonds and carbon pricing.",""],[1,"33","1","GX Economy Transition Bond Issuance","government will utilize GX Economy Transition Bonds through the steady issuance of labeled bonds",""],[1,"33","1","GX System Full Operation","fully operate the system",""],[1,"33","1","GX League Review","review the GX League",""],[1,"33","1","GX Information Dissemination Strengthening","strengthen information dissemination by the GX Acceleration Agency",""],[1,"33","1","ESG and Transition Finance Promotion","We will promote ESG finance, including transition finance.",""],[1,"32","5","Pro-Growth Carbon Pricing Scheme","Toward the realization of the Pro-Growth Carbon Pricing Scheme",""],[1,"33","5","Labeled Green and Sustainable Bond Issuance","To be issued not only as financial instruments identical to existing government bonds (construction bonds, etc.), but also as labeled bonds.",""],[1,"33","3","GHG Emissions Visualization Rules Development","the government will promote the development of rules through visualization of GHG75 emissions",""],[1,"33","3","Transition Finance Promotion","promotion of transition finance",""],[1,"33","3","Joint Crediting Mechanism Expansion","expansion of the JCM",""],[1,"33","3","Asia Zero Emission Center Support","We will also advance our support through the Asia Zero Emission Center and other international organizations",""],[1,"33","3","International Technology and Systems Cooperation","proceed with international cooperation by utilizing Japan’s technologies and systems",""]],"105":[[1,"34","1","Ocean Policy Command Function Strengthening","Headquarters for Ocean Policy and the National Ocean Policy Secretariat will drastically strengthen their command functions",""],[1,"34","1","Marine Resource Technology Development and Verification","will work to develop and verify technologies for methane hydrate, manganese nodules, and rare earth mud, etc. to support social implementation and industrialization.",""]],"106":[[1,"35","2","Artificial Intelligence Research and Utilization Policy","Based on the AI Act,84 the government will promote the R&D and utilization of AI while both promoting innovation and mitigating risks.",""],[1,"35","2","Artificial Intelligence Human Resources Development","We will also develop and secure human resources.",""],[1,"35","2","High-Quality Data and Artificial Intelligence Research Capacity Strengthening","The government will promote the improvement of high-quality data, the strengthening and utilization of R&D capabilities,",""],[1,"35","2","Computing Resources and Information Infrastructure Upgrade","and the upgrading of computing resources and information and communication infrastructure.",""],[1,"35","2","Government Artificial Intelligence Infrastructure and Procurement Governance","For this purpose, we will build the AI infrastructure of the government, etc. through internal development as well as, ensure governance based on the Guideline for Procurements and Utilizations of Generative AI.85",""],[1,"35","2","Ethical and Fair Artificial Intelligence Governance","For the ethical and fair social implementation of AI, we will strengthen the perspective of ethics and diversity from the institutional design stage, and promote a system to prevent gender bias and enhance human resources development.",""],[1,"35","2","International Artificial Intelligence Policy Cooperation","The government continues to take the lead in international policymaking by increasing the number of organizations participating in the “Reporting Framework” for Hiroshima AI Process, promoting its Friends Group,",""],[1,"35","2","Artificial Intelligence Safety Assessment and Tool Development","and developing safety assessments and tools by AISI.86",""],[1,"36","2","Digital Skills Development Platform","The Information-technology Promotion Agency, Japan (IPA) will build a platform for developing digital skills in fiscal 2026.","The Information-technology Promotion Agency, Japan (IPA)"],[1,"36","2","Information Technology Engineer Examination Reform","The government will review the information technology engineer examination system with a view to taking into account the use of AI and modernizing the system",""],[1,"36","2","Young Digital Top-Talent Development Programme","will foster young top-talent.",""],[1,"36","2","Local Digital Skills Education Support","the government will encourage the education of digital skills eligible for receiving New Regional Economy and Living Environment Creation Grant,88",""],[1,"36","2","Local Government Digital Skills Grant Utilization","will encourage local governments to utilize this grant.",""]],"107":[[1,"35","3","Next-Generation Semiconductor Mass Production Investment","The government will invest in mass production of next-generation semiconductors among other things.",""],[1,"35","3","Semiconductor Capital Investment Support","The government will support capital investment",""],[1,"35","3","Semiconductor Supply Chain Infrastructure Development","strengthen supply chains through infrastructure development",""],[1,"35","3","Advanced Semiconductor Design and Development Support","support design and development",""],[1,"35","3","Highly Skilled Semiconductor Workforce Development","foster highly skilled human resources",""],[1,"35","3","Domestic Advanced Semiconductor and Sovereign AI Ecosystem","Japan will build a domestic ecosystem that extends from the design and manufacturing of advanced semiconductors, the assembly and operation of servers, through the development and use of sovereign AI.",""],[1,"35","3","AI-Enabled Robot Competitiveness Expansion Strategy","By the end of fiscal 2025, the government will formulate a strategy for expanding the implementation and strengthening competitiveness of robots to which AI and advanced semiconductors will be implemented.",""],[1,"35","4","Regional Semiconductor Supply Chain SME Support Initiative","A regional consortium, in which semiconductor-related companies, the National Institute of Advanced Industrial Science and Technology (AIST), and universities, etc., are participating, will promote the entry of SMEs into the semiconductor supply chain through ongoing support by corporate human resources, etc., while also taking into account the future market and technological trends.",""],[1,"36","1","Industrial Property Rights System Development","the government will consider developing an industrial property rights system with a view to promoting DX and spreading AI.",""]],"108":[[1,"40","2","Autoflow Road Technology Verification Programme","Regarding Autoflow Road, which will contribute to the resolution of the logistics crisis, the government will conduct early experiments for technological verification, with the aim of conducting experiments on the under-construction sections of the Shin-Tomei Expressway by fiscal 2027 and starting the operation on the first section by the mid-2030s.",""],[1,"40","2","Autoflow Road Operational Institutional Arrangements","We will make necessary institutional arrangements for the operation.",""],[1,"40","2","Logistics Facility Automation Programme","The government will promote the automation in logistics facilities.",""],[1,"40","2","Port Digital Transformation Programme","We will promote DX for ports through AI terminals100 and Cyber Port.101",""],[1,"40","2","Autonomous Ships Operation Programme","The government also aims to achieve the operation of autonomous ships by around 2030.",""],[1,"40","4","AI-Enabled Automated Container Terminal Initiative","This initiative aims to realize container terminals that ensure both the productivity and the proper working environment, including through the introduction of cargo-handling machines that combine AI, IoT, and automation technologies.",""],[1,"40","4","Port Procedures Digitalization Data Platform","A data platform to digitalize related procedures for improving overall port productivity and enhancing support during a disaster.",""]],"109":[[1,"41","1","Tourism Data and Generative AI Utilization Initiative","The government will advance the use of reservation, settlement data and generative AI, etc. in tourist destinations and the tourism industry.",""],[1,"41","1","Airport Operations Digital Transformation","The government will work towards rigorous and smooth immigration control by taking the initiatives toward the advancement of DX in airport operations, including the streamlining of passenger procedures using new technologies such as facial recognition",""],[1,"41","1","Japan Electronic Travel Authorization Introduction","the early introduction of the Japan Electronic System for Travel Authorization (JESTA)",""],[1,"41","1","JESTA Fee Financing Mechanism for Foreign Nationals Policies","We will advance discussions about the relevant issues, such as the utilization of the fees to be collected from foreign nationals to use JESTA, as a financial resource for policies for foreign nationals",""],[1,"41","2","Judicial and Legal Administration Digitalization","the government will advance the digitalization of civil and criminal procedures, etc. in the judicial field.",""],[1,"41","3","Central Bank Digital Currency Institutional Design and Issuance Examination","The government and the Bank of Japan will further advance their consideration of Central Bank Digital Currency (CBDC), taking into account developments in other countries, based on the interim reports, 104 in order to clarify fundamental perspectives and options on key issues as a broad outline for institutional design.",""]],"110":[[1,"46","1","Infrastructure System Overseas Promotion Strategy 2030","the government drives the Infrastructure System Overseas Promotion Strategy 2030,125 which aims at 45 trillion yen orders receiving in 2030.",""],[1,"46","1","Public-Private Overseas Expansion Support Mechanism","It enhances public-private partnerships leveraged by overseas diplomatic offices, support functions of public finance bodies, and risk-response capabilities of export and investment insurance.",""],[1,"46","1","High-Level Global South Project Promotion","the government engages in high level promotion by the Prime Minister and Cabinet Members",""],[1,"46","1","Global South Project Demonstration Support","support for project demonstrations in such fields as GX, DX, health and medical care, disaster management, urban development, and the water cycle.",""],[1,"46","2","SME Export and Overseas Expansion Support","For the reconstruction of Ukraine, the government supports the on-site activities of Japanese companies.",""],[1,"46","3","Export Test Marketing Support","For businesses considering export, the government will support their test marketing.",""],[1,"46","3","Expert Support for Export-Ready Businesses","For businesses ready to export, we will provide them with the accompanied support by experts",""],[1,"46","3","Overseas E-Commerce Sales Channel Expansion","the sales channel expansion support through overseas e-commerce sites.",""],[1,"46","4","Creator Support and Content Overseas Expansion Programme","The government will promote consistent support and system development for the fostering of creators126 and the overseas expansion of content, including the use and further integration of the Creator Support Fund.",""],[1,"46","4","Content Distribution and Financial Provider Matching Support","the government will support initiatives such as matching with domestic and overseas distribution and financial service providers at the planning and development stages as well as promoting the use of advanced technology.",""],[1,"46","4","Public Communication Phonogram Remuneration Reform","We will reach an early conclusion on the introduction of the right to remuneration for communication of phonograms to the public.",""],[1,"46","4","Content Industry Statistical Data System","Statistical data on the content industry will be prepared.",""],[1,"46","5","Film and Animation Trading Environment Survey","the Japan Fair Trade Commission will conduct a fact-finding survey or surveys in the film and animation fields with the aim of publishing the results in autumn 2025","Japan Fair Trade Commission"],[1,"46","5","Content Industry Fair Trading Guidelines","Based on the results, the government will formulate guidelines.",""],[1,"46","5","Dissemination of Content Industry Compliance Efforts","These efforts will be disseminated.",""],[1,"47","1","Content Regional Revitalization Bases and Community Efforts","the government will select Content Regional Revitalization Bases and accelerate community-wide efforts, such as animation tourism and location incentives.",""],[1,"47","1","Long-Production Works and Overseas Producer Attraction","The government will encourage the production of works that take a long time and the invitation to overseas producers, etc. for shooting on location.",""],[1,"47","1","Expedited Location-Shooting Permission Procedures","We will also facilitate and expedite procedures for permission to shoot on location.",""]],"111":[[1,"50","3","Disaster Management Infrastructure Development","the government must develop and manage disaster management infrastructure that protects the lives and property of our citizens",""],[1,"50","3","River Basin Disaster Resilience and Sustainability","accelerating and deepening River Basin Disaster Resilience and Sustainability by All based on the anticipated impacts of future climate change",""],[1,"50","3","Embankment Safety Improvement","improving the safety of embankments",""],[1,"50","3","Public-Private Port Protection Collaboration","strengthening public-private collaboration for protecting ports",""],[1,"50","3","Disaster Meteorological Forecasting Enhancement","enhancing disaster meteorological information by improving the forecasting accuracy of linear precipitation zones, typhoons, floods, landslides, and storm surges through the use of next-generation geostationary satellites",""],[1,"50","3","Forest Management and Conservation","promoting forest management and conservation",""],[1,"50","3","Phase-Free Lifeline Infrastructure Approach","introducing phase-free approaches",""],[1,"50","3","Water and Sewer System Upgrades","accelerating upgrades for infrastructure such as aging and earthquake-prone water and sewer systems",""],[1,"50","3","High-Standard Highway Network Completion","completing missing sections of high-standard highways",""],[1,"50","3","Disaster-Resilient Transportation Networks","building disaster-resilient transportation networks by developing ports and airports as disaster response hubs",""],[1,"50","3","Utility Pole Removal","promoting the removal of utility poles",""],[1,"50","3","Heavy Snow Disaster Measures","strengthening measures against heavy snow",""],[1,"50","3","Post-Disaster Road Clearance Planning","improve the effectiveness of Plans for Road Clearance after Disasters",""],[1,"50","3","National Disaster Response Capability Expansion","expanding and strengthening national disaster response capabilities, including the Technical Emergency Control Force (TEC-FORCE) and other related functions",""],[1,"50","3","Digital Transformation in Firefighting and Disaster Management","advancing digital transformation in firefighting and disaster management",""],[1,"50","4","Coastal Erosion Countermeasures","Includes coastal erosion countermeasures",""],[1,"50","4","Reservoir Disaster Management and Mitigation Measures","disaster management and mitigation measures related to reservoirs",""],[1,"50","4","Green Infrastructure Promotion","the promotion of green infrastructure",""],[1,"51","1","Supply Chain Disaster Resilience Programme","enhancing the resilience of supply chains",""],[1,"51","1","Disaster Risk Reduction and Land-Use Planning Integration","promoting disaster risk reduction measures integrated with land use planning",""],[1,"51","1","Disaster Waste Management System Improvement","improving disaster waste management systems, including necessary institutional arrangement",""],[1,"51","1","Local Disaster Risk Information Organization","organizing disaster risk information",""],[1,"51","1","Accessible Weather and Disaster Information Provision","providing clear and accessible weather and disaster related information",""],[1,"51","1","Disaster-Resilient Evacuation Shelter Enhancement","enhancing the disaster resilience of evacuation shelters, including schools",""],[1,"51","1","Renewable Energy and Battery Installation at Shelters","installing renewable energy systems and storage batteries at such facilities",""],[1,"51","1","Local Cultural Asset Disaster Protection Measures","implementing protective measures to safeguard valuable local cultural assets",""]],"112":[[1,"51","3","Earthquake Recovery and Reconstruction Programme","recovery and reconstruction from the Noto Peninsula Earthquake, etc.",""],[1,"51","4","Post-Earthquake Recovery Financing Mechanism","To promote stronger and more effective recovery measures than in the previous five years, we will secure the necessary financial resources.",""],[1,"51","5","Mental Health Care Support for Disaster-Affected Areas","the government will respond to medium- and long-term issues, such as mental health care by utilizing government-wide policies.",""],[1,"51","5","Nuclear Disaster Area Reconstruction and Revitalization","The national government will play a leading role in the reconstruction and revitalization of areas affected by the nuclear disaster.",""],[1,"52","2","Victims' Daily Lives and Livelihoods Restoration","the swift restoration of the victims' daily lives and livelihoods",""],[1,"52","2","Earthquake-Affected Infrastructure Recovery","recovery of infrastructure",""],[1,"52","2","Publicly Funded Demolition of Damaged Buildings","demolition of damaged buildings funded by public expenditure",""],[1,"52","2","Community-Based Recovery and Reconstruction Projects","the implementation of projects based on community-based recovery and reconstruction plans",""],[1,"52","2","Public Housing Development","the development of public housing",""],[1,"53","1","Noto Creative Reconstruction Support Programme","we will support the creative reconstruction of the Noto region, including efforts in areas of culture and the arts.",""],[1,"53","1","Noto Tourism Demand Stimulation Measures","To revitalize tourism in Noto, we will take various demand-stimulating measures in accordance with the reconstruction situation.",""],[1,"53","2","Multi-Hazard Earthquake Disaster Management Measures","The government will advance disaster management measures a Nankai Trough earthquake based on the revised damage projections, a Tokyo inland earthquake, subduction-zone earthquakes along the Japan Trench and Chishima Trench, and a possible eruption of Mount Fuji.",""],[1,"53","2","Volcanic Disaster Management Measures","we will promote measures against volcanic disasters",""],[1,"53","2","Volcanic Research and Analysis Programme","the research such as analysis of volcanic products at the Headquarters for Volcano Research Promotion",""],[1,"53","2","Volcanology Expert Development and Retention","the development and retention of experts in these fields",""],[1,"53","2","Crisis Management and Administrative Continuity Systems","We will also work to strengthen crisis management systems, taking into account the need to back up core administrative functions.",""],[1,"53","2","Disaster Management Industry Overseas Expansion","We will also foster the disaster management industry and promote its expansion into overseas markets.",""],[1,"53","3","Local Government Disaster Supply Stockpiling Programme","We will support local governments in stockpiling essential equipment and supplies so they can quickly provide toilets, partitions, portable beds, hot meals, and bathing facilities at the time of a disaster, in order to fundamentally improve conditions in evacuation shelters and ensure hygiene.",""],[1,"53","3","Pre-Disaster Evacuation Shelter Facility Improvements","In addition, we will advance pre-disaster measures such as the use of trailer houses, the introduction of comfortable Western-style toilets, and the installation of air conditioning in schools that serve as shelters.",""],[1,"53","3","Disaster Health and School Support Capacity Development","We will further enhance systems and develop human resources for teams engaged in health, medical, and welfare services, as well as for disaster school support teams.",""],[1,"53","4","Disaster Case Management and Victim Support","disaster case management securing personnel for victim support through collaboration with civil society organizations and private companies, including efforts to encourage participation in volunteer activities",""],[1,"53","4","Certified Victim Assistance Organization System","improving the operating environment for support activities through systems such as the Certified Organizations for Victim Assistance",""],[1,"53","4","Disaster Response Coordination Organizations","establishing and reinforcing coordinating organizations for disaster response",""],[1,"53","4","Enhanced Evacuation Measures for Persons Requiring Special Care","enhancing evacuation measures for persons requiring special care",""],[1,"53","4","Wide-Area Evacuation Facilitation","facilitating wide-area evacuations",""],[1,"53","4","Timeline-Based Disaster Preparedness","promote timeline-based disaster preparedness by encouraging the use of meteorological disaster advisors and community disaster managers",""],[1,"53","4","Regional Disaster Management Hubs","the development of disaster management hubs that contribute to regional revitalization and local economic vitality",""],[1,"53","4","Cross-Sectoral Pre-Disaster Initiatives","support for innovative and cross-sectoral pre-disaster initiatives in cooperation with relevant ministries and local governments",""],[1,"53","4","Disaster Education Programme","disaster education",""],[1,"53","4","Firefighting and Disaster Response Capacity Enhancement","enhanced firefighting and disaster response capabilities",""],[1,"53","5","Partial Revision of the Basic Act on Disaster Management","Act for Partial Revision of the Basic Act on Disaster Management (Act No. 51 of 2025).",""],[1,"54","1","Forest Fire Prevention and Firefighting Systems","In light of recent large-scale forest fires, we will strengthen preventive measures and firefighting systems.",""],[1,"54","1","Compound Disaster Emergency Response System","To prepare for compound disasters, we will improve emergency response systems, including the assessment of post-disaster site conditions, safety evaluations, and risk communication.",""],[1,"54","1","Pre-Disaster Mitigation and Community Reconstruction Planning","We will also advance pre-disaster mitigation and community-based reconstruction planning.",""],[1,"54","2","Decentralized Water and Sewer Systems Implementation","accelerating the practical implementation of decentralized water and sewer systems",""],[1,"54","2","Alternative Water Sources Development","securing alternative water sources, including the use of emergency wells and other groundwater resources",""],[1,"54","2","Subsurface Cavity Surveys Beneath Roads","conducting subsurface cavity surveys beneath road surfaces",""],[1,"54","2","Liquefaction Countermeasures","implementing liquefaction countermeasures",""],[1,"54","2","Roadside Station Hub Function Enhancement","enhancing the hub functions of roadside stations (Michi-no-Eki)",""],[1,"54","2","Communication and Broadcasting Network Resilience","reinforcing the resilience of communication and broadcasting networks",""],[1,"54","2","Industrial Complex Earthquake and Tsunami Resistance","improving earthquake and tsunami resistance at industrial complexes",""],[1,"54","2","Peninsula and Remote Island Disaster Resilience Measures","promote disaster management and national resilience measures for peninsulas and remote islands",""]],"113":[[1,"55","4","Defense Capabilities Reinforcement Initiative","the government will promote efforts to fundamentally reinforce defense capabilities, based on the National Security Strategy and other documents147.",""],[1,"56","1","Operational Defense Equipment Availability Improvement","the government will promote improving the number of operationally available equipment",""],[1,"56","1","Defense Ammunition and Fuel Security","securing ammunition and fuel",""],[1,"56","1","Defense Facility Resilience Improvement","improving resiliency of defense facilities",""],[1,"56","1","Defense Procurement Efficiency and Rationalization","the government will fully pursue further efficiency and rationalization in procurement",""],[1,"56","2","Self-Defense Forces Human Resource Development","the government will reinforce the human resource base of the Self-Defense Forces",""],[1,"56","2","Self-Defense Forces Medical Function Enhancement","enhance their medical functions",""],[1,"56","2","Expansion of State Ministers of Defense","the number of State Ministers of Defense will be increased from one to two",""],[1,"56","3","Defense Production and Technology Base Enhancement","By implementing the Act on Enhancing Defense Production and Technology Bases150, the government will promote the development of a strong and sustainable defense industry, effective responses to various risks, cooperation with the defense industry, and the transfer of defense equipment.",""],[1,"56","3","Next-Generation Defense Technology Research and Development","The government will promote research and development—including the joint development of next-generation fighter aircraft—and the utilization of advanced technologies from the private sector, including startups, which serve as key players in dual-use applications.",""],[1,"56","3","Innovative Technology Development and Diffusion Ecosystem","Through these efforts, the government will build an ecosystem that identifies and nurtures innovative technologies and delivers their benefits to society.",""],[1,"56","3","Japan-U.S. Alliance Deterrence and Response Enhancement","The government will strengthen the deterrence and response capabilities of the Japan-U.S. alliance",""],[1,"56","3","Defense Cooperation with Like-Minded Countries","while also enhancing cooperation with like-minded countries and others.",""],[1,"56","3","U.S. Forces Realignment and Base-Related Measures","The government will promote the realignment of U.S. Forces in Japan and base-related measures.",""],[1,"56","4","Defense Capability Financing Mechanism","The government will continue to secure these financial resources in line with the Defense Buildup Program, etc. including agile and flexible approaches.",""],[1,"56","4","Personal Income Tax Reform Measures","The government will continue to examine tax measures related to personal income tax, based on the Outline of the Tax Reform for Fiscal 2023151 and other relevant policies.",""],[1,"56","5","Defense Research and Development Programme","The government will further promote efforts in four key areas—research and development, public infrastructure development, and others—to strengthen our comprehensive defense posture",""],[1,"56","5","Defense-Supporting Public Infrastructure Development","The government will further promote efforts in four key areas—research and development, public infrastructure development, and others—to strengthen our comprehensive defense posture",""],[1,"56","5","Relevant Ministries and Agencies Capacity Enhancement","The government will also advance the strategic reinforcement of essential foundations that support the nation and people's lives, including energy and food.",""],[1,"56","5","Strategic Reinforcement of Energy and Food Foundations","The government will also advance the strategic reinforcement of essential foundations that support the nation and people's lives, including energy and food.",""],[1,"57","1","Wide-Area Evacuation and Reception Arrangements Study","The government will implement a study regarding wide-area evacuation and reception arrangements for residents, focusing on regions such as the southwestern islands.",""],[1,"57","1","Sakishima Islands Basic Reception Guideline","In particular, the government will develop a Basic Reception Guideline for the evacuation of residents from the Sakishima Islands by the end of FY 2026.",""],[1,"57","1","Underground Shelter Use and Civil Protection Policy","To secure shelters in the event of armed attacks, the government will work to promote the use of underground facilities and formulate an implementation policy by the end of FY 2025, thereby strengthening our civil protection framework.",""]],"114":[[1,"57","2","Maritime Domain Awareness Maritime Security Initiative","The government will promote comprehensive maritime security and other initiatives through Maritime Domain Awareness (MDA) based on the Basic Plan on Ocean Policy 152.",""],[1,"57","2","Japan Coast Guard Patrol Vessel Renewal","The government will also reinforce and renew Japan Coast Guard’s patrol vessels and the like",""],[1,"57","2","Maritime Security Operating Expense Financing","secure operating expenses",""],[1,"57","2","Unmanned Aircraft Maritime Security Technology Deployment","promote the use of new technologies such as unmanned aircraft",""],[1,"57","2","Interagency and International Coast Guard Cooperation","strengthen cooperation and collaboration with the police, the Self-Defense Forces and oversea coast guard agencies",""],[1,"57","2","Maritime Security Workforce Development and Workplace Improvement","advance effort to secure and develop human resources, improve work environment, and enhance personnel treatment based on the Policy on the Strengthening Maritime Security Capabilities153",""],[1,"57","3","Satellite Constellation Development","building a satellite constellation",""],[1,"57","3","Disinformation Response Capability Strengthening","We will reinforce our structure and capabilities to strengthen measures against disinformation",""],[1,"57","3","National Intelligence Collection and Analysis","efforts on collection and analysis of information, including human intelligence",""],[1,"57","3","Strategic Communication Capability Strengthening","strategic communication",""],[1,"57","4","National Cybersecurity Command Structure","the government will establish a new command structure to serve as the core of our national cybersecurity framework",""],[1,"57","4","Advanced Cybersecurity Information Infrastructure","building infrastructure for advanced collection, analysis, and sharing of information",""],[1,"57","4","Cross-Government Cybersecurity Monitoring","strengthening cross-government monitoring functions",""],[1,"57","4","JC-STAR Government Procurement Initiative","use of JC-STAR in government procurement by the end of FY 2025",""],[1,"57","4","Next-Generation Cybersecurity Technology R&D Programme","expanding R&D projects on next-generation cybersecurity technologies—including post-quantum cryptography",""],[1,"57","4","Cybersecurity Supply Chain Security Measures","enhancing supply chain security measures",""],[1,"57","5","IoT Device Security Certification System","A certification system that verifies the safety of IoT devices based on specific security standards, which was launched in March 2025.",""],[1,"58","1","Human Resources Development Initiative","fostering human resources",""],[1,"58","1","Domestic Technology-Based Cybersecurity Capability Enhancement","improving our cybersecurity capabilities by leveraging domestic technologies as the core.",""],[1,"58","1","Next Cybersecurity Strategy Formulation","We will formulate the next Cybersecurity Strategy, incorporating these initiatives, by the end of 2025.",""],[1,"58","2","Whole-of-Government Economic Security Framework","strengthen our whole-of-government framework with the National Security Secretariat serving as the command center.",""],[1,"58","2","Free and Open International Order Initiative","uphold and reinforce a free and open international order based on the rule of law",""],[1,"58","2","International Allies Cooperation Initiative","deepen cooperation with allies and like-minded countries",""]],"115":[[1,"60","4","Whole-of-Government Land and Asset Management Review","The government will conduct a comprehensive review of how land and assets are managed and utilized, including acquisition by foreign nationals, with a leadership under a whole-of-government coordination framework.",""],[1,"60","4","Land Ownership Registry and Database Transparency Upgrade","To enhance the transparency in land ownership across the country, including for foreign nationals, we will consider enhancement to owner information in land-related registries and upgrade to relevant databases.",""],[1,"60","5","Important Real Estate and Facilities Act Measures","we will continue to implement measures under the Act on the Review of Important Real Estate and Facilities161 and other relevant regulations",""],[1,"60","5","Domestic and International Situation Monitoring","we will closely monitor the domestic and international situation",""],[1,"60","5","Review of Important Real Estate and Facilities Act","consider further actions, including a possible review of the Act",""],[1,"60","6","Real Estate Use Regulation Act for Important Facilities and Remote Islands","Act on the Review and Regulation of the Use of Real Estate Surrounding Important Facilities and on Remote Territorial Islands (Act No. 84 of 2021)",""]],"116":[[1,"62","2","Transportation Sector Safety Measures","The government will work on safety measures in the transportation sector",""],[1,"62","2","Automobile Manufacturer Fraud Prevention","prevent fraud by automobile manufacturers",""],[1,"62","2","Elderly Driver Accident Prevention","prevent accidents involving elderly drivers",""],[1,"62","2","Automobile Accident Victim Support","support victims of automobile accidents",""],[1,"62","3","Local Consumer Administration Enhancement Grant Revision","we will revise the Local Consumer Administration Enhancement Grant to support initiatives such as revitalizing community monitoring activities and recruiting and training consumer affairs consultants.",""],[1,"62","3","Digital Food Loss and Donation Promotion Initiative","We will also promote Food Loss and Waste reduction and food donations by leveraging digital transformation (DX).",""],[1,"62","3","Whistleblower Protection Guidelines Update","In preparation for the enforcement of the amended Whistleblower Protection Act171 in FY 2026, we will update the relevant guidelines.",""],[1,"62","4","Workplace Harassment Prevention Measures","we will promote workplace harassment prevention measures, including the development of guidelines to address customer harassment by the summer of 2026.",""]],"117":[[1,"62","5","Post-COVID-19 and Vaccine Safety Studies","We will advance surveys and studies on post COVID-19 condition and adverse reactions to vaccines.",""],[1,"62","5","Next Infectious Disease Crisis Readiness","we will work closely with the Japan Institute for Health Security to ensure full readiness for the next infectious disease crisis.",""],[1,"62","5","Online Rabies Prevention Procedures","we will reach a conclusion within FY 2025 on the online processing of procedures related to the Rabies Prevention Act.",""],[1,"62","5","Pollen Allergy Source Control Measures","We will promote source control measures based on the Overall Picture of the Measures Against Pollen Allergy.",""],[1,"62","5","Heat Illness Prevention Measures","measures against heat illness, including the use of Special Heat Stroke Alert information",""],[1,"62","5","Bear Damage Countermeasures","Measures to Prevent Bear-Related Harm Based on the Amended Wildlife Protection and Management Act and the Policy Package for Bear Damage Countermeasures",""],[1,"62","5","Invasive Alien Species Management","and invasive alien species management.",""],[1,"62","5","PFAS Knowledge and Water Supplier Support Measures","Regarding PFAS measures, we will enhance scientific knowledge and provide support to water suppliers.",""]],"118":[[1,"63","2","Long-Term Care and Welfare Workforce Development Measures","To secure the necessary long-term care and welfare services across the country, we will promote the measures, for securing human resources including foreign nationals.",""],[1,"63","2","Support for Local Caregiver Initiatives","We will support local government initiatives for caregivers179, such as young and working caregivers, regardless of age or employment status",""],[1,"63","2","Collaborative Youth Support with Private Organizations","promote youth support in collaboration with private organizations, including NPOs.",""],[1,"63","2","Cross-Sectoral Multi-Generational Collaboration Platforms","We will also advance the development of platforms180 for diverse actors to collaborate across sectors and address local issues through multi-generational participation",""],[1,"63","2","Comprehensive Self-Reliance Support System","the establishment of a comprehensive support system centered on the self-reliance support for needy persons.",""],[1,"63","3","Educational and Daily Life Support for Children","educational and daily life support for children to prevent intergenerational poverty",""],[1,"63","3","Housing Assistance for Secure Living Environments","housing assistance to ensure secure living environments",""],[1,"63","3","Public Assistance System Administration and Public Understanding","promoting public understanding of the system and ensuring its proper administration",""],[1,"63","3","Employment and Education Support for Public Assistance Recipients","supporting employment and education to help recipients achieve self-reliance",""],[1,"63","3","Digitalized Medical Visit and Health Management Support","promoting appropriate medical visits and health management through digitalization",""],[1,"63","3","Low-Income Household Consumption Data and Livelihood Standards Review","we will work to improve and utilize consumption data of general low-income households and examine necessary measures based on trends in the socio-economic situation",""],[1,"63","5","Local Caregiver Support Initiatives","Local government initiatives to support caregivers who assist family members in need of care due to disabilities, illness, or other conditions.",""]],"119":[[1,"63","4","Compensation for Persons Subjected to Eugenic Surgery","We will provide compensation in accordance with the Act on the Payment of Compensation, etc. to Persons Who Underwent Eugenic Surgery, etc. Under the Now-defunct Eugenic Protection Law",""],[1,"63","4","Disability Inclusion Policies Based on the Social Model","advance policies based on the concept of the social model of disability in line with Action Plan Toward a Society of Coexistence Without Prejudice or Discrimination Against Persons with Disabilities",""],[1,"63","4","Disability Discrimination Elimination Measures","we will promote the elimination of discrimination",""],[1,"64","1","Community Development and Barrier-Free Mindset Initiatives","design community development184 and barrier-free mindset initiatives",""],[1,"64","1","Employment and Independent Living Support for Persons with Disabilities","support for employment and independent living for persons with disabilities",""],[1,"64","1","Accessibility Improvement Initiative","improvement of accessibility",""],[1,"64","2","Social Withdrawal Self-Reliance Support Programme","we will enhance support for socially withdrawn individuals (hikikomori) by promoting initiatives based on an assessment of the actual conditions and effectiveness of self-reliance support, including group living programs.",""],[1,"64","2","Comprehensive Rights Protection and Adult Guardianship","We will advance comprehensive rights protection, including adult guardianship",""],[1,"64","2","Family Register Access and Resolution Measures","work to promote the resolution of the problem involving persons without a family register.",""],[1,"64","2","Sexual Orientation and Gender Identity Public Understanding Measures","With regard to sexual orientation and gender identity, the government will promote measures based on the Act on Promoting Public Understanding186.",""],[1,"64","2","Animal Welfare and Management Measures","We will promote animal welfare and management.",""],[1,"64","5","Barrier-Free Transport and Facility Design","Barrier-free design in the transport, building, and facility sectors, such as the installation of platform doors at train stations.",""]],"120":[[1,"64","3","Local Public-Private Coordination Platforms","backing up local governments at the stage of establishing the local Public-Private Coordination Platforms",""],[1,"64","3","Ongoing Support for NPO Activities","supporting various activities of NPOs on an ongoing basis",""],[1,"64","3","Community Social Connections and Places","creating loose social connections and places",""],[1,"64","3","Tsunagari Supporters Development Initiative","fostering principal supports and those who are interested in those around them, and that they support troubled people where possible (so-called “Tsunagari Supporters”)",""],[1,"64","3","Cross-Sectoral Loneliness Prevention Coordination","promoting cross-sectoral coordination, to create social connections",""],[1,"64","3","Government and Local Government Social Connection Prevention Efforts","advancing efforts by the related governmental ministries and agencies as well as local government collaborating to prevent the loss of social connections that leads to isolated death",""],[1,"64","4","Social Sector Support and Donation Promotion","The government will strengthen support for private entities working to solve social issues, including the promotion of donations and support through intermediate support organizations that support NPO activities, and work to develop the social sector.",""],[1,"64","4","Online Procedures for Incorporated NPOs","the government will put into place a proper environment to promote online procedures",""],[1,"64","4","Counter-Terrorism Financing Measures for NPOs","measures against the financing of terrorism",""],[1,"64","4","Public Interest Corporation System Implementation","the government will develop the necessary systems for implementing the new system",""],[1,"64","4","Public Interest Information Platform","as well as an information platform",""],[1,"65","1","Civil Society Self-Reliance Support Initiatives","support initiatives driven by private-sector creativity to foster and empower civil society organizations to become self-reliant.",""],[1,"65","1","Pay for Success Contracting Expansion","The government will work to further expand the use of the Pay for Success (PFS) contracting system, including SIBs188",""],[1,"65","6","Social Impact Bonds","SIB is a system where a private business operator that is entrusted with a results-linked private contract type project procures funds for the project from financial institutions or other fund providers, and repays the funds according to the amount of payment from local public entities linked to the project.",""]],"121":[[1,"65","2","Employment and Working Conditions Support Programme","support for employment and better working conditions, such as enhanced reskilling and upskilling opportunities",""],[1,"65","2","Social Participation Connection Support","step-by-step support for social participation, such as providing places for connection",""],[1,"65","2","Old-Age Household Budget and Asset-Building Support","support with a view toward old age, such as assistance for household budget improvement and asset building",""],[1,"65","3","Employment Conditions and Policy Needs Survey","we will conduct surveys to better understand actual conditions and policy needs.",""],[1,"65","3","Employment Ice Age Generation Support Programme","we aim to compile a new program within FY 2025.",""],[1,"65","3","Enhanced Outreach for Employment Support","enhanced outreach to the individuals concerned, their families, and support providers.",""],[1,"66","3","Labor Measures and Vocational Life Amendment Act","The Act to Partially Amend the Act on Comprehensively Advancing LaborMeasures, and Stabilizing the Employment of Workers, and Enriching Workers' Vocational Lives, etc. (Act No. 63 of 2025).",""],[1,"66","3","Research on Barriers to Employment After Reskilling","We will consider conducting research on factors that hinder employment even after reskilling and upskilling, such as time constraints and limited work locations",""],[1,"66","3","Flexible Job Opportunity Creation Support","supporting the creation of flexible job opportunities.",""],[1,"67","2","Elderly Employment Matching Services Improvement","For the elderly, we will facilitate access to diverse employment and other opportunities through public-private collaboration by improving matching services that reflect their individual needs.",""]],"122":[[1,"73","2","Sustainable Long-Term Care Service Delivery Policy","we will formulate, by the end of 2025, a policy direction for securing a sustainable long-term care service delivery system.",""],[1,"73","2","Regional Community-Based Integrated Care Strategy","we will organize strategies to deepen community-based integrated care systems in each region, including flexible responses in mountainous areas, that reflect regional differences in service demand due to demographic shifts such as depopulation and ever-growing aging society.",""],[1,"73","2","Medical and Long-Term Care Coordination and Prevention","promoting coordination between medical and long-term care services and strengthening preventive care efforts, based on the Community Health Care Visions",""],[1,"73","2","Care Professional Collaboration and Quality Improvement","enhancing collaboration and consultation frameworks among diverse professionals, including improving care management quality",""],[1,"73","2","Long-Term Care Technology Demonstration and Adoption","improving productivity through demonstration, introduction, and hands-on support for the social implementation of long-term care technologies",""],[1,"73","2","Long-Term Care Provider Management and Scale-Up Support","supporting efforts to improve management through collaboration and scale-up among service providers",""],[1,"73","2","Public-Private Expansion of Care Services","expanding non-insurance-based services through public-private partnerships, including support for working caregivers",""],[1,"73","2","Long-Term Care Workforce Recruitment and Retention","securing and retaining care workers, including foreign nationals",""],[1,"73","2","Transparency and Quality Regulation for Fee-Based Care Homes","We will also ensure the transparency and quality of the operation and services of fee-based long-term homes.",""],[1,"73","3","Long-Term Care Insurance Benefits and Contributions Review","We will examine issues related to the revision of benefits and contributions under the long-term care insurance system, including a review of the criteria for determining user copayments, with the aim of reaching a conclusion by the end of 2025.",""],[1,"73","5","Long-Term Care Support Specialist Renewal Training Reform","Includes revising the renewal training for long-term care support specialists.",""],[1,"77","1","Evidence-Based Elderly Social Participation Initiative","To promote social participation among the elderly and reduce the rate of long-term care certification, we will expand evidence-based initiatives using data.",""],[1,"77","1","Local Stakeholder Long-Term Care Prevention Coordination","These will include coordinated efforts by diverse local stakeholders",""],[1,"77","1","Outcome-Oriented Long-Term Care Prevention and Rehabilitation","outcome-oriented approaches for effective long-term care prevention and rehabilitation",""]],"123":[[1,"77","2","Whole-of-Government Pharmaceutical Control Tower","We will enhance our whole-of-government control tower function",""],[1,"77","2","Pharmaceutical Industry Structural Reform","advancing structural reforms in the pharmaceutical industry",""],[1,"77","2","Integrated Drug Discovery and Healthcare Innovation Policy","we will implement integrated policies to strengthen the drug discovery ecosystem, expand the healthcare market, and reinforce the foundation for pharmaceutical innovation",""],[1,"77","2","International Clinical Trials and First-in-Human Facilities","We will develop a system to conduct international-level clinical trials, including new facilities capable of First-in-Human (FIH) studies.",""],[1,"77","2","Healthcare Startup Support Frameworks","We will reinforce the frameworks of MEDISO225 and CARISO226 to provide robust support for healthcare startups.",""],[1,"77","2","Innovative Pharmaceuticals Commercialization Fund Expansion","we will consider expanding the scope of the Fund to Support the Practical Application of Innovative Pharmaceuticals and Related Products, thereby supporting the commercialization of promising drug discoveries.",""],[1,"77","2","Innovation-Oriented Pharmaceutical Drug Pricing","The government will implement appropriate drug pricing that balances reducing the public burden with encouraging pharmaceutical innovation 227",""],[1,"77","2","Pharmaceutical Approval Review and Consultation System Strengthening","strengthen the approval review and consultation systems",""],[1,"77","2","Pharmaceutical Manufacturing Infrastructure Development","advance the development of manufacturing infrastructure for pharmaceuticals, including biopharmaceuticals",""],[1,"77","2","Pharmaceutical Workforce Training and Retention","promote the training and retention of related human resources",""],[1,"77","2","Global-Standard Pharmaceutical Research and Development Environment","Through these efforts, we will establish a research and development environment that meets global standards",""],[1,"77","2","Drug Lag and Drug Loss Reduction Measures","while also addressing drug lag and drug loss",""],[1,"77","2","Program-Based Medical Device Approval Facilitation","facilitating the approval of program-based medical devices",""],[1,"77","3","Medical Venture Total Support Office","Medical venture total support office called MEDical Innovation Support Office.",""],[1,"77","3","Nursing Care Innovation Consultation Office","Similar to MEDISO in the nursing care field, the CARe Innovation Support Office (CARISO) serves as a consultation desk.",""],[1,"77","3","Patent-Period Innovative Drug Pricing Review","we will also consider how to handle such drugs during their patent period from the perspective of promoting pharmaceutical innovation.",""],[1,"78","1","Overseas Pharmaceutical Regulatory Harmonization Mechanism","utilize overseas offices of the Pharmaceuticals and Medical Devices Agency (PMDA) to advance pharmaceutical regulatory consultation and harmonization.",""],[1,"78","1","Medical Industry Promotion and Late-Stage R&D Support","The government will strengthen support for industrial promotion hub functions and research and development aimed at late-stage development and international expansion.",""],[1,"78","1","Joint Medical Device Demonstration Platforms","we will establish demonstration platforms jointly operated by universities, national centers, and medical institutions.",""],[1,"78","1","Japan-Originated Medical Device Development","Through these efforts, we will promote the creation of Japan-originated medical devices, including therapeutic devices and software devices (Software as a Medical Device: SaMD).",""],[1,"78","2","Whole Genome Analysis Infrastructure and Implementation","We will promote whole genome analysis.",""],[1,"78","2","Advanced Biomedical Research and Drug Discovery","We will promote drug discovery utilizing iPS cells and research and development in regenerative medicine, cell and gene therapy.",""],[1,"78","2","Market Incentives for New Antibiotic Development","We will also ensure the availability of antimicrobials effective against antimicrobial-resistant bacteria by introducing market incentives for the development of new antibiotics.",""],[1,"78","2","Cost-Effectiveness Evaluation System Enhancement","From the perspectives of promoting innovation and considering the insurance premium burden on the working generation, we will seek to further utilize the Cost-effectiveness Evaluation System based on objective reviews.",""],[1,"78","2","Research on Effective Standard Drug Therapies","To establish standard drug therapies, we will conduct research on effective",""],[1,"79","4","Radioisotope Production and Utilization Action Plan for Medical Use","Action Plan for Promotion of Production and Utilization of Radioisotopes for Medical Use",""]],"124":[[1,"78","2","Essential Medicines Supply Chain and Distribution System","To ensure a stable supply of medicines, we will work to reinforce supply chains for antibiotics and other essential drugs, and develop a sustainable distribution system that reflects changing circumstances.",""],[1,"78","2","Infectious Disease Outbreak Pharmaceutical Supply Measures","At the same time, we will take measures against risks such as surges in demand during infectious disease outbreaks and address the current supply uncertainty surrounding essential pharmaceuticals228.",""],[1,"78","2","Generic Drug Industry Reorganization","We will also promote reorganization within the generic drug industry to resolve the issue of producing small quantities of a wide variety of items.",""],[1,"78","2","Domestic Biosimilar Production and Workforce Development","Regarding biosimilars, we will steadily establish domestic production systems and develop and secure skilled personnel, thereby encouraging their use.",""],[1,"78","2","Over-the-Counter Pharmaceutical and Test Kit Access","We will further promote the switch to over-the-counter (OTC) status for pharmaceuticals and test kits such as medicines regularly taken by patients with stable conditions based on an initial diagnosis or prescription by a physician, and test agents for minimally invasive samples such as puncture blood.",""],[1,"78","2","Self-Care and Self-Medication Roadmap","For these and related initiatives, we will develop a concrete roadmap to promote self-care and self-medication, while reviewing out-of-pocket costs for medications.",""],[1,"78","2","Medical Countermeasure Development Strategies","In addition, we will formulate development strategies for medical countermeasures for responding to infectious disease crises—such as vaccines, diagnostics, and therapeutics—and promote their research and development.",""],[1,"79","1","Clinical Treatment Guideline Integration","incorporate the findings into clinical practice guidelines",""],[1,"79","1","Pharmaceutical Use and Generic Drug Promotion","promoting the proper use of pharmaceuticals and encouraging the use of generic drugs",""],[1,"79","1","Regional Formulary Adoption","we will promote the adoption of regional formularies as part of efforts to optimize healthcare spending",""],[1,"79","1","School-Based Blood Donation Awareness","We will work to deepen understanding of blood donation from the elementary and junior high school level.",""],[1,"79","1","Domestic Blood Product Supply and Proper Use","we will promote domestic self-sufficiency, stable supply, and proper use of blood products for transfusion and fractionated plasma products such as immunoglobulin and fibrinogen preparations",""],[1,"79","1","Domestic Medical Radioisotope Production System","we will take steps to establish necessary systems for the domestic production and expanded use of medical radioisotopes",""]],"125":[[1,"82","2","Support for Children Facing Bullying and Distress","We will strongly promote support for children and parents facing bullying, chronic absenteeism, or emotional distress",""],[1,"82","2","Child and Youth Suicide Prevention Measures","as well as measures to prevent suicide among children and youth",""],[1,"82","2","Child Mental Health Support","improve mental health support for children.",""],[1,"82","2","Child Death Review Mechanism","We will promote Child Death Reviews (CDR) with the aim of preventing child deaths.",""],[1,"84","1","School Counseling Access Environments","developing environments in which people can consult with SCs and SSWs",""],[1,"84","1","Chronic Absenteeism, Bullying, and Suicide Prevention","advancing measures to prevent chronic absenteeism, serious bullying, and suicide by strengthening cooperation with the medical and welfare sectors",""],[1,"84","1","School Safety Promotion","promoting school safety that incorporates the concept of safety promotion schools",""],[1,"84","1","Student Physical Strength and Vision Measures","measures will be strengthened to improve physical strength and prevent the decline in vision",""],[1,"84","1","Dental Health and Food Education","to promote dental health education and food education, including the use of local products in school lunches",""]],"126":[[1,"83","3","Community School and School-Community Collaboration Initiative","accelerate integrated initiatives for community schools and collaborative activities between schools and communities",""],[1,"83","3","Nationwide Community Club Activity Transformation","the nationwide implementation of transformation to community club activities",""],[1,"84","3","School Commuting Safety Improvement Programme","This includes safety measures for commuting to school, such as the promotion of school guard leaders and the use of school buses.",""],[1,"84","3","Integrated School Disaster Preparedness and Facility Renewal","This includes integrated implementation of disaster preparedness enhancements and deterioration countermeasures for school facilities.",""]],"127":[[1,"84","2","University Collaboration and Reorganization Reform","the government will advance the optimization of scale through collaboration, reorganization, and integration of national, public, and private universities, including the downsizing or withdrawal of some institutions",""],[1,"84","2","Higher Education Financial Support System","we will steadily implement the expanded new financial support system for higher education",""],[1,"84","2","Tuition Fee Deferred Payment System","we will steadily implement the deferred payment system for tuition fees",""],[1,"85","1","Public-Private Support Mechanism for International Student Mobility","we will work on the strategic utilization of public-private support measures.",""],[1,"85","5","International Student Diversity Policy","attention will be paid to ensuring diversity in the countries and regions of origin of international students.",""],[1,"85","5","Campus Co-Creation Hubs Development","further development of co-creation hubs on campuses through the use of diverse funding sources such as donations.",""]],"129":[[1,"86","2","Geospatial and Three-Dimensional Urban Development Digital Transformation","By attaching geospatial information to real estate IDs and advancing the integration of three-dimensional models, such as BIM258 and PLATEAU, we will promote digital transformation (DX) in architecture and urban development, thereby advancing disaster preparedness, upgrading community planning, and facilitating the creation of new businesses.",""],[1,"86","3","i-Construction 2.0 Automation Programme","We will continue to promote i-Construction 2.0 to advance automation and labor saving at construction sites",""],[1,"86","3","Inclusive Construction Workforce Development Initiative","promoting the active participation of diverse human resources, including women and foreign nationals, and working to secure and develop the workforce in the construction industry",""],[1,"86","3","Cross-Sectoral Infrastructure Data Development and Disclosure","We will accelerate infrastructure DX by promoting the cross-sectoral development and disclosure of infrastructure data",""],[1,"86","5","Building Information Modeling Implementation","This modeling is designed to improve the efficiency of the entire construction production and management system by sharing data among related parties.",""],[1,"86","5","Land, Infrastructure, Transport and Tourism Data Platform","This includes the Land, Infrastructure, Transport and Tourism Data Platform",""],[1,"86","5","Project LINKS Data Utilization and Business Creation","Project LINKS, which will engage in EBPM and business creation through data preparation and utilization.",""]],"130":[[1,"88","2","Vertical Intergovernmental Support for Municipalities","we will promote efforts such as vertical support from the national and prefectural governments to municipalities",""],[1,"88","2","Horizontal Municipal Cooperation Mechanism","horizontal cooperation among municipalities",""],[1,"88","2","Multi-Stakeholder Local Government Collaboration","collaboration with a variety of stakeholders",""],[1,"88","2","Digital Technology Use in Local Government Operations","the use of digital technologies",""],[1,"88","2","Review of Intergovernmental Government Roles","we will also facilitate discussions to resolve these challenges, including a review of the respective roles of the national, prefectural, and municipal governments",""],[1,"88","2","Joint Regional Human Resources Development Initiative","we will promote initiatives in which local governments work together to secure and develop the human resources needed in their regions",""],[1,"88","2","Joint Use and Consolidation of Public Facilities","efforts to consolidate, integrate, and jointly use public facilities across multiple jurisdictions",""],[1,"88","3","Local Tax System Equalization Reform","We will analyze the causes and issues behind the widening gaps in tax revenue distribution and fiscal capacity among local governments, and work toward the development of a local tax system characterized by a more even distribution of tax sources and stable revenue.",""],[1,"88","4","Local Government Cost Pass-Through Policy","the appropriate transfer of cost increases to prices in public works, facility management, and services provided by local governments",""],[1,"88","4","Regional Healthcare Delivery Security Measures","take measures to secure regional healthcare delivery systems",""],[1,"88","4","Local Government Revenue Strengthening Mechanism","ensure the total amount of local governments’ general revenue sources264",""],[1,"88","5","Regional Productivity Improvement Initiative","we will promote productivity improvements in each region.",""],[1,"88","5","Local Administrative Simplification and Streamlining Reform","we will encourage the simplification and streamlining of administrative operations at the local level through measures such as improving the efficiency of planning processes, eliminating intermediary administrative procedures, reviewing intermediary surveys",""],[1,"88","6","Local Government Fiscal Stability Financing Mechanism","the government will ensure that the total amount of general revenue sources necessary for stable fiscal management of local governments, including those receiving local allocation tax grants, shall be maintained substantially at the same level as that of the FY 2024 Fiscal Plan of Local Governments, and not below.",""]],"131":[[1,"89","2","Online Public Application and One-Stop Counter Reform","we will work on front-yard reforms, such as online application and the \"one-stop counter without writing,\"",""],[1,"89","2","Local Government Core Systems Standardization Reform","backyard reforms, such as the unification and standardization of core service systems",""],[1,"89","2","eL-QR Public Money Payment System","utilization of eL-QR for payment of public money other than local taxes",""],[1,"89","2","Joint Local Government Systems Procurement and Use","We will support efforts to jointly procure and use systems and tools across local governments.",""],[1,"89","2","Local Government Digital Transformation Promotion System","we will drive efforts for prefectural governments and municipalities to establish a system for promoting the DX, in which they ensure the human resources pool function to support the municipalities.",""],[1,"89","2","Local Government Cybersecurity Policy and Infrastructure Strengthening","we will strengthen efforts to further enhance security by promoting the formulation of policies to ensure cybersecurity in local governments and reinforcing their security infrastructure.",""],[1,"89","2","Govbot Administrative Service Chatbot Improvement","we will continue to improve “Govbot”, an administrative service information chatbot, from the user perspective.",""]],"132":[[1,"91","2","Well-Being KPI Integration in Key Plans and Strategies","we will encourage the incorporation of effective KPIs that help improve well-being in key plans and strategies related to employment, education, health, child-rearing, and community life.",""],[1,"91","2","Population Well-Being Monitoring System","we will continue and strengthen efforts to monitor well-being across the population.",""],[1,"91","2","Public Systems Review and Revision for Rising Prices","Review and Revision of public systems in line with rising prices",""],[1,"91","3","Wage Growth and Labor Value Recognition Policy","the government will take the lead in ensuring that wage increases outpace inflation by comprehensively implementing the following three measures",""],[1,"91","4","Public Systems Benchmark Review and Revision","we will conduct a comprehensive, cross-ministerial review and revision of the long-standing fixed benchmark amounts and thresholds in public systems related to the budgets and tax systems",""],[1,"91","4","Regular Inflation-Based Benchmark Update Mechanism","we will develop mechanisms that allow timely responses to current inflation by establishing rules that require regular updates of benchmark amounts and thresholds in line with the characteristics of each public system",""],[1,"91","5","Government-Set Price Adjustment for Social Services","raising government-set prices (such as those for medical care, long-term care, childcare, and social welfare);",""],[1,"91","5","Full Government Procurement Price Pass-Through","ensuring full price pass-through in government procurement to secure sufficient funding for wage increases for workers.",""],[1,"91","6","Review of Public Programme Benchmarks and Tax Exemption Thresholds","These benchmarks will be reviewed without delay.",""],[1,"92","4","Agile Inflation Response Policy Measures","We will continue to implement agile policy measures in response to economic conditions and inflation trends.",""]],"134":[[1,"93","1","Declining Birthrate and Child Policy Measures","steadily implementing measures to address the declining birthrate and child-related policies",""]],"135":[[1,"93","1","Disaster Management and National Resilience Enhancement","enhancing disaster management, mitigation, and national resilience",""],[1,"93","1","Defense Capability Strengthening","fundamentally strengthening our defense capabilities",""],[1,"93","1","External Shock-Resilient Economic Structure","building an economic structure resilient to external shocks",""]]}});